window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4601,"title":"Chapter 4601: Powerful Enemy","paragraphs":["Chapter 4601: Powerful Enemy","What the several Elders were thinking was exactly what the Patriarch was thinking at the moment. They didn’t have the heart to protect the three children from the beginning, and even wanted to play with the three children and the Super Sacred Beast, but it was only after Hao’er promised them that as long as they were safe, they would be given the benefit of a medicinal pill when they returned that they changed their attitude.","Now, when the threat had expanded to the point that it was directly related to their lives, they naturally compared the benefits to the immediate danger, and after some thought, they had an idea in mind.","‘Let’s go and take a look first! If we can dissuade him, we will try our best to dissuade him back, if it really comes to the point where there is no other way, then ...’ The Patriarch’s voice lurched and fell silent, not saying any more.","‘Alright, we’ll listen to the Patriarch.’ The three elders said, agreeing to his method.","‘Let’s go then!’ The Patriarch said, walking quickly outside.","There at the mountain gate, the third elder was smiling with a compensatory smile, saying, ‘Old Mountain Demon has not taken a step out of the Black Mountain Gate for many years, but I never thought that he would visit our clan today, it is truly a blessing for our clan.’","‘Hehe, Yuan San, it seems that your strength hasn’t grown much over the years.’ The person who spoke had grey hair draped over his head, while his face looked like that of a young man in his twenties.","He was wearing a black cloak, which wrapped his entire body, only his head above the neck was exposed, and his hands were hidden within the cloak, not showing half of it.","His face was not outstanding, it could even be said that it was so unusual that people would forget it after a glance, but his eyes were filled with hostility and bloodthirsty killing, sinister and venomous.","When that gaze fell on a person, it would make them involuntarily shiver, as if they were being stared at by a poisonous snake, striking fear in their hearts, and even, unable to resist the urge to pull out their legs and run.","At this moment, the third elder was just like that, only, he forced himself to hold back and calm down, hoping in his heart that the Patriarch would come soon, while also circling around with it.","‘I have limited talent, so I cannot compare myself to Old Mountain Demon, only, I wonder if Old Mountain Demon came this time to get together with our Patriarch? Or is there something else going on?’","‘Why bother beating around the bush? This ancestor has already arrived here, could it be that you still can’t guess my ancestor’s intentions?’ He snorted and looked at the Third Taoist Priest, ‘Don’t drag your feet, what this honourable father is going to do today, even if you pour out your clan, you won’t be able to stop it, if you’re sensible, you’d better hurry up and hand over the person and that Super Sacred Beast that this honourable father wants!’ As he spoke, the pressure from his body spread out and attacked towards that front mountain gate.","The disciple guarding the mountain gate clutched his head and cried out in pain, involuntarily squatting down and screaming miserably.","And the Third Elder’s face changed as he immediately droned, ‘Mountain Demon! You’re a Heavenly Deity powerhouse, how can you have the nerve to strike out at my sect’s disciples? Aren’t you afraid of getting a bad reputation as a bully?’","‘Hahahahahaha!’","Rampant laughter rang out, only to see him laughing up to the sky, his laughter was accompanied by a mighty pressure that filled the air, that powerful air current pressure was like ripples that swept through the air, especially like a demonic sound that travelled into the ears of the sect’s disciples, causing them to crouch with their heads held in their hands, crying out in pain and screaming miserably.","The third elder was furious, but there was nothing he could do about it, because even he himself, under that powerful airflow fluctuation, the blood qi in his body also tumbled and surged up, if it was not forcibly suppressed, I was afraid that a mouthful of blood would have been sprayed out.Chapter 4591 – Powerful Enemy","What the several Elders were thinking was exactly what the Patriarch was thinking at the moment. They didn’t have the heart to protect the three children from the beginning, and even wanted to play with the three children and the Super Sacred Beast, but it was only after Hao’er promised them that as long as they were safe, they would be given the benefit of a medicinal pill when they returned that they changed their attitude.","Now, when the threat had expanded to the point that it was directly related to their lives, they naturally compared the benefits to the immediate danger, and after some thought, they had an idea in mind.","‘Let’s go and take a look first! If we can dissuade him, we will try our best to dissuade him back, if it really comes to the point where there is no other way, then ...’ The Patriarch’s voice lurched and fell silent, not saying any more.","‘Alright, we’ll listen to the Patriarch.’ The three elders said, agreeing to his method.","‘Let’s go then!’ The Patriarch said, walking quickly outside.","There at the mountain gate, the third elder was smiling with a compensatory smile, saying, ‘Old Mountain Demon has not taken a step out of the Black Mountain Gate for many years, but I never thought that he would visit our clan today, it is truly a blessing for our clan.’","‘Hehe, Yuan San, it seems that your strength hasn’t grown much over the years.’ The person who spoke had grey hair draped over his head, while his face looked like that of a young man in his twenties.","He was wearing a black cloak, which wrapped his entire body, only his head above the neck was exposed, and his hands were hidden within the cloak, not showing half of it.","His face was not outstanding, it could even be said that it was so unusual that people would forget it after a glance, but his eyes were filled with hostility and bloodthirsty killing, sinister and venomous.","When that gaze fell on a person, it would make them involuntarily shiver, as if they were being stared at by a poisonous snake, striking fear in their hearts, and even, unable to resist the urge to pull out their legs and run.","At this moment, the third elder was just like that, only, he forced himself to hold back and calm down, hoping in his heart that the Patriarch would come soon, while also circling around with it.","‘I have limited talent, so I cannot compare myself to Old Mountain Demon, only, I wonder if Old Mountain Demon came this time to get together with our Patriarch? Or is there something else going on?’","‘Why bother beating around the bush? This ancestor has already arrived here, could it be that you still can’t guess my ancestor’s intentions?’ He snorted and looked at the Third Taoist Priest, ‘Don’t drag your feet, what this honourable father is going to do today, even if you pour out your clan, you won’t be able to stop it, if you’re sensible, you’d better hurry up and hand over the person and that Super Sacred Beast that this honourable father wants!’ As he spoke, the pressure from his body spread out and attacked towards that front mountain gate.","The disciple guarding the mountain gate clutched his head and cried out in pain, involuntarily squatting down and screaming miserably.","And the Third Elder’s face changed as he immediately droned, ‘Mountain Demon! You’re a Heavenly Deity powerhouse, how can you have the nerve to strike out at my sect’s disciples? Aren’t you afraid of getting a bad reputation as a bully?’","‘Hahahahahaha!’","Rampant laughter rang out, only to see him laughing up to the sky, his laughter was accompanied by a mighty pressure that filled the air, that powerful air current pressure was like ripples that swept through the air, especially like a demonic sound that travelled into the ears of the sect’s disciples, causing them to crouch with their heads held in their hands, crying out in pain and screaming miserably.","The third elder was furious, but there was nothing he could do about it, because even he himself, under that powerful airflow fluctuation, the blood qi in his body also tumbled and surged up, if it was not forcibly suppressed, I was afraid that a mouthful of blood would have been sprayed out."]},{"number":4602,"title":"Chapter 4602: Kill for Me","paragraphs":["Chapter 4602: Kill for Me","“Have mercy!”","The Patriarch’s voice, tinged with urgency, echoed. As he spoke, a surge of energy emanated from within the sect, countering the Old Mountain Demon’s pressure and forming a protective shield for the disciples.","Upon seeing the Patriarch and the Elders arrive, the diciples finally felt relieved and their faces shone with excitement.","They believed their Patriarch could confront the Old Mountain Demon. Even if he couldn’t win, their combined strength would deter him. The Old Mountain Demon will not get away so easily!","Seeing the arrival of more people, the Old Mountain Demon snorted, withdrawing his pressure. His voice, filled with dominance, rang out. “I have no patience for talk. Bring me the children and the beast, or I’ll begin a massacre!”","“Our sect has always been peaceful with yours. Why are you here, bullying our disciples? Do you think we don’t have anyone in our sect?” The Patriarch, humiliated in front of his people, struggled to maintain composure.","“I only want the children and the beast! Refuse, and you’ll face the consequences!” Old Mountain Demon growled.","“You know their origins. Do you dare to harm them? Aren’t you afraid of Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu’s wrath?” The Patriarch invoked Feng Jiu’s name as a threat.","“Hahahahahaha! Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu? Where is she? I’d like to meet her and see if she’s as powerful as they say. But where is she? Tell her to come out!” Old Mountain Demon sneered. “If you can’t summon her, hand over the children!”","“You!”","The Patriarch glared, his fists clenched. He dared not attack, but he also refused to yield. To surrender in front of his disciples and outsiders would be a devastating humiliation.","“It seems that if I don’t show you some of my prowess, you’ll never bring anyone out,” TheOld Mountain Demon said as a bloodthirsty smile emerged as he uttered two words coldly: “Kill them!”","“Kill!”","“Kill!”","“Kill, kill, kill!”","The cries echoed, sending shivers through the crowd. Almost instantly, the Black Mountain Sect members surged forward, attacking the sect’s disciples.","The clash erupted, swords clashing, shouts and screams filling the air. The smell of blood began to permeate the air as blood flowed like a river.","Seeing the melee, the Patriarch led his people into the fray, determined to protect his disciples.","Old Mountain Demon watched, then hummed, his black cloak billowing as energy surged from him. He revealed his hands, previously hidden beneath the cloak..."]},{"number":4603,"title":"Chapter 4603: Broken Promise","paragraphs":["Chapter 4603: Broken Promise","His hands were pale and aged, a stark contrast to his youthful face. Veins pulsed beneath the thin, wrinkled skin, speckled with dark age spots. As he moved his hands, visible air currents formed, whistling through the air. With each deliberate movement, these currents intensified, then erupted forward, aimed with blinding speed towards the Sect Master.","“Whoosh!”","“Hooooooo!”","The air currents, accompanied by a sharp sound, tore through the air, striking the disciples on both sides of the battle and then the Sect Master.","“Arghhhhh!”","The disciples were thrown back, screaming in agony. The Sect Master, unable to block the attack, coughed up blood and was hurled several metres back, landing heavily with a loud thud.","“Ughhh!”","After letting out a muffled groan, blood was surging chaotically in his chest and he could not help but spat out a mouthful of blood as blood continued gurgling out of his mount and spilling down his chin.","“Sect Master!”","“Sect Master!”","Alarmed cries echoed thoughout. The fighting abruptly ceased as both sides witnessed the Sect Master’s injury. The Black Mountain Sect members retreated behind their leader.","He paid no heed to the Black Mountain disciples who had fallen. Their lives, in his eyes, were as insignificant as ants.","The Old Mountain Demon slowly advanced. With each step, the sect members retreated, until they were pressed against the wall. They watched, pale-faced, as he approached, their hearts in disarray.","The elders watched him, towering over the fallen Sect Master. Yet, no one dared to help. They held their breath, watching tensely.","“Do you want to die? Or do you want to hand over those people?” A sinister voice, laced with murderous intent, addressed the Sect Master. A chilling laugh escaped him.","The Sect Master’s heart pounded. He couldn’t bring himself to betray the children, not in front of his people.","He desperately wanted to save himself and the sect, but he couldn’t utter their names.","Anxiety and fear warred within him. Finally, he glanced at the Grand Elder, then, as if overwhelmed by his injuries, he fainted, spitting out another mouthful of blood.","“Sect Master!”","The Grand Elder, aware of the Sect Master’s plan, quickly stepped forward. Seeing the unconscious Sect Master, he spoke. “Old Mountain Demon, you want the children and the beast. Why make things difficult for our sect? We’ve done our best to protect them. If you promise to leave and never return, we’ll hand them over!”"]},{"number":4604,"title":"Chapter 4604: Escape","paragraphs":["Chapter 4604: Escape","As soon as the Grand Elder spoke, the two venerable masters, who knew about the promise to protect the children, exchanged glances, their eyes flickering.","After learning the children’s identities, they reported to the Sect Master and followed him to the courtyard. Though guarding the outer courtyard, they had overheard the conversation.","They thought that after knowing their esteemed identities, the Sect Master and elders would anticipate the danger and resist, but they hadn’t expected...","Their gazes shifted to the Sect Master’s twitching eyelashes, and they sighed inwardly. They hadn’t expected the Sect Master to yield so easily to Old Mountain Demon.","Hearing this, the Old Mountain Demon narrowed his sinister eyes, a sneer appeared oh his face as he scanned them contemptuously. His voice slowed. “Fine. I don’t want to be your enemy either. As long as you hand them over, I won’t attack your sect.”","The Grand Elder gritted his teeth. “Fine! Old Mountain Demon, wait here. I’ll bring them out.” He turned to two venerable masters. “Come with me.”","The venerable masters paused, nodded, and followed him.","As they watched them go, the others carried the Sect Master aside.","Old Mountain Demon glanced at the feigning unconscious Sect Master, a mocking smile curling his lips. He waited leisurely.","In a world where strength reigned supreme, even decent sects yielded to formidable enemies.","Hao’er and the others were unaware of the commotion outside, but Seventeen, who had been gathering news, knew. He rushed back to the courtyard when he learned they were to be handed over.","“Master, it’s bad! The sect is going to hand us over to Old Mountain Demon. They’re coming! What do we do?” Despite being an adult, he asked Hao’er for guidance.","Hao’er, who was in the midst of guiding Muchen and Muyue, asked, “The Sect Master and Elders agreed?” He knew they must have, or they wouldn’t agree to hand them over.","“The Sect Master was injured and fainted, but I think he’s faking it. He’s no match for Old Mountain Demon, and neither are the Elders. They negotiated and agreed that if we’re handed over, he’ll leave. The Elders are coming with the Grand Elder,” Seventeen said anxiously.","Even the Sect Master and Elders couldn’t defeat the Old Mountain Demon. Only Silver Wolf stood a chance. But they were outnumbered, and Silver Wolf couldn’t protect everyone.","“Let’s go! We’ll take the back mountain path!”","Hao’er said decisively, turning to Muchen and Muyue. “Muchen, Yue’er, get on Silver Wolf’s back! He’ll be faster!”"]},{"number":4605,"title":"Chapter 4605: Cut Off","paragraphs":["Chapter 4605: Cut Off","“Yeah!!”","The twins responded quickly as Silver Wolf lay down, allowing them to climb onto his back. Once they were settled, he said, “Stay low, hold onto my fur, and don’t fall off.”","“Mm hmm!” The twins, their small hands gripping his thick fur, leaned forward, their faces pressed against his warm coat. Almost immediately, he leapt up and ran towards the dense, shadowed back mountain.","“Go!” Hao’er grabbed Seventeen, mounted his sword, and headed for the back mountain.","Usually, few people were in their area, and now most disciples were at the front gate, aiding their escape.","However, the Elder and others arrived quickly. Seeing the empty courtyard, their faces changed. “Oh no! They must have found out and escaped! Quickly, we’ve got to chase them!” If they didn’t present them to the Old Mountain Demon, their sect would suffer!","The venerable masters hesitated. “Elder, they’re Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu’s children. If something happens, and she finds out, she’ll come after us.”","Seeing them stop, the Grand Elder reprimanded them. “Don’t you think I know that? But if we don’t hand them over, our sect is finished! Can anyone withstand the Mountain Demon? No! Even the Sect Master is injured. Do we want to sacrifice everyone for those children?”","The venerable masters were silent, heads tucked low.","“What are you waiting for? Go after them!” He swept his sleeve and dashed off, not after Hao’er, but to activate the formation and trap them. Otherwise, they couldn’t explain to the Old Mountain Demon.","Hao’er and the others, heading for the mountains, encountered disciples, but Silver Wolf’s pressure forced them away. They followed the winding path downwards, the sounds of pursuit growing louder, echoing through the trees.","“Stop running! You cannot escape! Return with us!”","Hao’er and Seventeen didn’t turn, just sped up. Silver Wolf did the same, but as they reached the foot of the mountain, he abruptly stopped, his keen eyes detecting the line of guards stationed there.","Suddenly, Seventeen cried out. Silver Wolf and the twins looked back, seeing a hemispherical barrier isolating the mountain. Hao’er, on his sword, crashed into it, sending him and Seventeen tumbling to the ground.","“Big Brother!”","“Big Brother!”","The twins cried out, pulling on Silver Wolf’s fur. “Hurry! We have to go back! Big Brother can’t get out!”","Silver Wolf, seeing the scene, grew colder. He glared at the guards before running to the barrier, extending his paw."]},{"number":4606,"title":"Chapter 4606: Anxious","paragraphs":["Just as he pressed his paws against the enchantment, he was pushed away. He glanced inside and saw the sect members approaching. He stepped back and told the twins, \"Get down and stand aside. I'll try to break it.\"","\"Alright!\" The twins quickly dismounted and stood together.","Meanwhile, the cultivators at the foot of the mountain were excitedly discussing: \"Look! Are those the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu's children? They look just like her! And that silver wolf, wow! It's really magnificent!\"","\"They're in trouble. Old Mountain Demon is at the main gate, waiting to capture them. The sect agreed to hand them over. They even activated the formation. Once it's up, no one can get in or out. Even if that silver wolf is a Super Sacred Beast, it can't break through.\"","Some cultivators even shouted, \"Don't bother trying. Only someone from the sect can open it.\"","Silver Wolf ignored them. He backed up and charged again, but couldn't breach the barrier. He was bounced back, flipping in midair before landing. Fortunately, the twins weren't on his back.","The venerable masters and disciples arrived. Seeing Hao'er and Seventeen trapped inside, and Silver Wolf and the twins outside, they felt relieved. They wouldn't dare face Silver Wolf directly, but the formation isolated him.","\"Come back with us! You can't escape,\" one venerable master hollered.","\"Your sect is full of oath-breakers. Go back with you? No way. Hmph.\" Hao'er spat out coldly, word for word while glaring at them.","Being berated by a child, the venerable masters took a deep breath as they felt ashamed. \"Our sect did its best to protect you. We can't sacrifice everyone for you. Please understand.\"","\"If you couldn't do it, you shouldn't have agreed. And you shouldn't have betrayed us either.\" Hao'er said, his gaze contemptuous. \"You're all old monsters, scheming against children, and you want us to understand? Dream on!\"","With a cold harrumph, he drew his sword and attacked.","With the barrier up, fighting was the only option.","However, even at his peak, Hao'er couldn't defeat the venerable masters without Silver Wolf. Muchen and Muyue, outside the barrier, grew anxious.","\"Oh no! What do we do? Big Brother can't beat them! What should we do?\" Yue'er stamped her foot. \"If you hurt my Big Brother, my Mother will never let you go!\"","The venerable masters, about to attack, heard this and hesitated, retracting their attacks."]},{"number":4607,"title":"Chapter 4607: Threat","paragraphs":["The two hesitated, afraid to fight back for fear of injuring the young boy. Nevertheless, Hao'er's attacks grew increasingly precise, making it difficult for them to evade his strikes.","At this time, the dozen disciples behind them quietly surrounded Seventeen. Against this low-level cultivator who had just started to practice, any one of the disciples could absolutely suppress him. In no time, they first captured Seventeen.","\"Stop! Otherwise, we'll kill him!\" One of the disciples bellowed, pressing his sword's edge against Seventeen's throat, threatening the young child.","\"Seventeen!\" Yue'er exclaimed, her beautiful eyes overflowing with anger.","Muchen pursed his lips, clenched his fists, and said nothing. His eyes coldly fixed on the disciple holding the sword at Seventeen's neck.","Hao'er stopped, his gaze sharp like a knife, cold and piercing as he looked at that shameless disciple who had the audacity to threaten them. The cold gaze made the disciple shiver, and he involuntarily flinched backwards, but the hand holding the sword at Seventeen's neck did not move.","\"Seize him!\"","A commanding voice echoed, and the Grand Elder, accompanied by his entourage, rushed forward, immediately ordering Hao'er's capture.","\"Young Master, pay me no mind!\" Seventeen shouted, struggling against his captors, only to be nicked by the sword's edge, a trickle of blood staining his neck.","\"Seventeen, remain still!\"","Hao'er's voice was frigid, his small, stern face etched with frost. His gaze flickered over Seventeen's bleeding wound before settling on the disciple, his voice cutting through the air, \"If he dies, I'll ensure you and your entire family will perish with him!\"","Because of these words, and because of Hao'er's cold gaze and serious expression, the disciple was shocked into retreat. He was so scared that his face turned white, his lips trembled, and he took a step back without realising it. He also carefully moved the sword that was resting on Seventeen's neck a little, lest he should accidentally kill him with his sword.","Seventeen listened to Hao'er's words, his eyes welling with tears and his throat choking. He stood still and watched as several disciples came forward and bound Hao'er with ropes.","\"I'm sorry, Young Master, I've caused you trouble,\" he said, bowing his head in self-reproach and feeling very guilty.","\"It's not your fault, we just couldn't beat them,\" Hao'er said, his eyes cold as he stared at the Grand Elder, and at the same time he commanded, \"Silver Wolf, take Chen'er and Yue'er and leave!\"","\"No! I'm not leaving! I want to stay with Big Brother!\" Yue'er exclaimed.","\"I'm not leaving either!\" Muchen shouted his stance as he remained at his spot.","The silver wolf glanced at the two little ones and said nothing. Even if they fled with them at this point, they wouldn't know where to go, not to mention that they were so young, how could they manage without Hao'er and Seventeen looking after them?","Moreover, Hao'er was its contract master, and it could not just leave him alone.","\"Hahahaha, even if you want to leave, you can't.'","A sinister voice, laced with excitement and malice, echoed through the air.","The Silver Wolf spun around, placing itself between the children and the approaching crowd, shielding them behind its massive form. Its bloodthirsty gaze scanned the throng, finally settling on a cultivator draped in a black cloak.","\"Is this the Super Sacred Beast, the Silver Wolf? Indeed, a sight to behold!\" The Old Predecessor of the Mountain Demon fixed his predatory gaze on the Silver Wolf, as if it were a prized possession. His gaze was intensely possessive."]},{"number":4608,"title":"Chapter 4608: Wolf howl","paragraphs":["The silver wolf glanced at him, snorted twice through his nose. Deliberately, it raised a paw, the sharp, formidable claws extended, and then, it licked them slowly. This seemingly casual action carried an undercurrent of menace, a silent threat that resonated deeply with those who witnessed it.","He didn't say a word, but his stance and actions looked extremely threatening to others. The display served as a stark reminder of the creature's predatory nature, a subtle but potent demonstration of its lethal capabilities. It was like a demon was sharpening its knife, preparing to kill, and involuntarily made people feel a chill in their hearts and a sense of vigilance.","The people from the Black Mountain Gate did not dare to get anywhere near the silver wolf; it was a Super Sacred Beast! Even a single bit of pressure from it could make them all collapse. They could only hope for the best, and it seemed that they could only count on their Old Predecessor.","The Old Mountain Demon had trained for many years with few rivals and had now reached the level of a Celestial. Seeing such a dazzling Super Sacred Beast, he felt a rush of excitement and the desire to tame it.","When he saw the silver wolf make a provocative and threatening move, he laughed sinisterly. His gaze swept past the two children standing behind the silver wolf and then landed on the silver wolf in front.","\"Today, let's see just how powerful the Super Sacred Beast really is!\"","With these words, his dark cloak billowed, and a wave of oppressive energy permeated the atmosphere, forcing the people behind him to quickly retreat. No one dared to be too close.","He then revealed his aged, speckled hands, which were obscured by the cloak. He clenched his fists and lunged forward, punching fiercely at the silver wolf in front of him.","\"Stand back.\" The silver wolf warned the two little ones. The Old Mountain Demon lunged forward, but the silver wolf leaped onto its four paws and pounced. The wolf was determined to draw a distance between them to prevent their battle auras from harming the two little ones.","\"Whoosh!\"","The sound of a fierce gust of air cut through the air. The silver wolf leaped into the air, its sharp, pointed claws reflecting a bloodthirsty sheen in the sunlight as it slashed towards the Old Mountain Demon at a speed that was faster than the speed of sound.","The Old Mountain Demon Predecessor was caught off guard; he didn't expect such speed. Despite his strength, he couldn't avoid the attack. His attack struck the silver wolf, but it was easily avoided.","\"Swish! Swish! Swish!\"","The silver wolf's sharp claws sliced through the air, creating visible streams that not only cut through the Old Mountain Demon's black robe but also left a deep gash on his arm from his wrist to his elbow. Even the air currents that passed over the ground made a loud thudding sound like sword energy slashing the ground.","The pressure of the Super Sacred Beast overwhelmed even the Old Predecessor, causing sweat to trickle down his forehead.","\"Hiss! Old Predecessor!\"","\"Old Predecessor, be careful!\"","Seeing that their Old Predecessor had actually been injured after just one exchange with the Super Sacred Beast, everyone's faces changed, and even the people from the sect looked a little unpleasant.","It has eventually come to this. If the Old Mountain Demon Ancestor can suppress them, that would be fine, but if he couldn't.... no one dared to think further.","The silver wolf, whose heart was filled with bloodthirsty murderous intent, did not give the Old Mountain Demon Ancestor a chance to catch his breath. After scratching him, he watched as Shadow One stumbled back, and then pounced again, opening his wolf's mouth and howling, exposing his sharp, bloodthirsty fangs as he viciously pounced on the Old Mountain Demon Ancestor.","\"Awoooo!\"","The wolf's howl carried the pressure of a Super Sacred Beast, long and loud, reverberating through the sky and echoing in everyone's ears for a long time..."]},{"number":4609,"title":"Chapter 4609: Those who oppose me shall perish","paragraphs":["The resonating echo of the silver wolf's howl, while undeniably potent, failed to divert the attention of the assembled observers. Whether they were members of the martial academy, adherents of the Black Mountain Gate, or simply itinerant cultivators, their collective focus remained fixed upon the unfolding confrontation. The contest between the venerable Old Mountain Demon and the majestic silver wolf held their undivided attention, the question of ultimate dominance hanging in the air.","Unfortunately, the sheer velocity of both combatants rendered the engagement a spectacle of rapid, near-indiscernible motion. The Old Mountain Demon and the silver wolf exchanged blows with such speed that their movements blurred into fleeting shadows. A palpable energy radiated from their point of contact, creating a turbulent atmosphere that rippled outward, affecting the surrounding environment.","Muchen and Muyue, positioned behind the engaged parties, remained remarkably unaffected by the surging pressure. The ancient divine beasts residing within their young forms provided a natural buffer against the turbulent forces. However, the relentless air currents, generated by the ferocity of the combat, caused a slight discomfort, reddening their delicate features.","With a protective instinct, Muchen turned, enfolding his sister within his arms, effectively shielding her from the abrasive winds. However, the exposed dorsal surface of his hand, vulnerable to the swirling currents, sustained a minor laceration, a thin trickle of blood staining his pale skin.","\"Insolence!\" Hao'er, witnessing the peril faced by his younger siblings, and the sight of Muchen's blood, felt a surge of incandescent rage. His typically stoic expression twisted into a mask of fury. However, his attempts to intervene were thwarted by the constricting immortal-tying rope, which tightened with each exertion.","Muyue, her head tilted back within Muchen's embrace, observed the crimson streaks marring her twin brother's skin. \"Brother, you are injured!\" she exclaimed, her voice rising in a pitch of childish alarm, her eyes flashing with a fierce protectiveness.","Muchen, his lips pressed together in silent resolve, offered no response, instead tightening his hold on her, pressing her head against his chest to ensure her safety.","The silver wolf, perhaps alerted by Muyue's cry, glanced back and observed the crimson streaks marring Muchen's pristine robe. The stark contrast of the bright red blood against the pale fabric ignited a primal fury within the creature.","With a menacing grin, it lunged forward, its teeth sinking into the Old Mountain Demon's arm.","\"Agh!\" A sharp cry, laced with pain and fear, echoed through the air. The Old Mountain Demon, unable to extricate himself from the wolf's powerful grip, retaliated with a forceful palm strike. However, this action proved to be his undoing. The silver wolf, seizing the opportunity, clamped down with renewed ferocity, severing the limb from its socket. The Old Mountain Demon's body, caught off guard, failed to evade the retaliatory blow.","\"Old Predecessor!\" The assembled onlookers erupted in a chorus of horrified exclamations, their eyes wide with disbelief. They recoiled, their voices trembling, as they witnessed the Old Mountain Demon's severed arm, the bloody wound, and the silver wolf's grisly trophy.","The Old Mountain Demon, his face contorted in agony, clutched at the gaping wound, his pale hand quickly becoming saturated with blood. The crimson fluid flowed unchecked, dripping onto the ground and staining the earth.","He stumbled backward, his forehead glistening with cold sweat, his gaze fixed on the silver wolf, a malevolent intent burning in his eyes. \"Those who obey me will live! Those who oppose me shall perish! I want none of you to survive!\" he roared, his voice a venomous declaration of vengeance."]},{"number":4610,"title":"Chapter 4610: Seize","paragraphs":["His arm was torn off, and the murderous intent surging through the body of the Old Predecessor of the Mountain Demon made his eyes turn bloodshot. A murderous aura burst out from his body, his sinister and bloodthirsty gaze sweeping past the silver wolf and landing on Muchen and Muyue, as well as the bound Hao'er. His face was slightly distorted with anger and hatred, and his entire face became somewhat hideous.","He released his grip on his severed arm, utilizing his spiritual energy to staunch the bleeding and prevent further loss of vital Qi by applying pressure to specific points on his shoulder. \"Seize those brats!\" he commanded, his voice raspy, the words accompanied by a surge of malevolence. He then attacked the silver wolf with renewed ferocity.","The surrounding individuals, who had retreated in the face of the escalating conflict, hesitated upon hearing his command. Observing the Old Mountain Demon's engagement with the Super Sacred Beast, the Sect Master and his Deputy exchanged a grim glance. With gritted teeth, they gathered their energy and rushed towards Muchen and Muyue.","\"Run!\" Hao'er shouted, his voice filled with desperation.","Muchen, perceiving the approaching threat, immediately seized his sister's hand and attempted to flee. However, despite their agility, they were no match for the superior speed and training of the gate's leaders.","\"You little vermin, you will not escape!\" the two men sneered, flanking the children, their hands outstretched to seize them. They prepared to lift the children with a triumphant air, but just as their hands were about to close around their collars, the children, who had appeared to shrink in fear, suddenly sprang into action. Cold, gleaming blades flashed with unexpected speed.","The sharp edges sliced through the men's arms with alarming efficiency, leaving deep, bone-exposing gashes.","\"Ssshh!\" The two men hissed in shock, recoiling from the unexpected attack. One hand pressed against their wounds, while their incredulous eyes fixed upon the four-year-olds.","The children now stood poised like miniature predators, their delicate faces hardened with anger and ferocity. Their small bodies were half-crouched, and they gripped blood-dripping daggers, prepared for further combat.","The surrounding observers were taken aback by this display. Surprise and shock mingled in their expressions.","The fact that these two young children had managed to inflict such grievous wounds upon the masters of the Black Mountain Gate was truly remarkable. Their courage and determination were qualities that many adults lacked, yet these four year olds possessed them in abundance. A common thought echoed through the minds of many: \"They are indeed the children of the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu.\"","However, a grim reality remained. While the children had exploited the men's initial underestimation to inflict damage, they could not withstand a sustained assault. This initial strike was one of opportunity, not of sustained power.","As expected, the men's faces darkened with rage. \"Good, very good!\" they snarled. \"We shall see if you maintain this demeanor!\"","With renewed aggression, they launched another attack, their movements now precise and calculated. If the first encounter had been a lapse in judgement, this would be a demonstration of their true power. They easily deflected the children's attacks, disarmed them, and produced ropes to bind them."]},{"number":4611,"title":"Chapter 4611: Watch Them Die","paragraphs":["The silver wolf, engaged in a fierce struggle with the one-armed Mountain Demon, was momentarily distracted by a commotion behind it. As it glanced back, the Mountain Demon, who had been retreating, seized the opportunity. A strange glint flashed in his eyes, and he swiftly hurled an object, accompanied by a resounding shout.","\"Profound Golden Steel Cage! Trap!\"","Hao'er, witnessing the Mountain Demon's action, immediately narrowed his eyes and shouted out: \"Be careful!\"","The silver wolf, turning its attention back, observed a golden, glowing object descending. It attempted to leap away, but the object seemed to gain an unnatural weight, plummeting with alarming speed.","\"Bang!\"","A deafening thud echoed through the air, and a cloud of dust and smoke billowed outwards. When the dust settled, the silver wolf was seen trapped within a massive, golden, bell-shaped steel cage.","Unlike a traditional bell, this cage was not solid and opaque. Instead, it was a cage constructed of thick steel bars on all sides. The silver wolf, trapped within, attempted to break free, but despite its powerful efforts, the cage remained unyielding.","\"Ha ha ha ha!\"","The Mountain Demon erupted in a triumphant laugh, a sound filled with exhilaration, bloodlust, and a touch of madness. The laughter resonated through the air, vibrating like ripples in water, lingering for an unnerving duration.","Abruptly, his laughter ceased, and his distorted face fixed upon the trapped silver wolf, his eyes burning with bloodthirsty ferocity. \"You tore off my arm,\" he growled, his voice thick with hatred and anger, \"So I shall tear off both arms of your masters! I will make them suffer, a fate worse than death! I shall have my vengeance!\"","\"If you dare to harm them in any way,\" the silver wolf retorted, its voice emanating from within the golden steel cage, the threat and murderous intent unmistakable, \"I will obliterate your entire lineage and leave you without a burial!\"","\"Is that so? I would like to see you try. What can you possibly do?\" he taunted. Just as he took a step forward, a sudden cacophony of sounds erupted from the surrounding area.","\"Awoooooooooo!\"","\"Awoooooo!\"","\"Awooooooooo!\"","The howls of wolves echoed from all directions, drawing closer with each passing moment, and the sheer number of them was alarming.","\"Why are there wolf howls?\"","\"Why are there wolves here?\"","\"And so many of them!\"","The onlookers exclaimed in surprise, exchanging bewildered glances. Some immediately ascended into the air to gain a broader perspective. Their faces paled at what they saw.","\"Oh no! A large pack of wolves is approaching! There are at least two or three hundred of them!\"","The cultivator who had taken to the sky descended, his voice urgent. \"Those wolves are coming from the forest behind the sect! They are not ordinary wolves, but wind wolves!\"","\"What? What are we going to do?\"","Panic gripped those with weaker constitutions. Wind wolves were known for their speed and ferocity, and the sheer number of them presented a formidable threat. Facing them in combat offered no guarantee of survival.","Hearing the reports, the Mountain Demon narrowed his malevolent gaze and fixed it on the trapped silver wolf. \"You summoned them!\"","\"Hmph!\" The silver wolf snorted, offering no further explanation.","The Mountain Demon, his eyes narrowed, glanced at the wolf, then addressed the two men holding Muchen and Muyue. \"Bring those two brats here!\" He extended his tongue, licking the blood on the back of his hand, his voice thick with malicious intent. \"I wish to see with your very own eyes and watch how these brats die a slow and painful death!\""]},{"number":4612,"title":"Chapter 4612: Angry Throw","paragraphs":["The silver wolf, its eyes blazing with fury, hissed and growled, \"Do not lay a hand on them!\"","\"Hahaha! And why should I not?\" the Old Mountain Demon sneered, his gaze filled with malice. \"Because they are the offspring of Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu? Where is she? Why does she not appear? Even if I slaughter her children before her very eyes, what can she possibly do?\"","Hao'er, trapped within the formation, clenched his fists, his anger reaching a boiling point. He yearned to tear the man apart, but his strength was insufficient, even to contend with the sect's dignitaries.","As he watched the two men drag the bound Muchen and Muyue forward, Hao'er took a deep breath and shouted, \"Wait!\"","His usually stoic face was taut with tension as he addressed the Old Mountain Demon. \"I will command the Silver Wolf to recall the wolves. I, and the Silver Wolf, will accompany you. In exchange, you will release my siblings and the guard.\"","The Old Mountain Demon narrowed his eyes, scrutinizing Hao'er without uttering a word.","\"Do you not desire my contracted beast?\" Hao'er continued, his eyes fixed on the man. \"The Silver Wolf is a Super Sacred Beast. If you release my siblings and their escorts, I will sever my contract with it, allowing you to forge a new one.\" He paused, then added, \"You should understand that Super Sacred Beasts are exceedingly rare. Without my voluntary release, you will never tame the Silver Wolf and form a contract.\"","The silver wolf turned its attention to Hao'er, its gaze questioning.","Hao'er, maintaining eye contact, conveyed his intentions through spiritual awareness. For now, they needed to buy time and ensure Muchen and Muyue's safety. They would devise a plan once the children were out of harm's way.","The silver wolf, understanding the situation, glanced at the magical artifact that held it captive. It recognized the futility of resistance for the moment. This was their only option.","The Old Mountain Demon, his gaze shifting between the four-year-old children, curled his lips into a bloodthirsty grin. \"Release them? Hah! Do you take me for a fool? Do you not know the saying, 'to release a tiger back into the mountains'? These two brats, barely four years old, managed to wound two of my Black Mountain Gate masters. If I allow them to live, I will be sowing the seeds of our own destruction.\"","He fixed his malevolent gaze on Hao'er. \"You will sever your contract with the Silver Wolf, whether you desire it or not. Otherwise, I will break the limbs of these two children before your very eyes, then dismember them and feed them to the wolves! As for the rest of their bodies...\"","His eerie voice dripped with cruelty and bloodlust. He reached out, lifting Muyue by her collar, bringing her close to his face, inhaling her scent. \"A primordial spirit body,\" he mused, \"soaked in medicinal wine, it would make a potent tonic.\"","\"You dare!\" Hao'er's eyes burned with rage as he strained against his bonds, attempting to break free. But the immortal rope and the barrier held him fast.","\"You dare eat me? My Father and Mother will never let you!\" Muyue's young voice was filled with fury, her beautiful eyes glaring at him. Her small body dangled helplessly, preventing her from kicking him. In her fury, she spat directly into his face.","\"You are seeking death!\" A being of his stature, a powerful Celestial level, had been spat upon by a mere child. His killing intent surged. He raised her high above his head, preparing to slam her onto the ground."]},{"number":4613,"title":"Chapter 4613: Save","paragraphs":["\"Yue'er!\"","\"Sister!\"","\"Young Miss Yue!\"","Hao'er, Muchen, and Seventeen cried out in unison, their voices filled with terror. They strained against their restraints, desperate to intervene, but they were held fast, forced to watch as the Old Mountain Demon seized Yue'er by her collar and lifted her high, preparing to slam her onto the ground. The scene ignited a wave of horror, their hearts constricting with despair.","\"Yue'er!\" \"Little sister!\"","Hao'er and Muchen's voices, raw with desperation, echoed through the air, tinged with a heart-wrenching plea. \"No! Do not kill her! Please, do not!\"","Yue'er, suspended high above the Old Mountain Demon, was suddenly and violently hurled downwards. Caught completely off guard, she could only register the anguished cries of her brothers.","The Old Mountain Demon's descent was swift and brutal, fueled by a clear intent to kill. He aimed to crush her, to extinguish her life in a single, devastating blow. As Yue'er plummeted, she felt a chilling rush of air across her cheeks. Her vision blurred, and she instinctively squeezed her eyes shut, letting out a startled cry.","\"Ah!\"","The surrounding onlookers watched the scene unfold, their hearts pounding in their chests. A lump formed in their throats, and their breaths hitched.","They stared in disbelief. To them, she was an innocent child, yet the Old Mountain Demon was prepared to commit such a heinous act, to extinguish her life in such a brutal manner.","Considering the force with which the Old Mountain Demon was throwing her, augmented by his spiritual energy, Yue'er's body was destined to impact the ground with horrifying force. If her head struck the ground first, her skull would be shattered, her brains splattering.","The thought of such a gruesome spectacle was unbearable for many. They averted their gaze, closing their eyes or turning away, their hearts heavy with silent sorrow.","They felt a pang of pity for the little girl, a sense of injustice at her impending demise. They perceived the cruelty of her fate, yet no one dared to intervene, to defy the Old Mountain Demon's wrath.","However, just as everyone braced for the inevitable, a figure, swift and ethereal as a phantom, emerged from the formation. With astonishing speed, they reached out and caught Yue'er, halting her descent.","The sudden turn of events froze the air, silencing all but the rustling leaves and the approaching howls of the wolves.","Hao'er, Muchen, Seventeen, and the silver wolf released a collective sigh of relief as they witnessed Yue'er's rescue.","They turned their attention to the rescuer, their eyes searching for answers.","Who was this individual? How did they dare to intervene in such a perilous situation? Moreover, they did not recognize the person. Dressed in a black robe, they did not appear to be affiliated with the martial academy. And, most notably, they wore a mask!","\"Little girl, are you frightened?\"","The man's deep voice, laced with a gentle amusement, resonated with a pleasant timbre. It was soothing, like a gentle spring breeze, imbued with a sense of calm.","Hearing the voice, feeling the secure embrace of the rescuer, Yue'er slowly opened her eyes. She was met with the gaze of deep, dark pupils, filled with a gentle smile. However, she could not discern his features.","The man wore a demonic mask, concealing his face. She could only hear his voice, not see his true appearance."]},{"number":4614,"title":"Chapter 4614: Who are you?","paragraphs":["Yue'er blinked her large, captivating eyes, her delicate face registering a moment surprise. She hadn't anticipated a sudden rescuer. Her gaze settled on the masked figure before her, and she inquired in a soft, childlike voice, \"Who are you?\"","\"I am your rescuer,\" the man replied, a subtle smile playing upon his lips. He adjusted his hold on her, shifting her position. As he did so, the ropes binding her fell away, and he cradled her securely in one arm.","The sudden appearance of this individual sent ripples of shock through the crowd. The Grand Elder, who had previously encountered the man, was particularly stunned. His eyes widened with fear as he exclaimed, \"That is the wandering cultivator residing in the guest house!\"","Upon hearing this revelation, the martial sect members exchanged grave glances. One of the venerable elders observed, \"He bypassed the barrier with ease. Our barrier, he traversed it effortlessly.\"","\"And from such a distance, he managed to catch the little girl, whom the Old Mountain Demon threw with such force. The speed...\" another individual trailed off, his face paling.","\"I cannot discern his level of cultivation,\" another elder muttered, his voice laced with bewilderment.","In contrast to the others, the Old Mountain Demon's face was contorted with unvented fury. The unexpected arrival of this unknown figure ignited his rage. Immediately, he channeled his energy into a powerful palm strike, aiming it at the masked man.","However, as the visible wave of energy hurtled towards the masked man and Yue'er, the man did not flinch. He merely shifted his gaze from Yue'er's rosy cheeks, lifted his sleeve, and flicked it dismissively. The air current dissipated, and the Old Mountain Demon was sent hurtling backward several meters.","\"Bang!\"","The force of the deflected energy slammed into the Old Mountain Demon's chest, causing his internal energy and blood to surge upward. He coughed up a mouthful of blood.","\"Pffttt!\"","His footing faltered, and he lost his balance, tumbling to the ground.","\"Old Predecessor!\" The crowd cried out in alarm, rushing to his aid.","\"Stop! If you do not stop, I will kill him!\" The Sect Master of the Black Mountain Gate, holding Muchen captive, threatened the masked man.","\"Brother!\" Yue'er cried out, her voice filled with anxiety. Her small hands clutched at the masked man's clothing, her voice pleading, \"My brother, my brother, please save my brother!\"","\"Be good, do not worry,\" the man reassured her, patting her head awkwardly.","He raised his gaze, fixing it on the Black Mountain Gate leader. His deep eyes turned cold, and his voice hardened, \"Release the child, and I will grant you a swift death.\"","The indifferent tone, though seemingly gentle, sent a chill down the Black Mountain Gate Sect Master's spine. Fear gripped his heart, and beads of cold sweat trickled down his forehead. His grip on Muchen's neck trembled slightly.","\"Do not do anything rash. I have this child. If you dare to move, I will kill...\" the Black Mountain Gate Sect Master stammered. However, before he could finish his sentence, the masked man vanished."]},{"number":4615,"title":"Chapter 4615: For you","paragraphs":["\"Who do you intend to kill?\" The man who donned a ghost face mask, approached the Black Mountain Sect Master from behind with Yue'er held securely in his arm. His indifferent and cold voice was as terrifying as that of a hellish demon, entering his ears eerily.","The Sectmaster, previously a figure of formidable authority, found himself utterly immobilized. The sudden apparition of the masked man, combined with the palpable aura of death emanating from him, rendered any attempt at resistance futile. The mere touch of the man's hand upon his shoulder gave him a sense of impending doom, as fear overcame him.","The hands that had moments before restrained Muchen, one gripping his neck with cruel intent, involuntarily relaxed their hold. The pressure exerted by the masked man's presence compelled the Sect Master's limbs to relinquish their grasp, as if guided by an unseen force. Muchen, now free, hastily sought refuge beside the masked man, his gaze fixed on his sister. \"Yue'er, are you alright?\" he inquired, his voice laced with anxiety.","\"I am fine, brother~\" Yue'er responded, attempting to come down, but found herself firmly held within the masked man's grasp.","In the midst of their converstaion, they heard a sharp snapping sound as they both tunred their heads towardas the source of it. All they saw was thae Ghost Faced Masked Man give the Black Mountain Sect Master a light pat on the shoulder. It was as if all of his bones had been smashed, and his whole body collapsed into a ball on the ground. A miserable scream came from his mouth, his mouth overflowing with blood, his eyes wide open, and his body twitching, until, unable to catch his breath until finally, he stopped breathing.","Yue'er, momentarily stunned by the brutal display, observed as the masked man turned his attention towards her. \"Did I scare you?\" He asked apprehensively.","She shook her head, attempting to project an air of composure. \"No, I am quite brave.\"","Upon hearing this, the man smiled and said, \"Very good.'","\"You can put me down already~,\" Yue'er took the opportunity to say, and then looked at the Mountain Demon again, wrinkling her nose and saying, \"What if you can't deal with that Child-eating demon?\"","\"Ha ha...\" The man chuckled softly, still holding her in one arm, and said, \"I only need one hand to deal with him.\"","He then proceeded to release Muchen from his restraints with a swift, precise motion. His gaze shifted towards the trapped silver wolf, a creature of formidable power, and a subtle, enigmatic smile played upon his lips. He approached the caged beast, Yue'er still cradled in his arm, followed closely by Muchen.","\"The silver wolf is a Super Sacred Beast, he's sooooo powerful, how can this cage trap it?\" Yue'er asked, looking at the golden bell-shaped cage curiously.","\"This is a rare treasure, not to mention Super Sacred Beasts, but even Ancient Sacred Beasts can be trapped,\" he replied casually as he raised his hand and pressing it against the mysterious golden steel cover. With a gentle turn of the palm, all that could be heard was a clang accompanied by a burst of air.","\"Pfffft!\"","The Mountain Demon, who was being supported, had his blood contract with his precious artifact broken, causing his blood and energy to turn against him and his spirit energy to recede. A mouthful of his heart's blood spurted out, making his already pale face appear even paler. The spurting of his heart's blood also aggravated his injuries, causing him to feel a darkness before his eyes, but he forced himself to hold on.","Yue'er watched curiously as he turned his hand around, and the artifact was collected in the palm of his hand, becoming a small golden bell.","\"Here you go, it's yours now.\" He said as he placed the artifact in Yue'er's hand."]},{"number":4616,"title":"Chapter 4616: Strong","paragraphs":["Yue'er looked at the small object in her palm. A sly glint flashed by her beautiful eyes. She looked at him and said, \"My mother told me not to take things from strangers. Besides, I don't even know who you are, so I really can't accept this.\"","Hearing her words, the man's lips curled up slightly, revealing a shallow arc: \"You will learn my identity in time. For now, there is no rush.\"","Seeing that he divulge anything, Yue'er's sly gaze shifted to her Big Brother and Seventeen, who had been captured by the people from the sect, and said, \"But my Big Brother and Seventeen are still in their hands.\"","As soon as she finished her words, he saw him raise his hand, and the spiritual energy in the palm of his hand condensed and shot towards the barrier. With a thunderous impact, the barrier shattered, the released energy rippling outwards.","\"Aren't you going to save your master?\" The man glanced at the silver wolf next to him and spoke in a slow and steady voice.","The silver wolf glanced at him, and the next moment, he leapt towards the people from that sect.","Seeing this, the disciples were already too shocked to think, and had no heart to catch Hao'er and Seventeen. What's more, they had seen with their own eyes how the Black Mountain Sect Master had been killed by the mysterious Ghost Faced Masked Man with a single palm strike, and they didn't want to end up like that.","Therefore, when they saw the barrier broken and the silver wolf pounce towards them, they were so scared that their faces turned white, and they exclaimed, \"Quickly! Run away!\"","At this moment, they no longer cared about their image, and they all started running away in disarray. Some were so desperate that they fell to the ground and crawled desperately to get away.","\"Hmph! None of you will escape!\" The silver wolf snorted, and first came to Seventeen's side and used its claws to cut the ropes on his body. Then it said, \"Go untie that bundle of immortal ropes.\" At the same time, it raised its head and let out a long howl.","\"Awooooo!\"","The wolf's howl echoed in the air and, as it reached the distance, the wind wolves heard the sound and, one after the other, dashed past like the wind. When they arrived here, they pounced on the people and bit them hard.","As the several hundred wind wolves joined in the attack, the scene became chaotic. The people of Heishanmen also came to their senses in the midst of their horror, and without caring about the body of their master, they exclaimed in alarm, \"Run, run quickly!\"","Seeing that those people were about to escape with the Old Mountain Demon, Yue'er's eyes flashed with anger, and she said angrily, \"That demon who eats children cannot be allowed to go! Neither can any of their people leave alive!\"","She holds a grudge. These people want to kill them and eat them. She can't beat them, otherwise she would definitely kill them herself!","Listening to Yue'er's words, the Ghost Faced Masked Man curled his lips and said in a good-natured manner, \"Fine, let them all stay.\"","As soon as he spoke, a powerful pressure emanated from his body. As the pressure spread, those who had originally been about to run were one after the other overwhelmed by the powerful pressure and fell to the ground with a thud. They were unable to move, as if a mountain were weighing down on them, and they found it difficult to breathe.","\"Eh?\" Yue'er looked at the scene in surprise, then at him again. Her beautiful eyes blinked as she thought about something.","At this time, the Ghost Faced Masked Man held Yue'er in one arm and walked with steady steps towards the place where the Mountain Demon was, not stopping until he was in front of him."]},{"number":4617,"title":"Chapter 4617: Means","paragraphs":["\"Just who on earth are you?!\"","The Mountain Demon, a husk of his former self, lay sprawled on the blood-soaked earth as he uttered with desperation. His pale face, betrayed the utter defeat that gripped him. He knew escape was impossible, his fate sealed by the masked figure standing before him. His breaths, ragged and shallow, broke the tense silence.","\"Someone who can end you,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man replied, his voice a low, steady rumble that held the weight of finality. He tilted his head, his masked gaze shifting to Yue'er, who remained nestled in his arm. \"Little one, how would you have him meet his end?\"","Yue'er, her brow furrowed in thought, tilted her head, her delicate features a stark contrast to the brutality of the scene. After a moment of contemplation, her soft voice, surprisingly firm, echoed through the air. \"He tried to eat us. So, someone should pull out his teeth, snap his tendons, destroy his cultivation, and then throw him to the wolves.\"","A collective shiver ran through the onlookers. The delicate girl, a vision of innocence, had just delivered a verdict of chilling cruelty. They stared at her, their eyes wide with a mixture of fear and disbelief.","\"As you wish,\" the masked man said, his tone devoid of emotion. With a casual flick of his wrist, he obliterated the Mountain Demon's cultivation, eliciting a raw, guttural scream of agony. He then turned his attention to a trembling disciple of the Black Mountain Sect. \"You. Pull out his teeth, break his tendons, and deliver him to the wolves.\"","\"I... I can't,\" the disciple stammered, his legs buckling beneath him. His face, drained of color, mirrored the terror that gripped his soul. He glanced at the chaotic scene unfolding around him: wolves tearing into the flesh of his former allies, the ground slick with blood. The masked man, however, remained untouched, a silent sentinel amidst the carnage.","\"Do as I say, and you will live,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man stated, his voice a low, menacing promise. \"Refuse, and you will suffer a far worse fate.\"","The disciple, his body trembling uncontrollably, looked up, a flicker of desperate hope in his eyes. \"If I do it... I will live?\"","\"Yes,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man confirmed. \"I will spare you.\"","\"Alright, I will do it! I will do it!\" The disciple exclaimed, his voice filled with a newfound resolve. The prospect of survival, however slim, ignited a spark of determination within him. He approached the Old Predecessor, his hands trembling. \"Forgive me, Old Predecessor,\" he muttered, his voice barely a whisper. \"I have no choice.\"","He forced the Old Predecessor's mouth open, his hands moving with a grim efficiency. One by one, he extracted the man's teeth, each pull accompanied by a muffled groan of pain. The Mountain Demon's face, once a mask of cruel power, now resembled a grotesque caricature, his mouth a bloody ruin. With his cultivation destroyed, he appeared frail and ancient, on the verge of death.","The disciple then proceeded to sever the tendons in the Mountain Demon's hands and feet, rendering him utterly helpless. The once-powerful man could no longer even muster a scream, his body a broken, lifeless husk. The disciple, his face pale but resolute, lifted the limp body and, with a final, forceful heave, tossed it into the midst of the ravenous wolves.","A wave of revulsion and morbid fascination washed over the onlookers. They watched the disciple, their expressions a mix of horror and grudging understanding. In their hearts, they knew that, faced with the same choice, they might have made the same desperate bargain.","\"I have done as you commanded, Senior,\" the disciple said, his voice trembling as he bowed before the masked man."]},{"number":4618,"title":"Chapter 4618: Old Friend","paragraphs":["\"Get lost!\"","The Ghost Faced Masked Man said, not killing him with his hands. Instead, he held Yue'er in one arm and looked at the cultivators' intensifying fight with the wolves.","Hao'er and Seventeen came to the masked man's side. Hao'er looked at the man and held out his hands, saying, \"Give my sister back to me.\"","The Ghost Faced Masked Man, his gaze unwavering, responded, \"It's not safe.\" He remained resolute, the small child cradled securely in his arm, no intention to hand her over.","Hao'er and Muchen looked at each other. Since the guy wasn't making trouble, they just stayed close, watching the silver wolf lead the wind wolves against the sect and Black Mountain Gate people.","Meanwhile, Murong Yixuan was heading towards the sect. He had heard about a big fight happening there, with the Old Predecessor of Black Mountain Gate attacking three children. He immediately sped up as he stood on his sword, flying over at full speed.","He had met Feng Jiu and Xuanyuan Mo Ze and knew their children were missing. He had been asking around, looking for them.","He came to this area and heard that there were three kids were at the sect, thinking that by some stroke of luck, they might even be Feng Jiu's children, he rushed straight there.","Flying closer, he felt the air shaking, like a huge fight was happening. He also felt a strong oppressive aura of a beast.","\"They're really here,\" he thought. He realized the fight was at the back of the sect, so he flew that way.","Looking down, he saw chaos. The three children stood out.","\"Those are Feng Jiu and Xuanyuan Mo Ze's children...\"","He was about to land when the Ghost Faced Masked Man looked up at him. He frowned, wondering who he was.","He tried to sense the guy's power, but got nothing.","Down below, the Ghost Faced Masked Man glanced up, then looked away, like he didn't care.","Hao'er and Muchen followed the guy's gaze and saw the white-clad man in the sky. Muchen didn't know him, but Hao'er recognized him.","Murong Yixuan landed in front of them. He looked at the kids, then at Hao'er. \"Do you remember me?\" he asked gently.","Hao'er nodded.","Murong Yixuan smiled a little. \"Your parents are looking for you. Are you alright?\"","\"Have you met my Father and Mother?\" Yue'er blinked her big, beautiful eyes at Murong Yixuan in front of her and asked curiously."]},{"number":4619,"title":"Chapter 4619: Leave it be","paragraphs":["Murong Yixuan smiled gently, his gaze softening as he addressed the children. \"I have indeed had the pleasure of meeting your parents,\" he confirmed, his voice filled with warmth. \"They spoke of you, and I have come to know of your circumstances through them.\" His voice trailed off momentarily as his attention shifted to the Ghost Faced Masked Man, a subtle inquiry lingering in his eyes. \"Do you happen to know him?\" He asked, his gaze lingering on the enigmatic figure.","\"No, but he saved us~\" Yue'er replied honestly.","Upon hearing Yue'er's words, Murong Yixuan bowed his head respectfully towards the Ghost Faced Masked Man. \"I am Murong Yixuan,\" he introduced himself, his tone filled with gratitude. \"Thank you for saving my friend's children. How may I address you?\"","\"The reasons for my actions are of no concern to you,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man responded, his voice devoid of warmth, a chilling indifference permeating his words.","Undeterred, Murong Yixuan pressed on, his resolve unwavering. \"My intention is to reunite them with their parents. Therefore, please put the child down.\"","\"This young girl is my chosen disciple,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man declared, his voice firm and unyielding, his grip on Yue'er tightening. He displayed no inclination to relinquish her to anyone. In his perception, the moment he intervened to save her, her life became his to guide. He saw no reason to surrender his chosen apprentice.","Murong Yixuan's eyes flickered with a hint of surprise, yet he maintained his composure, offering a placating smile. \"It is commendable that you see her as a worthy apprentice,\" he conceded. \"However, they have endured a long and arduous journey, and their parents are consumed with worry. If you harbor reservations about my trustworthiness, I propose that you accompany us as we return them to their parents. After their reunion, you may formally request Feng Jiu's consent to take her as your disciple.\"","\"Hah! Do you presume to dictate my actions?\" The Ghost Faced Masked Man retorted, his voice laced with disdain, a clear indication of his displeasure.","\"I wish to return to my parents,\" Yue'er interjected, her voice trembling slightly, her small frame wriggling in his grasp. \"Please let me go. I do not wish to be your disciple.\"","\"Sister!\" Muchen exclaimed, seizing her hand, his eyes glaring at the masked man with fierce protectiveness. \"My Sister will never leave our side! You are not permitted to take her away!\"","Observing Yue'er's distress, her face etched with panic, as if she feared being abducted, Murong Yixuan reassured her, \"Do not worry. I will ensure you return to your parents.\"","Murong Yixuan then shifted the conversation, suggesting, \"Let us relocate to a more tranquil setting. This place is too chaotic, and you appear to be injured. Your wounds require attention.\" He directed his gaze towards Muchen, his concern evident.","\"Silver Wolf!\" Hao'er called out, attracting the attention of the imposing creature, who had been addressing several elders of the sect. Silver Wolf swiftly bounded towards them, his eyes scrutinizing Murong Yixuan.","\"How are the others?\" Hao'er inquired, referring to the elders and the sect master.","\"Hmph! The Sect Master feigned unconsciousness, observing from a concealed position. He fled the moment the barrier was breached. As for the elders, I imparted a lesson to them. They sustained severe injuries, though none are fatal,\" Silver Wolf reported, then inquired, \"Does Master wish for me to eliminate them?\"","Hao'er surveyed the scene, noting the absence of any approaching individuals or wolves. The immediate vicinity was littered with dismembered bodies, their blood staining the ground, a grim testament to the ferocity of the conflict. The casualties included both members of the Black Mountain Gate and cultivators from the sect. Hao'er, contemplating the horrific scene, pursed his lips and, after a moment of somber silence, declared, \"Nevermind, let's just leave it be.\""]},{"number":4620,"title":"Chapter 4620: Guan Xilin’s arrival","paragraphs":["So, in the midst of this chaotic battle, the Ghost Faced Masked Man and Murong Yixuan quietly left with the three children and Seventeen...","In a town a few hundred miles away...","Within the confines of a private dining room in a local restaurant, the group gathered around a table laden with an array of dishes. The Ghost Faced Masked Man, with a meticulous care that belied his previous cold demeanor, began to arrange the food before Yue'er, creating a veritable mountain of sustenance within her bowl.","\"Eat,\" he instructed, his gaze fixed upon Yue'er, urging her to partake of the meal.","Yue'er, confronted with the towering pile of food, stared in bewilderment, her voice tinged with incredulity. \"There is so much,\" she exclaimed, \"how can I possibly consume it all? My stomach would surely burst.\"","\"Then eat what pleases you, and leave what does not,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man replied, his tone softening slightly. \"Which dish do you like the most?\"","Murong Yixuan, observing the interaction, shook his head gently, a soft sigh escaping his lips. \"Just let her pick her own dishes,\" he suggested. \"She cannot possibly finish everything.\" He proceeded to ladle soup into each of the children's bowls.","\"Start with the soup then,\" he advised, his voice soothing. \"Go ahead and eat whatever you want. There's no need to rush.\"","Yue'er, who was sipping her soup slowly, asked: \"When will we return?\"","Hao'er and Muchen echoed her sentiment, their gazes fixed upon Murong Yixuan. They all had the thought that this person would be able to take them back.","Murong Yixuan offered a reassuring smile. \"I will take you back to Feng Manor, and once there, I will have them notify your Mother. However, I cannot bring you back instantly. It's still quite a distance away, but if you follow me, you need not worry about safety.\"","\"Very well,\" Hao'er nodded in agreement.","Murong Yixuan turned his attention to the masked man, taking a sip of his drink before posing a question. \"Did you know Feng Jiu and the others before?\" He wondered if this person was someone Feng Jiu knew.","\"I have heard of them, but we have never met,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man replied, maintaining his enigmatic persona.","\"I can see that your strength is unfathomable, and I imagine that you must also come from an extraordinary background.\" Murong Yixuan ventured, attempting to elicit further information. However, the Ghost Faced Masked Man remained unyielding, offering no further insights.","The Ghost Faced Masked Man, seemingly unfazed by Murong Yixuan's inquiries, continued to sip his wine, his demeanor suggesting that Murong Yixuan's presence was inconsequential.","Discerning the futility of his inquiries, Murong Yixuan shifted his focus to the children, ensuring they were comfortable and well-fed. He resolved to allow them ample time to rest and recuperate before commencing their journey back to Feng Manor.","Half a month later, Guan Xilin arrived at the boundary separating the mortal realm from the divine realm. His heart pulsed with anticipation as he traversed the terrain on his sword. Having traced their path to Floating Edge Immortal Island, he learned that the children had been brought to this region of the divine realm.","He had pressed onward with unwavering determination, confident that he would finally reunite with the children. He envisioned the joy that would illuminate Little Nine's face upon their return, a prospect that brought a broad, albeit slightly disheveled, smile to his own face.","He arrived at the sect's main gate, his sword carrying him swiftly through the air. As he approached, he noted the signs of a recent conflict, the surrounding trees bearing the marks of battle.","Despite his curiosity, he refrained from comment, instead opting to approach the gate and announce his presence. \"Open the door! Open the door!\" he called out.","The disciple of guarding the door couldn't help but pause slightly when he heard the sudden commotion. He thought about the life wrecking fight that happened half a month ago, and his heart still trembled slightly. Listening carefully, he seemed to hear only one person outside, so he asked loudly, \"Who is it knocking? What do you want?\""]},{"number":4621,"title":"Chapter 4621: Knowing","paragraphs":["\"I'm here to look for someone , open the door.\" Guan Xilin announced, his voice carrying a clear note of threat. His words, blunt and to the point, were designed to cut through any nonsense and get him inside quickly.","The disciple inside, still rattled from the recent violent clash, listened to the words and thought about it, before he opened a small crack. When he saw that there was indeed only one person outside, and that the man had broad shoulders and a powerful build, he let out a small sigh of relief.","This man had a beard covering his face, a stern expression, and a commanding presence. However, there was only one of him, and he was a stranger, so perhaps he was a relative of a sect member.","So the disciple who opened the door asked, \"Who are you? Who are you here to see?\"","\"Have three children come here? The older one's about ten, a young boy, and the younger two are twins, identical. I'm their Uncle, here to pick them up...\"","Before Guan Xilin could finish his sentence, the disciple who had been listening to him saw his eyes widen, and a look of sheer terror appeared on his face. Then, with a loud bang, he slammed the door shut, and faintly, from inside, there seemed to be panicked cries.","Guan Xilin rubbed his nose, a bit baffled. He hadn't even finished talking, and the other person had already slammed the door. Were the three kids here or not?","Thinking about this, he didn't wait outside the door either, but just used his energy and soared into the air, flying over their sect and heading inside. However, as he hovered high above and looked down, he saw that the disciple who had slammed the door was running up the mountain, shouting the whole time.","\"Oh no! Oh no! The three kids' Uncle's here!\"","As the disciple's cry of alarm spread throughout the sect, the disciples who had been sitting under the sect tree, practising swordplay in the open space, or walking slowly in groups of three or five, all turned pale with fear like startled birds and quickly fled back to their rooms.","\"What on earth's going on?\"","Guan Xilin looked at the rather odd scene in surprise, secretly puzzled. He flew slowly above the sect with his sword, and saw that the disciple who had originally run up the peak also wanted to hide when he realised there was no one around. At that moment, he descended from the sky and landed in front of the disciple.","\"Speak! What happened here!\" Guan Xilin shouted in a calm but forceful voice.","\"Ah! It's not my fault, honestly! It was the sect and a few elders who pushed those three children towards the Old Mountain Demon. It really wasn't my fault...\" The disciple's legs gave way with fear, and with a thud, he fell to his knees before Guan Xilin.","Hearing his words, Guan Xilin's face changed, and his aura immediately darkened. A fierce look crossed his eyes as he shouted in a stern voice, \"What are you talking about! To what Old Mountain Demon? How are they doing now?\" As he spoke, he leaned forward, took a step and grabbed the disciple by the lapel of his shirt, and lifted him up.","\"Mercy, have mercy... They, they're alright, they were rescued...\" The disciple said in a trembling voice, his eyes full of fear, for fear that the man in front of him would kill him with a single angry blow.","\"Rescued? Who rescued them? And where have they gone now? Tell me everything! If you hold anything back, I'll kill you!\" Guan Xilin put him down and spoke with authority and severity.","\"Yes, yes, here's what happened...\" The disciple didn't dare hold anything back and told him everything that had happened."]},{"number":4622,"title":"Chapter 4622: Unleash one’s power","paragraphs":["Upon hearing the words of the disciple, Guan Xilin's murderous aura also spread out along with it. His pair of majestic eyes swept across the pale face of the disciple, and he let out a loud harrumph.","\"Hmph! Sending three children out to die like this, such a sect is not worthy of being called a righteous sect, there is simply no need for it to exist!\"","The sonorous and powerful voice echoed in the air along with a strong sense of authority. As soon as he finished speaking, the aura of mysterious energy surging from his body, and he stomped his foot heavily on the ground.","\"Bang!\"","\"Crack!\"","His foot struck the ground with devastating force, causing it to crack open instantly, emitting a sharp, splintering sound. As the cracks spread outwards, a sudden, thunderous rumble emanated from the mountain peak, and half of it collapsed, sending rubble cascading down.","\"Rumble! Bang! Bang! Bang!\"","For a time, the peaks within the sect crumbled, gravel rolled down, and dust filled the air, obscuring the scene.","The Sect Master, alerted by the commotion, immediately emerged from his quarters, shouting angrily, \"Who dares to come here and act so recklessly!\"","He had been resting in his courtyard, attempting to recover from his injuries sustained in the recent conflict. Although he had escaped the Mountain Demon's attack relatively quickly, he had still suffered severe injuries from the powerful palm strike. As for the elders, they were also recuperating from the wounds inflicted by the Super Sacred Beast, both physically and emotionally traumatised, they rarely left their courtyards.","Hearing the sound of the mountain peak crumbling within the sect, they all emerged from their respective dwellings, gathering their remaining strength, determined to confront the intruder. The Sect Master, already seething with anger and seeking an outlet for his frustration, was eager to deal with the person causing such disruption.","However, upon seeing a man standing on a flying sword, hovering in midair, he frowned slightly and demanded angrily, \"Who are you, and why have you destroyed the main peak of my sect!\"","Guan Xilin looked him up and down, and then asked in a calm, authoritative voice, \"Are you the Sect Master of this sect?\"","\"Yes, I am...\" The Sect Master began to reply, but was interrupted by a snort from Guan Xilin.","\"Perfect timing! Take this!\"","As soon as the words left his lips, Guan Xilin's hand moved, and a long knife materialized in his grasp. In the next instant, the long knife swung, unleashing a torrent of energy that resembled a surging mountain river, hurtling towards the Sect Master. The sheer speed and force of the attack shocked the Sect Master, forcing him to dodge instinctively in a flustered manner.","\"Whoosh!\"","\"Bang!\"","The sound of the fierce air current sliced through the air, carrying the whistling of powerful wind blades. Suddenly, with a resounding bang, the blade of the great knife descended, its force encompassing mountains and rivers in a single stroke, cleaving the mountain peak behind the Sect Master in half!","\"Rumble!\"","A deafening rumble shook the entire sect. The powerful aura of the mysterious energy spread outwards with the slash, filling the air between the mountains.","The Sect Master looked back in horror and saw that the mountain peak had been cleanly bisected by the blade's aura, creating the appearance of two separate mountain peaks. Between the two peaks, due to the vibrations of the blade's energy, the falling rubble had created a gap several metres wide. At the foot of the mountain, dust and sand swirled, and the faint screams of the disciples could be heard echoing from the broken peak.","The Sect Master's face paled, his eyes wide with shock and fear. He looked back at the man holding the long knife and asked in a trembling voice, \"Who... who are you really...?\""]},{"number":4623,"title":"Chapter 4623: Abolish and Kill","paragraphs":["The disciple, who had scurried into a corner to hide the moment Guan Xilin stomped the ground and seized the opportunity to escape, witnessed the Sect Master's ashen face and his complete lack of recognition. He immediately blurted out, \"Sect, Sect Master, he's the Uncle of those three children!\"","The Sect Master, already pale with fear, recoiled several metres upon hearing this, his face contorted with terror. \"You, you're Guan Xilin!\"","Feng Jiu's adoptive brother, the legendary swordsman Guan Xilin! He had never met him, but he had heard countless tales of the renowned Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu and her formidable companions. Seeing the man's appearance, the long sword in his hand, and the overwhelming aura of power emanating from him, he was certain beyond doubt that this was Guan Xilin.","\"Hmph! I'm glad you know!\" Guan Xilin swung his massive sword, pointing it diagonally downward, his fierce gaze fixed on the Sect Master. \"Daring to endanger my precious niece and nephews! How do you wish to die?\"","The Sect Master trembled, his voice faltering. \"I was forced into it! Please, spare my life. Besides, the children have already been rescued. I...\"","\"Had they not been rescued, and anything happened to them, I would not only take your life but bury this entire sect with you!\" Guan Xilin roared, his broadsword flashing as he lunged forward.","Seeing this, the Sect Master turned to flee, but his strength was no match for Guan Xilin's. He was seized almost instantly.","\"Ah! What are you doing? Don't do anything rash...\" the Sect Master cried out, his cold sweat dripping. He had lost all semblance of composure.","Guan Xilin gripped him by the shoulders, his voice chilling. \"I'll naturally waste you!\" With a swift motion, he destroyed the Sect Master's cultivation, then threw him to the ground.","\"Arghhhhh!\"","A harrowing scream echoed through the sect, reverberating across the courtyard. Every resident, from disciples to elders, heard the Sect Master's agonizing cry, but none dared to venture out. They remained hidden, hoping the terrifying figure would depart quickly.","Having lost his cultivation, the Sect Master aged rapidly as he hit the ground. Blood spilled from his mouth, his body convulsing briefly before he fell still.","Guan Xilin looked on coldly, his gaze sweeping across the sect. His authoritative voice, amplified by his power, resonated through every corner. \"From this day forth! This sect is no more! Disperse, or I will return and raze this place!\"","Having delivered his ultimatum, he turned and soared into the sky.","He had received news at the Pan family that the children were on Floating Fate Island. After finally locating the island, he learned they had traveled to this realm. He had rushed here, only to find he was too late.","He was grateful, however, that the children had been rescued by kind individuals. Otherwise, he could not imagine the devastating news he would have received.","From the disciple, he learned that two individuals had taken the children: one wearing a Ghost Faced Mask, and the other a man in white with an ethereal aura. He had no idea who these two people were.","Generate Audio Overview"]},{"number":4624,"title":"Chapter 4624: News","paragraphs":["It seemed that for the time being, Guan Xilin needed to return and inform Feng Jiu and the others, including Wanyan Qianhua, hoping they could identify the two mysterious rescuers.","Meanwhile, in another realm, Feng Jiu, deep in meditation within a hotel room, abruptly opened her eyes, as if sensing a significant event. She retrieved the message jade from her spatial storage.","\"Could this be news of the children?\" she wondered, a surge of hope filling her as she saw her brother's name.","Simultaneously, Wanyan Qianhua and the others received Guan Xilin's message. Overjoyed by the news, they swiftly departed for the Feng family ancestral home.","Guan Xilin, after leaving the martial sect, had decided to return to the Feng family and had sent them a message. He reasoned that if the children were rescued by anyone they knew, they would likely be taken to the Feng family's ancestral home. Although Feng Jiu and her companions had numerous residences across various celestial realms, the Feng family's ancestral home in the Phoenix Empire remained a constant, always inhabited by Feng family members.","Moreover, with Old Patriarch Feng and Feng Xiao residing at the ancestral home, it was the ideal location for the children to be taken, provided their rescuers were willing to bring them there.","Feng Jiu pondered the information her brother had provided. A masked man? And a man in white with an ethereal aura?","Her mind immediately turned to Yi Xiuyan, but she dismissed the possibility. Based on her brother's description, the masked man possessed immense power, which Yi Xiuyan had yet to attain.","If it wasn't Yi Xiuyan, then who could it be?","And the man in white with an ethereal aura? If Mo Chen were still present, he would undoubtedly fit that description. However, Mo Chen was likely still on the mountain, unable to travel to rescue the children. If it wasn't Mo Chen, then who?","Her mind raced through a list of possibilities, but she couldn't pinpoint anyone. The limited information from her brother made it difficult to deduce their identities.","Nevertheless, she left her room, approached Leng Hua and Leng Shuang, who were guarding the door, and announced, \"I have news of the three children.\" With a wave of her hand, she created a vortex, transporting them to another realm. \"I need to return to the Feng family ancestral home immediately. You can follow later,\" she instructed.","As she spoke, she retrieved a teleportation axis, capable of instant travel, and departed. She could reach the Feng ancestral home much faster alone, but they could catch up within half a month.","Leng Shuang and Leng Hua, surprised by their master's sudden departure, exchanged glances. \"We should hurry as well,\" they said, retrieving their own teleportation axes and following as quickly as possible.","At the Feng family ancestral home, Feng Sanyuan paced the courtyard, his brow furrowed. He saw Feng Xiao approaching with a joyful expression and eagerly inquired, \"Is there news of the children? Where are they? Are they alright? Did Little Feng find them?\""]},{"number":4625,"title":"Chapter 4625: Feng Jiu Arrives","paragraphs":["\"Father, I just received news from Xilin! The three children have been found! Two people rescued them and are bringing them here,\" Feng Xiao said, his face alight with excitement.","\"That's wonderful, wonderful!\" Feng Sanyuan exclaimed. After a moment later, he sighed. \"After all this time, we finally have news. Are the children alright? How are they doing? Did Xilin mention anything else?\"","\"All three children are fine, but they've been out there without adults. I imagine they've suffered a great deal.\"","Hearing this, Feng Sanyuan sighed again. \"As long as they return safely, that's all that matters. Nothing is more important than their safety. Once they're back, we can finally put our minds at ease.\"","\"Quickly, go tell Wanrou and the others. I'll wait at the city gate,\" Feng Sanyuan said, unable to stay still after hearing the news. He immediately headed outside with large strides.","\"Father, they'll come here when they arrive. You might miss them at the city gate. Besides, we don't know how long it will take them to get here. I think we should wait at home,\" Feng Xiao said, stopping him.","Feng Sanyuan paused, considering this. \"You're right. Very well. Has the courtyard where they'll be staying been tidied up? Tell the caretaker to let us know as soon as they arrive.\"","\"Yes, yes, I'll tell them,\" Feng Xiao said, turning to leave. Just then, they felt a fluctuation of spirit energy in the air. A flash of light appeared, and Feng Jiu, who had been gone for so long, stood before them.","\"Little Feng!\"","\"Little Nine!\"","Feng Sanyuan and Feng Xiao exclaimed in surprise, rushing to her side. \"Why are you back so soon? We just received news from Xilin, and we thought you wouldn't be here for a few more days.\"","\"Little Feng, you've lost so much weight! Have you not been eating properly?\" Feng Sanyuan looked at her, his heart aching. She was much thinner than he remembered.","He had always cherished his granddaughter, and knowing she had suffered outside, unable to help her for years, seeing her return so thin filled him with distress.","Feng Jiu smiled, a hint of weariness in her expression. \"I'm fine. I just haven't had much of an appetite lately.\"","\"Then you should go home and rest. We'll let you know as soon as the children arrive. Once you're home, you don't need to do anything. Your family will take care of everything. Just rest!\" Feng Xiao said, noticing her exhaustion. He decided he would ask Wan Rou to prepare something light for her to eat.","Feng Jiu listened and nodded. \"Very well. I'll see Grandmother and Mother, then rest in the courtyard. Leng Hua and Leng Shuang should arrive later. I'm the only one who came back this time.\"","\"What about Mo Ze? Why didn't he come with you?\" Feng Sanyuan asked, surprised.","Feng Jiu's smile faded slightly. \"He probably won't be back for a while.\"","Feng Sanyuan and Feng Xiao were surprised, but since she didn't elaborate, they didn't press her. Feng Sanyuan simply said, \"Feng Xiao, go with Little Feng!\""]},{"number":4626,"title":"Chapter 4626: Home at last","paragraphs":["\"Mm, alright.\"","Feng Xiao replied, then turned to Feng Jiu. \"Let's go. I'll accompany you to see your Mother and Grandmother. They've been missing you terribly, and they'll be overjoyed to see you back. Oh, and I haven't told them the news about the children Xilin sent. They'll be happy to hear that too.\"","\"Mm hmm,\" Feng Jiu responded softly, and followed him.","As they watched them leave, Feng Sanyuan paced the courtyard, his brow furrowed in thought. Had something happened to Mo Ze? He couldn't help but recall the thunderous tribulation from some time ago, and Xilin's hasty departure then.","However, no one had explained what had transpired. They had initially assumed it was unrelated, but now, they feared otherwise...","It seemed they would need to question Xilin and the others thoroughly upon their return.","Three days later, at dusk, at the city gate.","Murong Yixuan gazed at the familiar yet foreign landscape, a sense of sadness washing over him.","This place held too many memories, both cherished and painful. He never imagined he would ever return.","\"Your servant greets the three young Masters!\"","The Feng Guards, who had been awaiting their arrival, emerged as soon as they recognized the three Young Masters. Some quickly rushed back to deliver the news.","Murong Yixuan's eyes flickered as he regarded the guards. \"Are you the Feng Guards?\" He focused on the Feng Tokens at their waists.","\"Yes.\" The two Feng Guards recognized him as well, and were surprised to see that he had escorted their Young Masters. They bowed in gratitude. \"Thank you, Young Master Murong, for bringing our Young Masters home.\"","\"Your Old Patriarch and Master are at home, correct? After escorting them back, please inform Feng Jiu to return as soon as possible.\" As he spoke, he glanced at the silent Ghost Faced Masked Man beside him.","The Feng Guards followed his gaze. They had noticed the man earlier, carrying their young lady with such care and affection. They had assumed he was a friend of their Master. But Murong Yixuan's words made them wary.","One of the Feng Guards replied, \"Our Patriarch returned several days ago and is waiting for the Young Masters at the manor.\" His gaze swept over Seventeen, observing him curiously.","\"Young Master Murong, this Master, please come with us to the manor!\" The Fengwei guard gestured politely.","Hearing that Feng Jiu was at the Feng Manor, Murong Yixuan felt a wave of relief. He told the Feng Guards, \"Now that the children are here and your Patriarch is at the manor, I have other matters to attend to. I won't be joining you. Please convey my regards to Feng Jiu and your Old Patriarch. I must take my leave.\"","He then looked at the three children and said gently, \"Listen to your Mother when you return. You'll be safest by her side. I'll be going now.\" He smiled and patted Muchen's head.","Hao'er, Muchen, and Muyue exchanged glances as he turned to leave. Hao'er and Muchen called out in unison, \"Uncle Murong, thank you.\""]},{"number":4627,"title":"Chapter 4627: Meeting Feng Jiu","paragraphs":["\"Uncle Murong, thank you! Come and visit Yue'er in the future!\" Yue'er chimed in with her sweet and childish voice.","Murong Yixuan paused briefly, but didn't turn around. He simply waved and continued walking. As his figure receded, he disappeared from their sight.","\"Yue'er! Hao'er, Chen'er!\"","A familiar voice, filled with surprise, reached the children's ears. Hearing it, they spun around and saw a figure in red rushing towards them.","\"Mother!\"","They cried out in unison. Hao'er and Mu Chen were the first to dash towards her, while Yue'er, held by the Ghost Faced Masked Man, struggled and shouted, \"Put me down, put me down! I want my mother!\"","The Ghost Faced Masked Man hesitated, then gently set her down. As soon as her feet touched the ground, she sprinted towards Feng Jiu with her tiny legs.","\"Mother!\"","The three children threw themselves into Feng Jiu's arms, their small hands clinging to her tightly as they called out to her repeatedly.","\"My children, you've finally returned.\"","Feng Jiu's heart overflowed with emotion, her voice trembling, on the verge of tears. She held them close, finally feeling the tangible reality of their presence. The worry that had weighed on her lifted as she held them safely in her embrace.","\"Mother, Hao'er missed you so much. Mother, Hao'er took care of his younger siblings,\" Hao'er said, his usually composed face softening with childlike affection.","Feng Jiu nodded, stroking his head. \"Mother knows, Mother knows my Hao'er has always been a good brother. I knew you would take care of your younger siblings while I was away.\" She spoke tenderly, embracing him and kissing his forehead.","Hao'er beamed, his face lighting up with the joy of a child praised by their mother.","\"Mother, Mother, Yue'er wants a kiss too!\" Yue'er piped up, pushing her rosy cheek forward. \"Yue'er wants Mother to kiss her face.\"","Mu Chen, a little shy, saw his mother kiss his older brother and his younger sister offer her cheek. He then quietly said, \"Mother, Mu Chen wants one too.\"","Feng Jiu smiled, affectionately patting their hair. \"Of course, of course. You are all Mother's little treasures, and Mother will kiss each one of you.\" She kissed their cheeks, her own smile mirroring their happiness.","After embracing her children, Feng Jiu stood up. She looked at the Ghost Faced Masked Man and the guard standing beside him.","\"I wonder who you are?\" she asked, her clear eyes flashing with a dark light as she studied the Ghost Faced Masked Man. She was inwardly astonished.","How was it that she couldn't perceive his strength with her cultivation? Was he concealing it, or was his power truly beyond measure?","\"I am their rescuer,\" the Ghost Faced Masked Man replied, his gaze shifting to Yue'er. \"And also, the little girl's Master.\""]},{"number":4628,"title":"Chapter 4628: Query","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu's eyebrows lifted slightly upon hearing this, and she gave him a thoughtful look. Without further comment, she gestured invitingly and said, \"You must be tired from escorting them all this way. Please, come to my house and rest for a while.\"","The Ghost Faced Masked Man nodded. \"That's agreeable. I also wish to discuss Yue'er's apprenticeship with you.\" He then stepped forward.","\"Mother, he is Seventeen, the escort the Pan family gave us,\" Yue'er whispered, wrapping her arms around Feng Jiu's neck. \"Mother, this masked man is very strange. He keeps telling me to call him Master, but he saved Yue'er from the bad guys, so he must be a good person. Also, Mother, there was an Uncle Murong who brought us back, but he left after dropping us off at the city gate.\"","\"Uncle Murong?\" Feng Jiu was momentarily surprised. After a moment's thought, she asked, \"Is that Murong Yixuan?\" Her brother had mentioned two people bringing back the children: one masked, the other clad in ethereal white.","However, the last time she saw Murong Yixuan, he was travel-worn and not wearing white. She had puzzled over the identities of those two people.","Seeing the masked man today, whose strength was unfathomable, and knowing that the other person was Murong Yixuan, who had already departed, clarified the situation.","\"It's Uncle Murong,\" Hao'er confirmed, looking at her. \"I don't think he wanted to enter the city. He stood at the gate, gazing into the city, and then said he had to leave. He left shortly before Mother arrived.\"","Feng Jiu nodded. \"I understand. I will thank him personally when I see him again.\"","\"Mother, where is Father? Why didn't he come?\" Yue'er asked, looking around.","Feng Jiu smiled softly at her daughter. \"Your father is in seclusion. He's not here.\"","With Yue'er in her arms, followed by Hao'er and Muchen, Feng Jiu entered Feng Manor. She first directed someone to show the masked man to his room, then took the children to the backyard.","\"Little Feng, who is that masked man? He seems very strange,\" Feng Sanyuan said, a hint of unease in his voice. He had noticed the man's unwavering gaze on Yue'er, as if he feared they would take her away.","Feng Jiu smiled. \"He saved the children. I'm not sure of his identity, but he claims to be Yue'er's master and wishes to take her as his disciple.\"","\"Yue'er is too young for a master. Besides, who could teach her better than you?\" Feng Xiao frowned, troubled by the man's unknown origins.","\"We'll discuss that later,\" Feng Jiu said, looking at the children in the courtyard. She scanned them with her spiritual awareness and noted that the blood curse remained in Muchen and Muyue, but had vanished from Hao'er. This revelation stirred her heart.","\"Hao'er, tell Mother everything that happened.\""]},{"number":4629,"title":"Chapter 4629: Strange Uncle","paragraphs":["\"Mother, after the blood demon sent us away, we landed in a forest in the mortal realm. I think it's because I wasn't born to my parents that the blood curse was broken in me that night. But I couldn't break it in my younger brother and sister, and they couldn't remember their parents either,\" Hao'er recounted, detailing their experiences in the world without adult supervision.","\"Big Brother was in a lot of pain. He kept screaming and sweating. We were scared, but we took care of Big Brother,\" Yue'er added.","Feng Jiu's heart ached. \"It's Mother's fault. Mother didn't take care of you.\"","\"No, Mother is very good. We love Mother the most,\" the three children said in unison, their eyes filled with love.","A tender smile appeared on Feng Jiu's face. She sat beside them, lifted Yue'er onto her lap, and said to Hao'er, \"Hao'er, please continue.\"","\"Well, because my strength hadn't fully recovered, I was afraid I couldn't protect my younger siblings if we encountered danger. So, we stayed in the forest for a few days before leaving. Later, when we reached the city, my younger siblings were almost abducted and sold. That's when I met Pan Ning...\"","He recounted every detail of their past two years, and as he spoke, darkness fell.","\"At that time, the Old Mountain Demon grabbed sister and threw her to the ground. The masked man suddenly appeared and caught her, saving her. But he wouldn't tell us his name. Later, Uncle Murong arrived, and they brought us back.\" Hao'er paused, looking at his mother.","Feng Jiu's heart clenched when she heard about the danger at the martial arts school. Her murderous intent flared. Such a respectable school, yet they abandoned the children in danger—unforgivable!","However, hearing that the masked man saved them eased her anxiety. They had turned disaster into fortune; otherwise, she couldn't imagine what might have happened.","\"Mother, that strange masked man is weird, but he's really good to Yue'er!\" Yue'er's soft voice broke through her thoughts. Afraid her mother would think the man was bad, she explained, \"If he hadn't saved Yue'er, she wouldn't be able to see you now. Besides, he was really nice to Yue'er on the way here. He's not a bad person.\"","Feng Jiu smiled and pinched her rosy cheek. \"Mother knows. If it weren't for him, Mother wouldn't see Little Yue'er now. Mother will thank him properly.\"","\"But, Mother, what if the strange uncle wants Yue'er to be his disciple?\" Yue'er asked, biting her lip, a little overwhelmed.","Feng Jiu smiled. \"Does Yue'er want him to be your Master?\"","The little girl blinked, her delicate face confused. She looked down, playing with her finger, and said softly, \"Yue'er doesn't want to leave Mother. Yue'er wants to be with Mother, but that strange uncle looks so pitiful.\""]},{"number":4630,"title":"Chapter 4630: Nine-Precious Fruit","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Feng Jiu was taken aback, then asked with a wry smile, \"Why does Yue'er say he's pitiful?\"","Yue'er looked up at her mother, her innocent eyes blinking. \"Because I don't talk to him much, so he just sits there quietly. He doesn't talk to anyone else either. And he often stares into space, like he's thinking about something.\"","She continued, \"But when Yue'er talks to him, he's very happy. He smiles, and he lets me call him Master. He also gives Yue'er delicious fruit to eat. Mother, Yue'er secretly saved it for you, even though Big Brother and Little Brother don't get any. They're for you to eat.\" Like a cunning little fox, she pulled the fruit she had hidden from her space and presented it to her mother as if it were a treasure.","\"This is... a Nine-Precious Fruit?\"","Feng Jiu stared at the spirit fruit in shock. It was an orange-red fruit, the size of an adult's fist, shaped like a budding flower. The fruit's shape was formed by nine segments of flesh, and its tip was a vibrant red. It emitted a faintly alluring and refreshing fragrance. Just smelling it made one feel invigorated, as if bathed in gentle spirit energy.","Feng Sanyuan, Feng Xiao, and the others looked at the fruit with surprise. They had seen many precious spirit fruits, but none like this. However, \"Nine-Precious Fruit\"? From Feng Jiu's reaction, it seemed exceptionally rare.","\"Mother, what is the Nine-Precious Fruit?\" Yue'er asked curiously, blinking her beautiful eyes.","Feng Jiu smiled and shook her head. \"Yue'er, it seems this 'strange uncle' is quite something. I've only seen Nine-Precious Fruits in books; I never imagined...\"","\"Mother, Yue'er ate two on the way!\" She held up her chubby little finger, beaming with pride. \"This is the third fruit, but Yue'er didn't want to eat it, so she hid it before the 'strange uncle' saw. He doesn't know!\"","\"Little Nine, is this fruit precious? What does it do? Can Yue'er eat two of them and her body handle it?\" Feng Xiao asked.","Feng Jiu chuckled. \"This fruit is extraordinary. It's considered the ultimate immortal fruit. If a mortal smells it, their lifespan increases by a hundred years. If they take a bite, even a mortal without a spiritual root can enter the world of cultivation. And if a cultivator eats it, their lifespan increases by a thousand years, and their spirit energy becomes more abundant and pure.\"","Seeing their astonished expressions, Feng Jiu continued, \"Not only that, but if a dying person eats it, they can be revived and their strength restored to its peak. According to the books, it takes 9,000 years to grow, 900 years to bloom, 900 years to bear fruit, and another 900 years to ripen. That's why it's called the Nine-Precious Fruit. It's a fairy fruit, not a spiritual fruit, and is incredibly precious.\"","Yue'er's eyes widened, and she stretched out her little finger to count. \"Yue'er ate two! One is a thousand years, and two are two thousand years.\" Then, looking worried, she asked, \"Mother, will Yue'er still grow? Will she stay small forever and be two thousand years old?\""]},{"number":4631,"title":"Chapter 4631: Don’t be negligent","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu chuckled lightly, pinched her little face, and said, \"You'll grow up, don't worry! Yue'er will grow into a beautiful young lady.\"","\"Yue'er will be as beautiful as Mother,\" she replied with a smile, her eyes curving like crescent moons.","\"Mother, the Pan family was kind to us. When we left, we promised to ask you to heal Young Master Pan's legs so he can stand again,\" Hao'er said, his gaze fixed on her.","Feng Jiu smiled. \"Alright, Mother knows. We'll visit him again soon.\"","Hao'er smiled and nodded, then fell silent.","\"Chen'er, how is your health?\" Feng Jiu asked, looking at her quiet son, and stroking his head. \"Are you alright?\"","\"Mmh, I'm fine, Mother, don't worry,\" Mu Chen replied, pausing before continuing, \"It's just that the blood curse isn't completely gone, but the symptoms we had earlier have disappeared recently.\" He hesitated before asking, \"Mother, is Father alright?\"","They had suspected that their physical condition was related to their parents'. They saw their mother today and she seemed fine, but they hadn't seen their father. They feared something had happened to him, but their mother hadn't said anything.","Feng Jiu's eyes flickered, and her smile faded slightly.","\"Mother, did something happen to Father?\" Yue'er asked, her eyes filled with worry.","Feng Sanyuan and the others exchanged glances, then looked at Feng Jiu. They had been unsure a few days ago, but after the children's questions, they had a general idea of Mo Ze's situation. Now that the children had asked, should they tell them?","\"You must be tired from your journey. It's late, so go have a hot bath and rest. I'll tell you about your father another time,\" Feng Jiu said softly, smiling at the children.","The children nodded and didn't press further.","\"I'll take them!\" Wanrong said, stepping forward to take Hao'er and the others by the hand. \"I'll take them back to their rooms. You come over later! Spend some time with them.\"","\"Alright, I will,\" Feng Jiu replied, watching them leave. Then, her smile faded, and a hint of weariness appeared. She rubbed her brow gently.","\"Little Feng, aren't you going to tell the children about Mo Ze?\" Feng Sanyuan asked, seeing her tired face and sighing lightly.","\"In a few days! I'll find a good time,\" Feng Jiu replied, standing up. \"The man is in the guest room in the west courtyard, right?\"","\"Yes, the guest room in the west courtyard,\" Feng Xiao confirmed.","She nodded. \"Alright, I'll go see him and find out where he's from.\"","\"It's getting late. Why not go in the morning? He might be resting,\" Feng Xiao suggested.","Feng Jiu looked at the sky, paused, and said, \"You're right. Then I'll go back to my courtyard. Tell the people in the west courtyard to take good care of him.\" She looked at the Nine-Precious Fruit on the table and stored it in her space."]},{"number":4632,"title":"Chapter 4632: Meet","paragraphs":["The next morning, before the children awoke, Feng Jiu rose early. After preparing herself, she went to the guest room in the western courtyard. Upon arrival, she found the masked man seated in the courtyard. Seeing her, he gestured to the seat opposite him and said, \"Sit.\"","Feng Jiu glanced at him, then walked over. She bowed slightly and said, \"Thank you for saving my child.\"","\"You wish to thank me?\" He asked, looking at her.","Feng Jiu's eyes flickered, and she smiled, taking the seat. \"What kind of thanks do you require? If it's within my power, I will not refuse.\"","\"I want your daughter as my apprentice,\" the masked man stated.","Feng Jiu remained composed. \"I still don't know who you are.\"","\"If I tell you, will you agree?\" His voice rose slightly, with a hint of disapproval.","Feng Jiu didn't answer directly. \"I don't believe we've met before, but I can see your strength is unfathomable, and you possess the Nine-Precious Immortal Fruit. It's clear you come from an extraordinary background. If so, why do you desire my daughter as your disciple?\"","She paused, looking at him. \"If we're speaking of talent, she may be exceptional, but she's not unique. Therefore, I don't understand your determination to have her as your disciple.\"","The masked man glanced at her. \"Does one need a reason to find her pleasing?\"","Feng Jiu frowned slightly, about to speak, when he continued.","\"I saved her life. If not for me, she would be dead. Therefore, from the moment I saved her, her life is almost mine. Now, I want her as my disciple, and I see nothing wrong with that.\" His voice was cold and firm.","\"Your Excellency saved Yue'er. I am grateful, but I can repay you in other ways. Yue'er is my child, not an object. She has her own opinions and thoughts. If she wishes to be your disciple, I won't stop her. If she doesn't, then no matter what you say, I won't agree.\"","Her voice trailed off, and she smiled at the man, whose aura had cooled. \"Your Excellency likely knows who I am. Even if we haven't met, you've heard my name. If you wish to fight me, I will oblige.\"","The masked man narrowed his eyes, seemingly displeased. \"I don't wish to be your enemy. I simply want a disciple.\"","Feng Jiu glanced at him. \"The disciple you desire is my child.\"","\"So, what will it take for you to agree?\" he asked calmly.","\"I said earlier: if Yue'er agrees, I won't stop you. However, even if she does, you must reveal your true face and tell me your real name and origin. Only then can I allow my daughter to leave with you. Otherwise...\"","\"Otherwise?\" he asked, snorting. \"Otherwise, you still wish to challenge me?\"","\"That's unnecessary.\" Feng Jiu smiled lightly, her gaze scrutinizing him. \"I'm merely curious about your abilities that qualify you to be my daughter's master.\""]},{"number":4633,"title":"Chapter 4633: Taking Off the Mask","paragraphs":["Hearing this, the masked man turned his gaze towards Feng Jiu, offering no further words but instead seeming to scrutinize her intently. After a prolonged silence, he finally spoke, his tone carrying a note of certainty. \"The little girl can only grow up safely if she is under my guidance. Your current circumstances prevent you from providing her with the necessary protection, especially with your husband, Xuanyuan Mo Ze, still missing. Do you truly believe she will be safe if you keep her by your side?\"","As he continued, the masked man's voice softened subtly. He rose to his feet, his gaze not meeting Feng Jiu's slightly shifting expression, and began to pace slowly across the courtyard, his hands clasped behind his back. Abruptly, he halted his movement, his eyes lifting to the sky as he addressed Feng Jiu once more. \"The intricacies of this world far surpass your current understanding. Consider this: with your level of cultivation, why are you still unable to control life and death?\"","Upon finishing his statement, his gaze returned to Feng Jiu, observing the slight furrow in her brow and the unwavering focus of her eyes upon him. A faint smile, devoid of genuine warmth, touched the corners of his lips. \"You have matured at an accelerated pace, so much so that your very existence poses a threat to certain powerful entities. Before you reach a level of power capable of shaking the foundations of the heavens and earth, they will undoubtedly seek to eliminate you, and they will not hesitate to harm your children in the process.\"","Feng Jiu's outward composure remained unbroken, yet within her, a storm of contemplation brewed. His words were laden with significant implications, prompting deep thought. Including the late Old Man Tianji, this was the second individual to impart such cryptic warnings to her. However, these pronouncements remained frustratingly vague, touching upon realms she had yet to encounter or comprehend.","\"You suggest that our existence poses a threat to certain powerful beings?\" Feng Jiu inquired, her gaze steady. She paused momentarily before continuing, \"What manner of beings are these powerful entities you speak of? We have resided in this world for a considerable time and have never encountered such beings. They are not present here.\"","\"Indeed, they are not here,\" the masked man affirmed, his eyes fixed on hers. \"Those who have ascended to higher realms cannot return to this one. Had they been here, you would not have survived for this long.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu's brow furrowed further, her gaze intensifying with suspicion. A note of caution laced her voice as she pressed him for answers. \"Then who are you? How do you possess this knowledge? And why do you desire to take my daughter as your disciple? What is your true purpose?\"","The masked man met her gaze directly, then abruptly reached up and removed the mask concealing his face, revealing the visage beneath.","It was a face marred by severe burns, rendering it unrecognizable and undeniably unsettling. Yet, having shed the mask, the man regarded Feng Jiu with a calm and indifferent expression, as if the disfigured face was merely an inconsequential detail. His following words validated this impression.","\"This face is somewhat unsightly, hence my use of a mask to avoid startling people, particularly the young girl who has caught my attention.\" Holding the mask in his hand, he slowly approached and seated himself opposite Feng Jiu. He placed the mask on the table and with a wave of his hand, a stream of air enveloped the courtyard, creating an apparent seal.","Feng Jiu's eyes flickered towards the seemingly sealed space, a glint of understanding in their depths.","\"To prevent those old codgers from eavesdropping,\" he explained matter-of-factly. \"I, too, originate from the higher realms, but I am unable to descend in my true form, thus I am utilizing this temporary vessel. Your two children were not originally destined to live, and had you not contracted an ancient Super Sacred Beast to illuminate their fate stars, they would not have survived until this point. However, even with this intervention, they will face numerous perils as they mature.\""]},{"number":4634,"title":"Chapter 4634: Origin","paragraphs":["His voice trailed off, and a faint sigh of regret accompanied his next words. \"While I was in secluded cultivation, my disciple suffered a devastating calamity and perished, her soul scattered across the vast expanse of the heavens and earth, lost to the cycle of rebirth. Because she was an anomaly, existing outside the conventional order of this world, I believed her essence would drift endlessly until its final dissipation. However, due to your own unique nature as an anomaly, our destinies became intertwined. Through a stroke of extraordinary fortune and accumulated good karma, she was granted a sliver of life and was reborn as your daughter. Upon discovering this, I sought to find a suitable vessel in the lower realm to facilitate her return.\"","Hearing this revelation, Feng Jiu was visibly taken aback. \"Are you saying that my daughter was your disciple in a previous life?\" she asked, her tone laced with clear disbelief. \"How could that possibly be?\"","The man cast a brief glance in her direction and stated slowly, \"She was indeed my disciple. Whether you choose to believe it or not is your prerogative; I have no need to deceive you in order to take her away.\"","Feng Jiu fixed her gaze upon him, her attention drawn to his eyes. She detected a fleeting hint of irritation, as if he were slightly vexed by her doubt, yet there was no trace of evasion or alarm in his expression, only a profound seriousness and depth.","Silence descended between them for a moment before Feng Jiu finally spoke, her voice carrying a note of concern. \"If you take her away, can you truly protect her and ensure her safe upbringing? Can you guarantee that she will never again face such peril?\"","\"You have no need for such worries. I possess the ability to protect her.\" He replied, exuding confidence.","\"Even if these so-called powerful beings you mentioned seek to end her life, you can protect her?\" Feng Jiu pressed, her gaze unwavering.","\"Before she reaches maturity, I will not allow those ancient fools to discover her lineage. Should they one day uncover the truth, I will exert every ounce of my being to shield her,\" he declared, his voice calm yet resolute, his eyes meeting Feng Jiu's without hesitation.","Witnessing his unwavering conviction, Feng Jiu conceded, \"Very well, I agree to let you take Yue'er away, but not immediately.\" She looked at him directly. \"She has only recently returned to me, and the blood curse afflicting her has not yet been fully eradicated. At least for the present, I cannot bear to part with her.\"","\"My stay here is limited to another half a year. After that, I must return. As for the little girl's blood curse, I can assist in breaking it once I have her with me.\" He added.","Hearing the remaining time he had, Feng Jiu pursed her lips thoughtfully. Then, upon learning of his ability to break the blood curse, she nodded. \"I understand.\" She rose to her feet, paused briefly, and then turned back to him. \"Who are you? You still haven't told me.\"","\"It is better that you remain unaware,\" he replied, shaking his head. He stood up, retrieved his mask, and placed it back over his face. \"There is no benefit in you knowing. Simply trust that I will not harm your daughter. If you fear that you will never see her again, rest assured that you will have the opportunity after your own ascension.\"","The mention of ascension caused Feng Jiu's eyes to flicker with interest, a stirring in her heart. \"Since you possess the means to take Yue'er with you, then take my son as well!\" She exclaimed. \"They are twins and share a deep bond. With Chen'er by her side, she will not be lonely.\"","Hearing this request, the man glanced at Feng Jiu, his hands still clasped behind his back. \"You are quite astute. You are not perhaps considering asking me to take your eldest son along as well, are you?\" He posed the question casually, but to his surprise, a smile bloomed on her face.","\"The thought did cross my mind,\" she admitted, \"but Hao'er has his own biological parents. I must first seek Hao'er's opinion and inform his parents, so...\""]},{"number":4635,"title":"Chapter 4635: Observation","paragraphs":["\"Do you think it's easy to just take someone up there?\" He snorted lightly, his gaze turned cold as he looked at her.","Seeing his reaction, Feng Jiu offered a disarming smile. \"Aren't you a powerful being from above? While others may be restricted from descending, you clearly possess the means to do so. That suggests a power beyond the ordinary. Besides,\" she continued, her tone persuasive, \"taking one person is no different than taking two. Surely it would pose no significant challenge for someone of your capabilities.\"","He remained silent for a moment, then with a dismissive wave of his hand, he dispelled the invisible barrier in the air. Simultaneously, he raised his hand and gently propelled Feng Jiu out of the courtyard.","Regaining her balance, a flicker of understanding ignited in Feng Jiu's eyes. She glanced back at the courtyard and observed the sudden formation of a new barrier, swirling currents of air rippling across its surface, gradually obscuring any view within.","Any lingering doubts she might have harbored vanished with this display of power. To effortlessly move someone of her cultivation level out of the courtyard was an undeniable testament to his strength.","With this realization, she chose not to linger and turned to depart. Although she had failed to uncover his true identity, she now possessed knowledge of his origins and the fact that his current physical form was not his own. As for the remaining mysteries, she had half a year to observe and assess.","If this enigmatic individual proved worthy of entrusting her three children to, she would need to begin making the necessary arrangements.","As for her adversaries...","Knowing the nature and the realm of existence of her enemies provided her with a crucial target for her future actions.","Over the subsequent two days, Feng Jiu dedicated her time to the three children, ensuring they received ample rest. She took them on outings throughout the city and spent a tranquil day with them at Peach Blossom Ridge.","It wasn't until the third day that Wanyan Qianhua and the others began to return. With the arrival of Guan Xilin, Du Fan, Leng Shuang, and the rest of their companions, the mansion buzzed with renewed energy and laughter.","That evening, after the celebratory banquet, Wanyan Qianhua drew Feng Jiu aside, her expression curious. \"Who is that masked man? There's something about him that feels...unusual.\"","Feng Jiu glanced towards the masked man, who was patiently assisting Yue'er with her meal. She smiled softly. \"Didn't I tell you? He is the children's savior. He wishes to take Yue'er as his disciple, and I intend to agree to his request.\"","\"You are already exceptionally skilled; why would you doubt your ability to teach three children?\" Wanyan Qianhua said, her tone laced with disapproval. \"Yue'er is still so young; how can you bear to let her go with someone who appeared out of nowhere?\" She paused, then added with concern, \"Besides, I find this man strange, and I cannot discern the depth of his cultivation. Are you certain about this decision?\"","\"Sister, let's discuss this later. Today, let's simply enjoy the reunion. I plan to take the three children to Black Tortoise Continent tomorrow so that Hao'er can finally meet his parents. The three children also incurred some debts of gratitude while they were stranded in the mortal realm, and I want to take them to repay those favors as well.\"","Feng Jiu sighed softly. \"You are also aware that Mo Ze is currently missing. I have no idea of his whereabouts. I don't know how to explain this to the three children. I also need to travel to Sky Mountain, so I likely won't be home for a long while.\"","Hearing this, Wanyan Qianhua also sighed, her initial disapproval softening. \"I understand. Since you have given so much thought, I won't press the matter further. You have a great many responsibilities to manage, so please do what you must. Don't worry about things here. Even if you are too occupied to return, we will make time to visit your grandfather, father, and mother. Moreover, your brother's residence is nearby, so he will undoubtedly oversee things should any issues arise.\""]},{"number":4636,"title":"Chapter 4636: Resentment","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu nodded in understanding. \"I know.\" With that simple acknowledgment, she took Wanyan Qianhua's hand and they returned to the lively table.","The following day, after bidding farewell to her family, Feng Jiu, accompanied by her three children, the ever-present masked man, Leng Hua, Leng Shuang, and Du Fan, set off towards the Black Tortoise Monarch's palace.","Aboard the airship, Hao'er's curiosity surfaced. \"Mother,\" he began, \"Seventeen went to the Phoenix Guard training camp. When we return to the mortal world, should we bring him along?\"","Since their return and the revelation of Seventeen's unwavering loyalty, their mother had arranged for him to join the prestigious Phoenix Guard training camp. Several days had passed since then, and they hadn't seen him, leaving them wondering about his current situation.","Feng Jiu, seated at the bow of the flying ship, was enjoying a cup of wine and conversing with the masked man. Hearing Hao'er's question, she turned with a gentle smile. \"Do you want to bring him with you?\"","Hao'er nodded eagerly. \"Yes, I want to take him back to have a look. He lived there for so many years, and all his friends are there. If we're going back anyway, let's take him!\"","\"Alright,\" Feng Jiu agreed readily. \"After we visit your parents, we'll pick him up and take him to the mortal world.\"","\"Mother, Mother, Yue'er has some very dear friends in the Pan family!\" Yue'er chimed in, leaning against her mother and speaking excitedly in her soft voice. \"There's Sister Xue'er, and there's also...\"","She nestled closer to Feng Jiu's chest, recounting the delightful times she had spent with the young masters and ladies of the Pan family.","The spaceship glided smoothly through the air. Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang stood, sat, or leaned against the sides, listening with smiles to Yue'er's sweet voice as she recounted one amusing anecdote after another with infectious enthusiasm. Before they knew it, time had slipped away unnoticed.","Within the Black Tortoise Palace, the Black Tortoise Monarch, having already received Feng Jiu's message, awaited their arrival in the main hall. Noticing that his wife had yet to join him, he addressed his attendants. \"Go and check on the lady and the young master again. Why haven't they arrived yet?\"","\"We're here.\" The Black Tortoise Mistress entered the hall, her young son by her side. She looked at the Black Tortoise Monarch, a hint of displeasure in her voice. \"They aren't here yet. Did you truly need to rush us over and over again?\" As she spoke, she led her young son forward, sat down beside her husband, and lifted the child onto her lap.","\"My lady, Feng Jiu is bringing Hao'er back today. They went through considerable difficulty to find our child and returned him to us personally. As the hosts and Hao'er's biological parents, we must ensure we are not rude or disrespectful,\" the Black Tortoise Monarch said gently, reaching out to take her hand.","\"They lost the child in the first place, so it's only natural that they found him,\" she retorted, a touch of bitterness in her tone. \"Besides, look at Hao'er. He has been constantly thinking about Feng Jiu and Xuanyuan Mo Ze, calling them Father and Mother. Anyone who didn't know would assume they were his real parents!\" A trace of resentment and unfairness were mixed in.","Hearing this, the Black Tortoise Monarch sighed softly. \"Why do you say such things? You know that Hao'er was lost when he was very young, and it was they who rescued him and raised him until he was five or six years old before we even knew where he was. It's only natural that he feels a distance from us. After all, he lived with them all that time, and they treated him with great kindness.\"","\"Yes, yes, I know,\" she conceded, her voice softening slightly. \"Hao'er is my son; how could I not love him? But this child has always been so reserved, like a piece of cold stone that cannot be warmed. As his mother, how can I not feel disheartened by this?\""]},{"number":4637,"title":"Chapter 4637: Meeting","paragraphs":["\"Alright, alright, say no more. It's pointless to dwell on it,\" the Black Tortoise Monarch said, gesturing for his wife to cease her complaints.","Before long, a guard entered the hall and reported respectfully, \"Your Majesty, the airship has landed outside the Palace.\"","Upon hearing this, the Black Tortoise Monarch swiftly rose to his feet. \"They're here,\" he announced to his wife. \"Let us go and welcome them.\"","Seeing his eagerness, the Black Tortoise Mistress stood up, her youngest son still cradled in her arms. A faint, polite smile graced her lips as she silently followed him out of the hall.","The airship gently descended, and Feng Jiu and her companions disembarked. Yue'er, in particular, was bubbling with excitement at being in a new and grand place. Upon learning that this was the palace where her Big Brother's biological parents resided, she exclaimed in wide-eyed surprise, \"Big Brother, it's so big and beautiful here!\"","Hao'er offered her a gentle smile. \"Big Brother will show you around in a little while.\"","\"Yeah!\" The two children jumped up in unison. Their attention then shifted to a group of people approaching them. At the forefront was a regal couple holding a young child, who appeared to be just a few months younger than themselves.","\"Ghost Doctor, you have finally arrived.\" The Black Tortoise Monarch said warmly as he approached Feng Jiu. He offered her a respectful bow, then turned his gaze to Hao'er, his eyes filled with relief and emotion. \"Hao'er, it warms our hearts to see you back safe and sound. We can finally rest assured.\"","\"Hao'er, come here and let your mother see you,\" the Black Tortoise Mistress said softly, putting down her younger son and opening her arms invitingly.","Seeing this gesture, Hao'er stepped forward and bowed respectfully to them. \"Your son greets his father and mother.\" After the customary greeting, he walked towards his biological mother.","\"Son, you must have suffered greatly while you were away! Mother told you not to venture out and to stay safely at home, but you disobeyed and went anyway. Look at all the hardships you have endured. Fortunately, you have returned safely, otherwise...\" She took his hand and began to speak with fervent concern. Hearing her words, the Black Tortoise Monarch felt a pang of awkwardness and quickly interjected.","\"Enough, enough. Hao'er is back now; why are you still dwelling on the past?\" the Black Tortoise Monarch chided her gently, then turned apologetically to Feng Jiu. \"Ghost Doctor, please do not take her words to heart. She meant no offense; she was simply overcome with worry for her son.\"","Feng Jiu smiled understandingly. \"It is quite alright. I have brought two other children back with Hao'er this time, so I am afraid we will be imposing on the Black Tortoise Monarch's hospitality for a few days.\"","\"Hahahaha, Ghost Doctor, what are you saying?\" The Black Tortoise Monarch chuckled heartily. \"We are absolutely delighted to have you stay here. Moreover, the children are all of similar ages and can play together. By the way, you haven't yet met my youngest son, have you?\" He smiled warmly as he looked at his youngest child standing beside him, his eyes brimming with affection.","Feng Jiu turned her gaze to the young boy, who appeared to be around the same age as Yue'er and Muchen, though perhaps a few months younger upon closer inspection. He was remarkably handsome, bearing a strong resemblance to his mother.","At that moment, the little boy was holding the Black Tortoise Mistress' hand with one of his own, while gently gnawing on the fingers of her other hand. His pair of curious eyes were fixed on Muchen and Muyue, as if pondering the reason for their identical appearance.","Feng Jiu smiled warmly. \"Du Fan mentioned during his last visit that the Young Master is exceptionally intelligent. Today, he looks remarkably handsome.\"","Hearing this praise, the Black Tortoise Monarch and his lady beamed with pleasure. After all, compliments regarding one's children were always well-received."]},{"number":4638,"title":"Chapter 4638: Getting along","paragraphs":["Chapter 4638: Getting along","The group entered the grand hall, where they engaged in pleasant conversation for a while, each enjoying a couple of cups of fragrant tea. After a comfortable interlude, the Black Tortoise Monarch addressed Feng Jiu and the others. “I have arranged for a courtyard to be prepared for your rest. You are welcome to stay here for a few days, allowing the children ample time to play together.”","As he spoke, his gaze rested on Feng Jiu, a warm smile gracing his lips. “Ghost Doctor, it is a rare occasion for you to visit, and I happen to have a matter I wish to discuss with you privately. Would you please join me in my study?”","Without hesitation, Feng Jiu replied, “Certainly.”","Turning to his wife, the Black Tortoise Monarch said, “Why don’t you take the children to explore the grounds and enjoy themselves? It has been a long time since we have had such a lively atmosphere here.”","“I will,” the Black Tortoise Mistress responded with a gentle nod. Taking her youngest son by the hand, she addressed Hao’er, Muchen, Muyue, and their companions. “Let’s take a stroll through the gardens! When you grow weary, we can return here to rest. I have already instructed the kitchen to prepare some of the children’s favorite snacks and have them brought to the garden.”","“Go on ahead!” Feng Jiu gestured for the children to follow the Black Tortoise Mistress.","Seeing this, Du Fan also rose to his feet with a smile. “I had the pleasure of visiting once before, but I didn’t have the opportunity to truly appreciate the unique flowers and plants in your garden. I must take a closer look this time.”","“I will gladly show you around. This way, please,” Lady Black Tortoise said with a gracious smile, gesturing for them to follow as she led the group outside.","Once they had departed, the Black Tortoise Monarch also stood up and gestured towards his study. “Ghost Doctor, please.”","Feng Jiu nodded and followed him. Her primary purpose for this visit was to return Hao’er to his biological parents. However, she also harbored a secondary intention: if they were agreeable, she wished to entrust Hao’er to the masked man, hoping he could guide the boy towards a reputable Sect or a powerful mentor for proper cultivation.","Yet, she remained uncertain about their willingness to part with Hao’er, nor was she entirely sure if her idea was too self-serving. Thus, she planned to use her time here to observe the Black Tortoise Monarch and his wife’s interactions with Hao’er, hoping to gauge their feelings and determine if they might consider allowing him to leave.","Meanwhile, the Black Tortoise Mistress led the children and Du Fan into the vibrant gardens, offering them an introduction. “The flowers in this garden are all rare specimens and precious herbs collected from various corners of the world. They are not merely for aesthetic pleasure; the majority of them also possess medicinal properties.”","“Herbs? How fascinating!” Yue’er’s soft voice was filled with genuine surprise, her small face radiating joy. “Yue’er is currently learning about herbs, so in the future, I will know many herbs and will also know what these medicinal flowers are used for~”","“Yue’er is so clever. In the future, she will undoubtedly become like Mother, a highly skilled alchemist and Pharmacist,” Hao’er said, looking at his younger sister, a rare, gentle smile softening his usually serious features.","Hearing his words, the Black Tortoise Mistress glanced at him. The tender expression on his face and his reference to Feng Jiu as “Mother” caused the smile on her own face to involuntarily falter.","After all, in his heart, Feng Jiu would always hold the place of his mother, while she, his biological mother, was addressed with a more formal and distant “Mother.”","The little boy holding the Black Tortoise Mistress’ hand looked from his older brother to Yue’er, blinked his innocent eyes, and remained silent, seemingly lost in his own thoughts.","“Big Brother, let’s go over there and look at those flowers!” Yue’er exclaimed, tugging on the hands of the two people beside her and skipping off in another direction."]},{"number":4639,"title":"Chapter 4639: Undercurrents","paragraphs":["Chapter 4639: Undercurrents","The little boy holding the Black Tortoise Mistress hand watched his older brother being led away by a girl who looked about his age. Even though he was clearly his older brother, she called him Big Brother. For a moment, he couldn’t help but bite his finger, his little face full of grievance.","Seeing that the others had walked some distance and no one was calling for him to join them, he abruptly shook off his mother’s hand and darted forward, determined to catch up.","The Black Tortoise Mistress, startled by his sudden movement, called out in concern, “Run slower, be careful not to fall!”","Hao’er, hearing the voice behind him, turned to see his younger brother hurrying towards them. He immediately slowed his pace and waited for him to arrive.","Yue’er, in the meantime, released Hao’er and Muchen’s hands and skipped ahead, crouching down to admire a cluster of vibrant flowers.","The little boy, finally reaching Hao’er’s side, reached out and tightly hugged his older brother’s arm, his eyes darting towards Muchen and Muyue with a possessive glare, as if to declare to them that this was his brother.","Muchen, with his characteristic maturity, simply ignored the younger boy’s silent declaration. Yue’er, still engrossed in the beauty of the flowers, didn’t even notice his pointed looks. Hao’er felt his younger brother’s tight grip but remained silent. Noticing Yue’er’s continued fascination with the flowers, he asked gently, “Yue’er, do you like that flower? Big Brother will pick it for you.”","Yue’er turned to him, her face bright with a smile. “Big Brother,” she said in her clear, sweet voice, “Picked flowers will wither quickly and lose their beauty. If we let them grow, we can admire them forever. Yue’er is a good child, so Yue’er won’t pick the flowers~”","Hearing her thoughtful words, Hao’er’s stern expression softened. “Then let’s go sit in the pavilion for a while,” he suggested. “We can have the servants bring us something to eat there.”","“Mm hmm~,” she replied happily, coming to stand beside him. She then noticed the little boy clinging tightly to her Big Brother’s arm, his small, tiger-like eyes glaring at her. Unable to resist, she blinked her own large, pretty eyes and said with a friendly smile, “Are you Big Brother’s little brother? What’s your name? My name is Muyue. You should call me Sister Yue’er!”","“Go away!” The little boy retorted, pushing Yue’er away with a sudden shove.","Caught off guard, Yue’er stumbled backward a few steps, her footing unsteady, and she fell to the ground.","“What are you doing!” Hao’er’s voice was sharp, his face instantly turning cold as he cast a stern glance at his younger brother beside him. He quickly freed his arm from his brother’s grip and stepped forward to help Yue’er up, gently brushing the dust off her pink skirt. “Yue’er, are you alright?”","“I’m fine,” Yue’er replied, looking down at the dirtied fabric. “Just my skirt is dirty.” The smile had vanished from her small face, replaced by a look of dismay.","Muchen, ever the pragmatist, reacted swiftly. He was not one for idle words and preferred direct action. Witnessing the little boy’s bullying of his sister, he immediately stepped forward and gave him a firm push, sending him tumbling to the ground.","“Waaaaaaaaaaaaa!” The little boy, clearly accustomed to being indulged, had now been scolded by Hao’er and pushed by Muchen, resulting in a fall. He promptly sat down and began to cry loudly.","Nearby, the Black Tortoise Mistress, who had been engaged in casual conversation with Du Fan and the others, heard her youngest son’s distressed cries. Her expression shifted instantly, and she hurried towards the commotion. Seeing her youngest child sitting on the ground, tears streaming down his face, a wave of sympathy washed over her, and she quickly scooped him up into her arms.","“What’s wrong? Why are you sitting on the ground crying like this?” she asked, her voice filled with concern.","“Wah, wah, wah, my brother yelled at me, they bullied me, wah, wah, wah...” the little boy cried sadly.","Upon hearing his tearful accusation, the Black Tortoise Mistress expression froze. She glanced at the three children standing before her, her eyes assessing the situation, but she remained silent, simply cooing softly to her youngest son, “It’s alright, it’s alright, don’t cry.”"]},{"number":4640,"title":"Chapter 4640: Angry","paragraphs":["Chapter 4640: Angry","She gently brushed the mud from her youngest son’s clothes, murmuring soothing words without so much as a glance at Hao’er and the others. With her little boy safely in her arms, she turned to Du Fan and the approaching group. “I am truly sorry, but I must take my leave first. Please feel free to continue exploring. I need to take my son home to change; he unfortunately fell and soiled his clothes.”","Seeing her concern, Du Fan offered a kind smile. “Madam, please don’t worry about us! We will happily wander around on our own.” As he watched her depart with her little son, Du Fan’s gaze lingered on Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue, though he offered no words. He couldn’t help but feel a pang of sympathy for them.","“Yue’er, would you like to change your dress?” Du Fan asked softly, his eyes resting on the little girl.","“No, Big Brother helped me clean it~” Yue’er replied in her clear voice. “I still want to play. If I change, I’ll just get dirty again.” She then looked at Hao’er, who was staring at the ground, and at Muchen, who was silently pursing his lips.","After a moment’s thought, Yue’er offered an explanation. “Uncle Du Fan, we didn’t bully Big Brother’s little brother. He pushed me first, so my brother pushed him back. We didn’t hit him!” Her soft voice carried a hint of anxiety, as if she feared they wouldn’t believe her. Hearing this earnest explanation, the masked man standing nearby allowed the corners of his lips to curl into a faint smile.","Being cultivators, they had all been aware of the commotion, even from across the flower bed, and understood the situation.","Moreover, despite their youthful appearances, Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue had already faced numerous dangers and hardships, including being lost on their own. This minor palace squabble was insignificant in comparison to their past experiences.","In truth, if a real confrontation had occurred, not only Muchen but even Yue’er could likely have defeated the spoiled little boy with ease.","“We know, don’t worry!” Du Fan reassured them gently. “It’s alright, the Black Tortoise Mistress won’t blame you.” In reality, they all sensed that despite her outward composure, the Black Tortoise Mistress must have been upset, otherwise she wouldn’t have immediately embraced her youngest son and left without a single word to Hao’er.","With this thought in mind, Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang exchanged knowing glances and looked at Hao’er, whose eyes remained downcast. Seeing his quiet dejection, they felt a pang of sympathy. Leng Hua stepped forward, gently ruffled Hao’er’s hair, and said, “Hao’er, you are familiar with this place. How about you show us around?”","Hearing this, Hao’er lifted his head, glanced at them, and nodded. “Mm, alright.”","After exploring more of the palace grounds, they returned to the courtyard to rest. Following a light meal together, Hao’er, who had his own courtyard within the palace, did not stay with Muchen and Muyue but returned to his own residence.","Leng Shuang helped Muyue take a bath and change into fresh clothes before joining the others in the courtyard. She noticed that her mother had not yet returned, but everyone else, except her big brother, was sitting and enjoying tea.","She ran over to the table and was about to climb onto a stool when she was gently lifted and placed firmly on the seat by someone beside her. She turned her head and offered a sweet smile. “Thank you, Uncle.”","The masked man glanced at her and corrected softly, “It’s Master.”","“Hehe.” Yue’er smiled sweetly but didn’t repeat the title. Instead, she turned her attention to Du Fan. “Uncle Du Fan, is my big brother unhappy? I noticed he wasn’t talking much just now. Did my brother push down my Big Brother’s younger brother, and that’s why he’s angry?”"]},{"number":4641,"title":"Chapter 4641: Teaching","paragraphs":["Chapter 4641: Teaching","Hearing this, Du Fan was momentarily surprised by Yue’er’s astute observation. However, recalling the inherent intelligence often displayed by his Master’s children, he simply smiled gently and said, “No, Yue’er, don’t overthink it. Your Big Brother won’t be angry with you.”","Yue’er blinked her large eyes, accepting his words without further comment. She merely nodded and then lay down on the table, resting her small chin on the back of her hand, patiently awaiting her mother’s return.","When Feng Jiu finally rejoined them, she found everyone still gathered in the courtyard, seated around the table. “Have you all eaten?” She asked gently. “Why didn’t you rest first?”","“We had some snacks, but not dinner yet. We’re waiting for Master to come back,” Leng Hua replied respectfully.","Seeing this, Feng Jiu instructed Leng Shuang, “Have the servants bring dinner. Just set it up here in the courtyard. Bring two tables from inside and place them together.” As she spoke, her gaze swept around, noting the absence of Hao’er. “Where is Hao’er? Did he join Black Tortoise Mistress for dinner?”","“Mother, earlier when I was in the garden, I pushed Big Brother’s little brother down,” Muchen stated, standing up to address her directly.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised her eyebrows slightly, squatted down to meet his gaze, and asked softly, “Then tell Mother, why did you push him down?”","“Mother, Mother, Big Brother’s little brother pushed Yue’er first, so my brother pushed him back,” Yue’er interjected quickly, hopping off her stool to stand protectively beside Muchen, clearly worried that her mother might scold him.","Feng Jiu gently patted both children on the head and smiled. “It is natural for brothers to protect their sisters; there is nothing wrong with that. However, we are guests in someone else’s home, so we must be mindful not to go too far. If it is a minor matter, it is often best to let it go and not hold a grudge. Harboring resentment over every little thing will only lead to trouble for yourselves in the long run.”","“Yes, we understand,” the two little ones replied in unison, their young minds carefully absorbing their mother’s teachings.","“That little boy is your Big Brother’s younger brother. He is younger than you and does not yet possess your understanding. You pushed him down. Tell me, whose side would your Big Brother likely take? Wouldn’t that place him in a difficult position?” Feng Jiu said softly, her eyes meeting theirs.","The two children listened intently to her words, exchanging a thoughtful glance. Muchen then asked, “Mother, what should we do?”","Feng Jiu smiled knowingly. “Didn’t you bring a gift for your Big Brother’s little brother? Mother will accompany you to give him the gift and offer an apology.”","“But Mother just said that it’s right for brothers to protect their sisters and that we did nothing wrong. Why do we have to apologize?” Yue’er asked, her brow furrowed in confusion.","Feng Jiu chuckled softly, gently pinching her daughter’s cheek. “We are not going to apologize because you did something wrong, but because it is a polite gesture. Besides, it was just a small incident, wasn’t it?”","The two children considered her words and finally nodded in agreement. “Alright! We will listen to Mother.”","Feng Jiu stood up and addressed the others in the courtyard. “You all eat first! Don’t wait for us. I will take them over there.”","“Since you said it was a small matter, why make them go over there? Besides, if anyone should apologize, it should be them,” the masked man remarked indifferently.","Feng Jiu turned to him, the corners of her lips curving into a subtle smile. “I am simply teaching the children how to navigate social interactions. Why resort to fists when you can use your brains to resolve things?”","She smiled again, looking down at the two children who were gazing up at her expectantly, then took their hands and led them out of the courtyard."]},{"number":4642,"title":"Chapter 4642: Rebuke","paragraphs":["Chapter 4642: Rebuke","Feng Jiu took their small hands in hers and, as they walked, asked the servants for directions to Hao’er’s courtyard, intending to see him first. Looking down at the two children beside her, she inquired softly, “Mother is taking you to apologize. Are you unhappy about that?”","“No,” they both replied, shaking their heads earnestly. “Mother must be doing this for our own good.”","Feng Jiu smiled, her eyes filled with affection as she gazed at them. “You still have much to learn,” she said gently. “In the future, Mother may not always be by your side to guide you, so you will need to rely on yourselves for many things. You must always remember that no matter how talented or powerful you become, you must never allow yourselves to be arrogant or conceited. Before you have fully matured, you can easily attract the attention of those who would plot against you and seek to destroy you. You must learn to protect yourselves and know when to conceal your abilities. When you encounter disagreements, do not immediately resort to violence. Think carefully about the consequences of your actions, use your minds, and exercise patience when you can. If you reach a point where you can no longer endure, then it is not too late to take action.”","The two children looked up at her, their expressions serious as they nodded in understanding. “Yes, we understand.”","Muchen silently resolved that in the future, he would heed his mother’s advice and ignore anyone who tried to provoke him. If he truly couldn’t restrain himself, he would ensure his retaliation was swift, clean, and decisive.","Yue’er pondered her mother’s words about using her brain more. She decided that when she didn’t want to fight, she would employ some of her medicinal knowledge to deal with those she disliked, ensuring they suffered silently without even realizing her involvement.","With these private thoughts, the two children exchanged a small, knowing smile.","Upon reaching Hao’er’s courtyard, they learned from the servants that the eldest young master had been summoned by the Black Tortoise Mistress. Consequently, they changed their course and headed towards the main courtyard.","Meanwhile, in the main courtyard, a little boy with tear-reddened eyes was nestled in his mother’s embrace, while the Black Tortoise Monarch sat beside her. Seeing Hao’er enter, he greeted him warmly. “Hao’er, come and sit down! It has been far too long since our family has shared a meal together. Let us enjoy a good meal today.”","Hao’er offered a polite reply and took a seat at the table. After a brief moment of contemplation, he spoke, “Mother, Chen’er did not push his younger brother intentionally. He was merely protecting Yue’er.”","Hearing this, the Black Tortoise Mistress cast him an indifferent glance. “Hao’er, you are our child and Bo’er’s older brother. Why do you consistently side with those two instead of protecting your own younger brother? You even speak on their behalf? Do you even remember whose child you are? Do you know who your real family is?”","Hao’er pursed his lips, his gaze falling to his lap, and remained silent.","“Alright, alright, why are you saying all of this? Your son has finally returned home; can’t you simply allow him to enjoy a peaceful meal with us? Why are you making such a significant issue out of this?” the Black Tortoise Monarch interjected, directing a disapproving look at his wife.","He then offered his eldest son a comforting smile. “Hao’er, your mother is simply like that; please don’t take her words to heart!”","On any other day, she would likely have remained silent after such a reprimand. However, today, her youngest son had been pushed and brought to tears. Her heart ached for him, and she felt a surge of annoyance. Thus, hearing her husband’s words, she retorted immediately, “Am I wrong to feel this way? Look at him; he is our own flesh and blood, yet he feels so distant from us. He addresses us as ‘mother’ and ‘father’ formally, but he calls Feng Jiu ‘Mother’ with such affection. I truly believe that in his heart, Feng Jiu is the only mother he acknowledges.”"]},{"number":4643,"title":"Chapter 4643: Cold Retort","paragraphs":["Chapter 4643: Cold Retort","Hearing this, the Black Tortoise Monarch felt a throbbing pain. “How can you even compare the two? You know perfectly well that if it hadn’t been for the Ghost Doctor saving our son, he would have perished long ago. He is still so young. How can you utter such words as his mother?”","“If I had known that he would never accept us as his parents, I would have preferred that he had died out there!” The moment the words left Black Tortoise Mistress’ lips, she realized the enormity of her transgression and fell silent, her gaze shifting to Hao’er with a look of guilt. Seeing the colour drain from his face, a sharp pang of regret pierced her heart.","Impulse was the devil. No matter what, he was the son she had carried for so many long months in her belly, and she should never have spoken to him in such a cruel manner.","Just as she was about to say something to retract her harsh words, Feng Jiu’s voice cut through the tense atmosphere, edged with a chilling coldness.","“In that case, Black Tortoise Mistress, just pretend you never had a son.”","Feng Jiu entered the courtyard, Muchen and Muyue close behind her. The two little ones had clearly overheard the earlier exchange, and their small faces were tight with anger.","“Big Brother!”","“Big Brother!”","They both ran forward and reached Hao’er’s side, each taking one of his hands, their gazes fixed on Lady Black Tortoise with the fierce protectiveness of small animals.","“Ghost Doctor, it’s a misunderstanding, truly a misunderstanding. My wife didn’t mean it; she spoke impulsively. Please don’t take it to heart.” Seeing Feng Jiu’s arrival, the Black Tortoise Monarch hurriedly stood up, attempting to smooth over the situation. However, the iciness of her expression made him feel profoundly uneasy.","Feng Jiu completely ignored him, walking slowly towards Hao’er. She reached out and gently stroked his head, her voice soft with reassurance. “It’s alright, Hao’er. We are still here for you.”","Hearing her tender words and feeling the warmth of her hand on his head, a wave of hurt and sadness washed over Hao’er. He forced himself to swallow the lump in his throat, looked up at the person beside him, and called out, his voice filled with helplessness, “Mother.”","Feng Jiu patted his shoulder gently and then turned to face Black Tortoise Mistress, her gaze frosty. “Hao’er was raised by me. In my heart, he is as dear as my own child. He has always been the treasure of my life. I cannot bear to see him suffer even the slightest injustice. I never imagined that upon coming to you, he would be treated in such a way, made to feel so unwanted. Since you do not want him, I will take him away with me. In the future, do not ever claim him as your son. In my eyes, you are not fit to be his mother.”","Her face paled visibly under Feng Jiu’s unwavering gaze. She tried to speak several times, but the sheer force of Feng Jiu’s cold fury rendered her speechless. She lacked the courage to utter a single word.","“Ghost Doctor, please calm down, Ghost Doctor, please calm down,” the Black Tortoise Monarch pleaded, his voice laced with anxiety. “My lady truly did not mean it.”","Feng Jiu turned her piercing gaze upon him. “Black Tortoise Monarch, since we are already addressing this matter, let us be clear! When I entrusted Hao’er back into your care, what promises did you both make to me? You swore that you would love him and never allow him to suffer even the slightest injustice. And what has transpired? Since you are incapable of loving, tolerating, and cherishing him as parents should, I am taking him with me today. You need not say anything further. When he grows up, if he chooses to return and see you, that will be his decision. I will never again bring him back here to endure such humiliation and injustice.”","“He is my son! I gave birth to him! How dare you try to take him away from me!” The Black Tortoise Mistress finally exploded, her voice filled with rage and indignation at Feng Jiu’s words."]},{"number":4644,"title":"Chapter 4644: Too Much","paragraphs":["Chapter 4644: Too Much","“Didn’t you just declare that you wished he had died out there back then? What? Now you suddenly claim him as your son?” Feng Jiu’s voice dripped with sarcasm as she glanced at the Black Tortoise Mistress, completely unmoved by her ashen face. She continued relentlessly, “As for why I am taking him away, have you never heard the saying, ‘The kindness of a parent is greater than the kindness of a friend’? Aside from the fact that I raised him, I rescued him from the very jaws of death and gave him a new lease on life. For that reason alone, I possess every right to take him!”","She then fixed the Black Tortoise Monarch with a cold stare. “If you, his biological parents, truly loved him unconditionally, I would naturally be overjoyed for him to have another set of parents who cherish him. But since you are demonstrably incapable of such genuine affection, then do not use your biological connection to restrict him and inflict further suffering upon him!”","Her protective instincts, especially where her children were concerned, were fierce. Had the Black Tortoise Monarch and his wife truly loved Hao’er, even if it caused her pain to part with the son she had raised with her own hands, she would have willingly sent him back to his biological parents for a harmonious and loving life. However, she would never, under any circumstances, allow the child she held so dear to endure humiliation and injustice at the hands of his own flesh and blood.","The Black Tortoise Monarch and his wife, hearing the unwavering conviction in her words, both paled and remained speechless, unable to find any rebuttal for a long moment.","Deep down, they knew Feng Jiu’s assessment was accurate. While they might have provided for Hao’er’s material needs, their love had been flawed. Initially, they had been eager to shower him with affection, wanting to compensate for his lost years.","However, Hao’er’s reserved nature had made it difficult to forge a deep connection. Later, with the arrival of their younger son, their focus and affection had shifted, creating an ever-widening chasm between them and Hao’er.","Feng Jiu’s sharp and direct words had pierced through their carefully constructed facade, exposing their own embarrassment and guilt, for they knew the truth of her accusations.","“Hao’er, come with Mother!” Feng Jiu said, not even glancing back at the stunned couple.","Without a word, Hao’er quietly rose, followed Feng Jiu, and walked out of the courtyard.","“Hao’er...” the Black Tortoise Monarch called out, his eyes filled with remorse.","Hao’er paused for a fleeting moment, but without turning his head, silently continued to follow Feng Jiu, never once looking back at them.","Muchen and Muyue, the two small figures, stayed close behind, each holding one of their big brother’s hands. They hadn’t fully grasped the extent of their big brother’s mistreatment by his biological parents before. Now that they understood, a surge of anger welled up within them, coupled with a silent vow to be even kinder and more supportive of their big brother in the future.","Watching them leave, the Black Tortoise Mistress’ face remained ashen. She sat motionless at the table, lost in her thoughts, the weight of regret or guilt heavy upon her.","The Black Tortoise Monarch sighed softly, glanced at his wife, and said, “Look at what you have done. Are you satisfied now?” He shook his head, his appetite gone, and walked out of the courtyard, his hands clasped behind his back.","The little boy still nestled in Black Tortoise Mistress’ arms was too young to fully comprehend the unfolding drama. He only understood that his brother had left again and might not return.","A small, worried voice escaped his lips. “Mother, will my brother come back?”"]},{"number":4645,"title":"Chapter 4645: Heart Turns Cold","paragraphs":["Chapter 4645: Heart Turns Cold","Hearing this, Black Tortoise Mistress’s face grew even paler. She remained silent, simply clutching her young son tightly to her chest and closing her eyes, a wave of guilt washing over her.","Meanwhile, Feng Jiu returned to the small courtyard that had been prepared for them, but she didn’t linger. Instead, she turned to her companions and declared, “Let’s go!” With that, she turned and strode out of the courtyard.","The others were taken aback for a moment. They exchanged bewildered glances before quickly following her.","They trailed behind Feng Jiu as she exited the palace grounds. Once outside, Feng Jiu summoned the flying ship. Just then, the Black Tortoise Monarch hurried towards them.","“Ghost Doctor, Ghost Doctor, wait, please wait!” He rushed forward, seeing that she was already preparing for departure with her people. “Ghost Doctor, you have only just arrived; why are you leaving so soon?” He then turned to Hao’er, who stood beside Feng Jiu, and pleaded, “Hao’er, persuade your mother to stay. Besides, you have just returned home; how can you...”","Hao’er looked at him, then his gaze drifted past him to the figure behind holding a small child. He spoke slowly, his voice cold and resolute. “I will not be coming back. Just consider me to have died back then! I no longer have a father or mother. I only have my parents. I have no further connection with you.”","As soon as he finished speaking, he turned and boarded the flying ship without a backward glance.","Witnessing Hao’er’s silent yet powerful declaration, Feng Jiu glanced at the Black Tortoise Monarch and the Black Tortoise Mistress standing behind him. “Farewell,” she said simply before turning and boarding the airship with her two children.","Du Fan and the others followed suit, boarding the airship one after another. Once the airship had lifted off and left the palace far behind, Du Fan noticed that Hao’er had retreated to the cabin to rest. He approached Feng Jiu and asked, “Master, what happened?”","Yue’er was still visibly upset. Hearing Du Fan’s question, she could not help but complain, “Hmph! They were mean to Big Brother!”","Feng Jiu gently patted her daughter’s head and explained slowly, “When I took the two little ones to their courtyard earlier, I overheard the Black Tortoise Mistress scolding Hao’er. I stopped the maids who were about to go in and report it by tapping their acupoints. We listened outside for a while and heard their conversation become increasingly outrageous. In the end, they even expressed that they wished Hao’er had died out there and never returned.”","A flash of coldness flickered in her eyes, and her voice grew a degree colder. “Hearing such heartless words, I couldn’t restrain myself. I took the two children inside and confronted them. Since they clearly held no regard for Hao’er, I declared that he would be mine from now on, and I would never bring him back to face their cruelty again.”","Hearing this, Du Fan sighed softly. “I did not expect the Black Tortoise Mistress to be so unreasonable, but perhaps this is for the best. At least Hao’er will not have to endure such treatment again.” He recalled that when his master had asked him to check on Hao’er’s well-being a few years prior, he had sensed that a direct confrontation would likely lead to a falling out. Sadly, his premonition had proven correct.","“It is growing late,” Feng Jiu said, her tone shifting to practicality. “Keep an eye out below. When we spot a town, we will descend and rest for the night. Also, the children have not yet had dinner. We must find them something to eat.”","“Do not worry, Master. I will keep watch,” Du Fan assured her. Seeing her walk towards the cabin, he settled down to one side and released his divine sense, scanning the area below for any signs of civilization.","Alone in the cabin, Hao’er sat by the window, gazing at the darkening sky. The harsh words his biological mother had spoken earlier echoed in his mind, sending a shiver down his spine. He instinctively drew his arms around himself, seeking a semblance of comfort in the growing darkness."]},{"number":4646,"title":"Chapter 4646: Relaxing","paragraphs":["Chapter 4646: Relaxing","“Hao’er? Mother has come to keep you company,” Feng Jiu said gently from outside the cabin door.","Hearing her voice, Hao’er quickly got up and opened the door. “Mother,” he murmured, throwing himself into her embrace, his voice filled with emotion.","Feng Jiu held him close, gently patting his back. “It’s alright, Mother is here with you,” she soothed him in a comforting voice.","She led him to the bed and sat down, speaking softly. “Hao’er, you must understand that no one in this world will always be by your side. On the path of growing up, you will encounter many things that you must learn to face and adapt to on your own.”","Feng Jiu stayed with Hao’er in the cabin, offering him comfort and guidance. Outside, when Du Fan spotted a town below, he approached the cabin and called out, “Master, there’s a town below.”","Taking Hao’er’s hand, Feng Jiu walked out of the cabin. “Let’s go down and rest for a while!” she said, and with that, she steered the flying ship towards the town.","Upon landing, she stowed away the flying ship, and the group made their way into the bustling city. The vibrant streets, children playing joyfully, and colorful lanterns illuminating the shops on either side caught Feng Jiu’s attention. “Du Fan,” she said, “go and find an inn first! I’ll take the children to explore the city for a bit.”","Turning to the masked man, she added, “You go and rest first! There’s no need for you to follow us around.”","The masked man glanced at Yue’er, then nodded indifferently. “Mm.” With that, he turned and headed off to find lodging.","“Master, don’t stay out too late. I’ll find a good inn and notify you with the communication jade,” Du Fan said, bowing slightly before following the masked man, leaving Leng Hua and Leng Shuang with Feng Jiu and the children.","“Come on, Mother will take you around. Tell me what you’d like to eat, and I’ll buy it for you,” Feng Jiu said with a warm smile, leading them forward.","Leng Hua and Leng Shuang exchanged a knowing glance and smiled, quietly trailing behind them, keeping a watchful eye on the three children.","Compared to the formal fare of restaurants, the three children clearly preferred the array of street snacks. Feng Jiu indulged them, letting them sample everything that caught their eye and buying them small toys. As they played and relaxed along the way, Hao’er’s mood gradually began to lift.","“Are you tired? Would you like to head back and rest?” Feng Jiu asked, observing the children’s obvious excitement.","“Mother, Mother, I heard people over there saying they are going to the river to release wish lanterns! Mother, let’s go too!” Yue’er tugged on her hand and shook it gently, looking up at her with a pleading expression.","Seeing her daughter’s eagerness, Feng Jiu smiled and replied with mock helplessness, “Okay, okay, Mother will go with you. Let’s go! First, we need to buy some wish lanterns.”","They walked towards the nearby stalls, purchased a few lanterns, and followed the other people carrying them until they reached a river where numerous wish lanterns were already floating.","On the water’s surface, the wish lanterns resembled blooming lotus flowers, emitting a soft, ethereal glow as they drifted along with the gentle current, creating a truly breathtaking spectacle.","The three children approached the riverbank, lanterns in hand. They joined their hands together, silently made their wishes, and then carefully placed the lanterns in the water, watching them float away slowly.","“Mother, let’s go back to the inn! Yue’er wants to go to sleep now,” Yue’er said, running to her mother’s side and looking up at her with her sleepy little face."]},{"number":4647,"title":"Chapter 4647: Reunion","paragraphs":["Chapter 4647: Reunion","“Alright, let’s go back and rest,” Feng Jiu agreed, bending down to carry Yue’er into her arms. She smiled at Hao’er and Muchen, who were walking towards them. “Let’s head to the inn and get some sleep!”","The two boys nodded and followed her to the inn.","The next day at noon, they boarded the airship and departed, their first stop the Feng family’s ancestral home to collect Seventeen before setting course for the mortal realm where the Pan Family resided.","A month later, the three children found themselves in the mortal realm once more. However, this time, the circumstances were vastly different from their previous, stranded predicament. Now, they were accompanied by their mother and their companions.","During their journey, Feng Jiu made sure to incorporate sightseeing and opportunities for Hao’er to relax, and for Muchen and Muyue to enjoy themselves. She also took the opportunity to impart some of her knowledge to them.","Yue’er showed a keen interest in medicine, so Feng Jiu began to teach her. Despite her young age, Yue’er was a quick study, and within a single month, she was already capable of mixing simple remedies on her own.","Feng Jiu also guided Hao’er and Muchen in their cultivation. The two often sparred, and Muchen showed rapid progress. However, Hao’er became increasingly withdrawn as they traveled. Though he tried to appear normal, Feng Jiu sensed the deep wound inflicted by his biological mother’s words, a sharp pain that would not easily heal.","Having arrived in the mortal realm, they forsook the flying ship, occasionally soaring through the skies on their swords but more often traveling on foot and resting along the way. Despite the leisurely pace, they reached the imperial city in the evening.","“Mother, we’re here!” Yue’er exclaimed excitedly. “I can go see Brother Boqing and Sister Xue’er!”","A rare smile touched Muchen’s lips as well. Though he remained silent, his anticipation at seeing their old friend was evident.","“Mother, the Pan Family is just ahead,” Hao’er said, pointing in the direction.","As they entered the city, the astonished and curious gazes of the citizens followed them intently. The aura of cultivators was unmistakable, far surpassing that of ordinary mortals, and their extraordinary appearances naturally drew everyone’s attention and sparked their curiosity.","“Hey, look! Aren’t those twins the ones who used to live in the Pan Family?” Someone recognized Muchen and Muyue. Their delicate and identical features made them difficult to forget.","“Those are immortal children! The immortal children are back! Look at the people around them; they are all so beautiful! They must be immortals!”","“Immortals have come to our Imperial City! Immortals have come to our Imperial City!”","As the excited cries of one commoner spread, the voices echoed and multiplied, and they found themselves surrounded by a dense crowd. Yet, no one blocked their path. As they continued forward, the surrounding commoners instinctively made way for them.","Some people even ran ahead to the Pan Family to spread the extraordinary news.","Pan Ning was in his courtyard, enjoying a cup of tea and reading a book, while his son Boqing practiced his boxing in the open space. Suddenly, he saw his Steward rush in, his face full of excitement. Pan Ning put down his teacup, a question in his eyes. “What is it?”","“Second Young Master, it’s incredible news, truly incredible news! An Immortal has arrived in the Imperial City, and according to the person who brought us the news, he also saw Young Master Hao, Young Master Chen, and Young Miss Yue’er!” The steward’s face was flushed with excitement as he hurriedly delivered the astonishing report."]},{"number":4648,"title":"Chapter 4648: Immortals","paragraphs":["Chapter 4648: Immortals","“Muchen and Yue’er are back?” Upon hearing this, Boqing’s eyes lit up, and he immediately ran outside, shouting, “Great, great! Muchen and Yue’er are back!”","Pan Ning was also taken aback, quickly stood up, and asked anxiously, “You said they’re back? Did someone accompany them?”","“Yes, someone accompanied them. They should be at the gate soon,” the butler said with a smile.","“Did you notify the Old Patriarch and the others?” Pan Ning asked as he hurried outside.","The steward followed behind him and replied, “Yes, I already notified them. The Old Patriarch and the others are already in the front yard.”","“Then what are you still standing there for? Hurry up and open the door. Let’s go out to welcome them,” Pan Ning urged as he moved quickly forward.","When Pan Ning arrived at the front yard, his elder brother, sister-in-law, the old master, several children, and his wife were already waiting. He quickly approached and said, “Grandfather, I heard that Muchen and Yue’er are back.”","“The man who claimed to be their uncle just left not long ago, and now we hear that several children have returned. I presume they have returned to their parents,” the Old Patriarch said. “Let’s go outside to welcome them! They have done a great favor for the Pan family.”","So, led by the Old Patriarch, the group proceeded to the front gate of the Pan family and waited. From a distance, they could see the group, surrounded by the townspeople, walking slowly towards them.","As they observed the approaching group, even the members of the Pan family couldn’t help but be shocked and surprised. This was because the people walking towards them, both men and women, were remarkably good-looking and possessed a stunning presence. What impressed them most profoundly was the extraordinary temperament they exuded. The ethereal grace of immortals and the noble aura they carried instilled a sense of awe, making one hesitant to be impolite.","“Brother Boqing! Brother Bowen! Sister Xue’er, we’re back!” Yue’er saw them from afar and hurriedly waved her little hands, shouting as she ran forward.","“Yue’er Sister!” Boqing waved back, his face radiating with excitement.","Bowen and Xue’er, who were standing beside Pan Hong, also smiled happily upon seeing her, their eyes shining as they looked at their little friend whom they hadn’t seen in a long time.","“Boqing, look, we’re back, and we brought my Mother with us~” Yue’er said with a smile, turning to look at her mother and adding with delight, “Boqing, look how beautiful my Mother is. The one in red is my Mother.”","Boqing gazed at the beautiful woman in the red dress and couldn’t help but widen his eyes in astonishment. “Yue’er, is your mother also an immortal?! Can your mother fly? Let me tell you, a few months ago, a man with a thick waist and broad back came looking for you and said he was your uncle. He can fly. I saw him fly away!”","“Hehe, that’s my uncle, but he didn’t come with us this time,” Yue’er replied with a giggle.","At this moment, the Old Patriarch of the Pan family stepped forward and bowed respectfully. “Greetings, distinguished guests. Please come inside.” He gestured for them to enter the mansion first.","“Please come inside, everyone,” Pan Hong and Pan Ning followed him and extended their invitation, bowing and gesturing for them to enter as well.","Feng Jiu glanced at them, offered a slight smile and a nod, and then followed them inside.","As the Pan family’s gate closed, the commoners who had been following them were left outside, their faces flushed red with excitement."]},{"number":4649,"title":"Chapter 4649: Coming to the door","paragraphs":["Chapter 4649: Coming to the door","Old Patriarch Pan respectfully welcomed Feng Jiu and the others into the hall. Displaying their deference, they did not dare to take seats before her, but instead invited Feng Jiu to occupy the seat of honor, positioning themselves on either side.","In contrast to the Pan family’s cautious and somewhat nervous demeanor, the children of the Pan family, particularly Boqing, exuded excitement. They eagerly crowded around Muchen and Yue’er, animatedly recounting how Boqing had begun learning martial arts and was already showing great progress.","Feng Jiu glanced at the children with a gentle smile, then turned her attention to the Old Patriarch of the Pan family. “My name is Feng Jiu,” she began, her voice calm and clear. “I am the mother of these three children. Some time ago, due to unforeseen circumstances, my children were separated from me and found themselves in the mortal world. I have only recently been reunited with them. Upon learning of the care and kindness your family has shown them, I came here to express my sincere gratitude.”","“Not at all, not at all,” the Old Patriarch responded quickly and repeatedly, his tone earnest. “It is our Pan family who owes your Young Masters and Young Miss a profound debt of gratitude. We dare not accept your thanks.”","Feng Jiu offered a polite smile and remained silent for a moment. Her gaze shifted to Pan Ning, then moved to Pan Hong, whom she appraised thoughtfully. Finally, her attention settled on his legs. “Muchen informed me that you extended them a significant kindness. When the eldest young master was ambushed and poisoned, you saved his life with a medicinal pill, but you were unable to heal his legs. I have come here this time to assess the condition of his legs.”","“Thank you, Madam,” the Old Patriarch said, standing up somewhat excitedly and bowing respectfully.","They engaged in casual conversation in the hall for a while. Meanwhile, outside, the city was abuzz with news. Even the Emperor within the Imperial Palace received reports from his secret guards that immortals had arrived at the Pan family. He had been in the midst of summoning his ministers for a meeting, but he promptly dismissed them. Among those present was Pan Ning’s father.","“Minister Pan, remain where you are,” the emperor called out as he rose from his seat.","Pan’s father was taken aback and hurriedly turned around, bowing with both hands. “What further command does Your Majesty have?” he asked, puzzled. He had been wondering why their discussion had been abruptly interrupted, but the Emperor’s intentions were often inscrutable, so he didn’t dwell on it. He had been thinking that it was getting late and he should return home for dinner, only to be summoned back by the Emperor’s voice.","“Hahaha, Minister Pan! Wait a moment; I will change into my casual attire and accompany you,” the emperor said with a smile, his eyes filled with amusement. He didn’t even allow Pan’s father time to respond, and after issuing a quick instruction to his attendants, he hurried back into the palace to change his clothes.","Pan’s father stood there in a daze, wondering why the Emperor wished to visit their humble abode once more. What was his purpose this time? Could something untoward have occurred at home? A sense of unease settled upon him as he waited, each moment feeling drawn out. Finally, when he saw the Emperor emerge in plain clothes, followed by several guards, he quickly stepped forward and inquired, “Your Majesty, why do you wish to go to this old servant’s house? Is anything amiss?”","“Hahahea let’s go! You will find out when we arrive,” the Emperor replied cryptically, offering a smile as he strode outside.","Helpless, Pan’s father could only follow swiftly.","Meanwhile, at the Pan residence, preparations for the evening banquet were underway. The children, who rarely had the opportunity to see each other, all headed to the martial arts training ground to play. Feng Jiu seized this quiet moment to thoroughly examine Pan Hong’s legs.","“It is not a significant problem. We will begin treatment tomorrow, and he will be able to stand within half a month,” Feng Jiu stated with a reassuring smile, observing their expressions of surprise and disbelief.","“Half a month, and he will be able to stand?” Old Patriarch Pan stammered, his voice filled with astonishment. Numerous physicians and even Imperial Physicians in the city had declared that Hong’er’s legs were beyond repair and that he would never walk again in his lifetime."]},{"number":4650,"title":"Chapter 4650: Mesmerized","paragraphs":["Chapter 4650: Mesmerized","“Yes, he will be able to stand up in half a month,” Feng Jiu confirmed with a nod.","“Thank you, Madam, thank you!” the Old Patriarch expressed his gratitude repeatedly, his voice filled with emotion.","Pan Hong, too, couldn’t conceal his excitement upon hearing that he would be able to stand in such a short time. His wife, who stood nearby, wiped away tears of relief and bowed gratefully to Feng Jiu. “Thank you, Madam!”","“Madam, please join us in the front courtyard for dinner!” Pan Ning gestured an invitation and said, “My father has not yet returned from the palace. When he comes back, we will come and pay our respects to you.”","“It’s fine,” Feng Jiu replied, waving a dismissive hand to indicate he needn’t trouble himself, and then walked towards the front courtyard accompanied by Pan Ning.","From the moment Pan’s father exited the palace gates, the coachman approached to congratulate him. He relayed the news that an Immortal had arrived at the Pan family and that someone had come to the palace specifically to inform them and urge them to return home swiftly.","Pan’s father was both surprised and delighted, finally understanding the Emperor’s peculiar request to accompany him. He glanced back and saw that the Emperor had already entered a modest yet luxurious carriage. He quickly boarded his own carriage and instructed the driver to hasten home.","As they traveled, the townspeople who recognized the Pan family’s carriage came forward to offer their congratulations, remarking that their family had been blessed by the arrival of an Immortal.","They hurried back home and found a large crowd gathered in front of the gate. They had the crowd dispersed and personally welcomed the Emperor, who was dressed in plain clothes, into their residence before closing the gate.","“Your Majesty, please come in.” Although Pan’s father was eager to rush inside to understand the situation, he couldn’t leave the Emperor unattended and thus urged him to enter first.","The Emperor, eager to catch a glimpse of the immortal, quickened his pace as he entered the Pan family’s house. Upon reaching the front courtyard and observing the servants bustling about, carrying dishes to the table, he couldn’t help but smile. “It seems I have arrived at just the right time!” he remarked.","Pan’s father offered an apologetic smile. “Your Majesty’s arrival ensures that we will all dine together. Perhaps you will even have the honor of meeting the Immortal.”","The two continued their conversation as they walked inside. The Emperor, who was leading the way, slowed his steps as he entered the banquet hall. His breath hitched in his throat, and he stopped abruptly, his eyes fixed on the stunningly beautiful woman dressed in a dazzling red dress who sat at the centre of the banquet table.","Could this breathtakingly beautiful woman be the Immortal?","Such a face, seemingly sculpted by the heavens themselves, surpassed the beauty of even the three thousand concubines in his harem. The noble and elegant aura that radiated from her was particularly captivating, capable of ensnaring any heart. She was like a radiant sun; in her presence, the brilliance of others seemed to fade into insignificance.","His heart skipped a beat, yet his breathing shallowed, as if he were afraid to disturb a celestial being. His burning gaze remained fixed on her, following her every movement, every smile, every slight frown. The more he looked, the more enchanting she became, and the more his heart ached with a newfound desire.","Feng Jiu immediately noticed the intense gaze, which held the possessiveness of a hunter eyeing its prey, but she chose to ignore it. However, she hadn’t anticipated that the gaze would become even more blatant, causing her smile to falter slightly as she conversed with Pan Ning and the others.","“Your Majesty, Your Majesty.”","Pan’s father called out anxiously twice. Witnessing the Emperor’s unwavering stare at the immortal, his worry intensified, fearing that the immortal would become angered and punish them. Forgetting all decorum in his apprehension, he stepped forward and tugged at the Emperor’s sleeve.","“Your Majesty, Your Majesty!”"]},{"number":4651,"title":"Chapter 4651: Frightened","paragraphs":["Chapter 4651: Frightened","His voice deepened slightly, carrying a note of impatience that finally snapped the Emperor out of his captivated state, where he had been utterly mesmerized by Feng Jiu’s unparalleled beauty.","“Ahem!”","Feeling a sense of unease, he pressed his fist to his lips and coughed lightly. He glanced at Pan’s father, then turned his gaze back to the stunning woman in red. “Minister Pan,” he began, his voice a little unsteady, “this young lady must be an Immortal, wouldn’t you agree?”","Pan’s father quickly wiped a bead of sweat from his brow. “I have not had the honour of meeting her before, Your Majesty, but given her presence here, it seems likely.”","Old Patriarch Pan, Pan Hong, Pan Ning, and the others had all noticed the Emperor’s arrival. They had also saw the way his gaze lingered on Feng Jiu, the unmistakable look of a man captivated by a woman. Under normal circumstances, if Feng Jiu were an ordinary woman, it might be understandable for the Emperor, as the ruler of the land, to regard her with such interest.","However, Feng Jiu was no ordinary woman. She was an Immortal, and importantly, an Immortal woman who already had a husband and three children! The Emperor’s blatant admiration felt like a profound disrespect, causing a wave of unease to ripple through them. They quickly rose, hoping to smooth over the awkward situation.","“Greetings, Your Majesty,” the Old Patriarch and the others said in unison, bowing respectfully.","“Haha, I came in disguise, so there is no need for such formalities between Emperor and subjects,” the Emperor said with a forced smile, waving his hand dismissively, though his gaze remained fixed on Feng Jiu. He watched as she sat gracefully, gently twirling a wine cup in her hand, her slender white fingers moving with delicate precision, creating an unexpectedly alluring spectacle.","“What audacity!”","The sharp rebuke, delivered with icy disdain by Leng Shuang, sent a jolt through the Emperor. He snapped his gaze away from Feng Jiu’s fingers, belatedly realizing he had been openly swallowing his saliva. A wave of embarrassment washed over him, his face flushing from pale to red as he struggled to regain his composure.","An oppressive aura filled the air, a palpable weight that pressed down on everyone present, making even the simple act of breathing feel labored. The most profoundly affected was undoubtedly the Emperor.","He stood there, beads of cold sweat trickling down his forehead. The immense pressure emanating from Leng Shuang instilled a deep sense of fear, and he felt an almost irresistible urge to kneel. However, Leng Shuang, ever mindful of the potential repercussions, knew her limits. Forcing the Emperor to kneel before so many members of the Pan family would likely provoke his wrath, which he might then vent on them.","Therefore, she merely exerted enough pressure to make him intensely uncomfortable, stopping short of forcing him to his knees.","Before long, the Emperor’s clothes were damp with cold sweat, and his legs felt weak and unsteady. Just then, Feng Jiu’s calm voice broke the tense silence. “All right, let’s go see if the children are here.”","“Yes,” Leng Shuang replied, immediately withdrawing her oppressive aura and turning to leave.","Seeing this opportunity, Pan’s father hurried forward to bow apologetically to Feng Jiu, offered a few conciliatory words, and then quickly assisted the visibly shaken emperor out of the hall.","“Madam, I must take my leave,” Pan Hong said, bowing respectfully to Feng Jiu before wheeling himself away.","“Madam, please do not take it personally. His Majesty has held power for a long time, and it is perhaps inevitable that he sometimes loses his sense of proportion,” the Old Patriarch offered hesitantly.","Feng Jiu smiled faintly. “It seems that your Emperor is not a particularly astute individual. For the ruler of a country to be so short-sighted is hardly a blessing for his people.”","The Pan family dared not voice their agreement or disagreement with such a statement. Pan Ning simply refilled Feng Jiu’s wine cup and steered the conversation towards safer topics.","On the other side of the courtyard, the Emperor, supported by Pan’s father, was helped into a quiet side room and gently lowered onto a chair. His legs felt like jelly, and he lacked the strength to even stand, as if all his vitality had been drained away.","He wiped off his cold sweat and muttered after a long silence, his voice still trembling slightly, “The pressure of an Immortal is truly... formidable.”"]},{"number":4652,"title":"Chapter 4652: Interests","paragraphs":["Chapter 4652: Interests","Pan’s father watched the Emperor depart, he looked like he wanted to say something but was holding back. He had a sinking feeling that the Emperor’s unexpected visit was not good. Just wait and see, he thought grimly. This time, they had inadvertently offended an Immortal, and the consequences could be dire, not just for the Emperor but potentially for the entire Pan family.","“Master, the eldest Young Master is here,” the attendant announced from outside.","Hearing this, Pan’s father glanced at the Emperor, the words “Your Majesty...” forming on his lips.","“Let him in,” the Emperor said listlessly, sinking back into his chair.","So Pan’s father went to open the door himself. Seeing his eldest son maneuvering his wheelchair into the room, he stepped forward to assist, pushing it slightly before closing the door behind them.","“Greetings, Your Majesty,” Pan Hong said, bowing his head from his wheelchair.","“No need,” the Emperor replied with a dismissive wave, his gaze fixed on Pan Hong. “What brings you here? Are you perhaps inviting me to join your dinner?”","“Your Majesty.”","Pan Hong’s expression was serious as he looked at the Emperor. “Your Majesty, what I am about to say may sound disrespectful, but I assure you it is entirely for your own benefit. I humbly beg your forgiveness in advance.”","Hearing this, the Emperor’s expression shifted, a flicker of unease crossing his features. He remained silent for a moment before simply saying, “Speak.”","“Yes.”","Pan Hong took a breath and continued, “I believe the Emperor’s actions just now were... inappropriate. Those are Immortals, beings from the heavens above. Even as the ruler of our great nation, you cannot afford to offend such beings. Your Majesty is surely aware of the nature of immortals. If you were to anger even one of them, they possess the power to obliterate our entire empire in the blink of an eye.”","Observing the Emperor’s increasingly tense demeanor, Pan Hong pressed on. “In the lands under Your Majesty’s rule, the arrival of Immortals at our imperial court is an immeasurable blessing, a stroke of fortune that cannot be sought or bought. Any monarch in the world, upon hearing such news, would undoubtedly bend over backwards to show goodwill and establish friendly relations. How can Your Majesty allow such a monumental blessing, such incredible good fortune, to be jeopardized by a moment of... confusion?”","“Then, according to you, what should I do now?” The Emperor’s voice held a newfound urgency. The gravity and importance of the situation had finally sunk in, the haze of infatuation momentarily dispelled. He looked at Pan Hong expectantly.","Pan Hong, confined to his wheelchair due to his paralyzed legs, had long since resigned from his official duties and now lived a quiet life at home. As a former court official, he technically should not have interfered in such matters. However, this situation concerned not only the Emperor but also the well-being of his own family, so he felt compelled to speak up and clearly lay out the potential consequences.","Seeing that the Emperor was finally listening intently, a sliver of relief washed over him. “If Your Majesty heeds my advice, you should go and apologize in person immediately, and then return to the palace.”","“Apologize?” The Emperor hesitated, a flicker of his royal pride surfacing. He was the supreme ruler of the land; how could he lower himself to apologize?","“If Your Majesty feels that a personal apology is inappropriate, you could return to the palace first and then dispatch someone with generous gifts as a token of apology. My father and I will certainly speak well of Your Majesty to the Immortal and implore her forgiveness,” Pan Hong suggested again.","Hearing this, the Emperor quickly agreed. “Alright, alright, we shall do as you say. I will return to the palace at once and send a lavish gift. You must both speak favorably of me to the immortal. I truly did not intend to cause any offense.”","“Yes, Your Majesty,” Pan Hong replied.","Seeing the Emperor’s cooperation, Pan’s father felt a wave of relief wash over him. He stepped forward. “Your Majesty, allow me to see you out.”","“No need, no need. You go and keep the Immortal company! I can manage on my own.” He waved his hand dismissively, took a deep breath, and walked out of the room, escorted by his guards.","Watching him leave, Pan’s father and Pan Hong exchanged a knowing glance and a small, hopeful smile."]},{"number":4653,"title":"Chapter 4653: Envy","paragraphs":["Chapter 4653: Envy","Fortunately, the Emperor still held his empire in high regard and didn’t allow mere beauty to cloud his judgment entirely. Otherwise, they would have been utterly at a loss on how to navigate such a delicate situation.","“Let’s return to the banquet hall first!” Pan’s father suggested, gesturing for Pan Hong to lead the way.","Pan Hong nodded and propelled his wheelchair forward. Pan’s father, walking beside him, refrained from assisting, respecting his son’s independence. “Our Pan family is truly blessed,” he mused. “I never anticipated Hao’er’s mother would come in person.”","“Yes, I also didn’t expect their return,” Pan Hong agreed.","In his mind, when the three children had departed previously, they had bestowed upon the Pan family valuable treasures and done them significant favors. Any perceived debt of gratitude, in his view, had long been repaid. Moreover, the Pan family had done little for the children in return, aside from offering them temporary shelter when they were stranded.","This time, their arrival was different. Everyone in the Pan family understood that their guests had not concealed their divine status upon entering the imperial city. Their presence in the Pan residence now bestowed immense honor upon them. From this day forward, it would be widely known that the Pan family had a connection to Immortials, and no one would dare to look down on them. This held true regardless of their official standing in the court; even if they were commoners, such an association would elevate their status immeasurably.","Upon reaching the main table, the other members of the family and the children also arrived. The two men approached Feng Jiu’s side, and Pan’s father said apologetically, “Madam, I am truly sorry for...”","Feng Jiu raised a hand, cutting him off gently. “Never mind, there is no need to dwell on it. Our stay here will be brief. Our primary purpose is to heal the eldest young master’s legs. Please, take your seats!”","Seeing her graciousness, the two men acknowledged her words and sat down at the table. Perhaps it was the undeniable presence of immortals among them, or perhaps it was the innate aura of authority that emanated from Feng Jiu and her companions, but the Pan family members were noticeably more reserved than before.","The children, however, were much more at ease at the table, especially Boqing, who was overjoyed to be reunited with his little friends.","The Pan family accompanied Feng Jiu and the others, engaging in polite conversation and sharing drinks until the late hours of the night before finally retiring to their respective courtyards to rest.","Despite the lateness of the hour, Seventeen, who had returned with Feng Jiu and the others, did not seek rest. Instead, he gathered with his former shadow guard comrades.","“Seventeen, I never imagined you would become an Immortal! You are truly blessed,” one of them exclaimed.","“Yes! It never crossed my mind that one day you would achieve such a feat! We are all incredibly envious.” Another chimed in.","“Seventeen, tell us about the world of immortals! What wonders await that we have never seen? Do immortals truly fly through the sky? Can you fly now, Seventeen?”","The shadow guards eagerly surrounded Seventeen, peppering him with questions filled with envy and curiosity. Among their ranks, Seventeen was the only one who had left their service. It had been the Second Young Master who had dispatched him to accompany Young Master Hao and the others, instructing him to follow their lead. Little did he know that this departure would lead him down a path to immortality.","Seventeen had originally been the Second Young Master’s personal shadow guard, a position of considerable trust and skill. Later, he had been assigned to care for three seemingly ordinary children. At the time, none of them knew the true identities of these children. They had only perceived it as a waste of Seventeen’s exceptional talents, assigning one of their top three bodyguards to protect mere children. However, what they had failed to anticipate was the immense influence of these three children and the extraordinary opportunity they would inadvertently provide Seventeen – a chance at immortality, something they themselves could never hope to achieve in countless lifetimes, yet it had fallen into Seventeen’s lap so unexpectedly."]},{"number":4654,"title":"Chapter 4654: Hopeful","paragraphs":["Chapter 4654: Hopeful","Ever since Seventeen had departed with the three children, a sense of unease had lingered among his former comrades. Some had even begun to fear the worst, imagining the dangers he might face protecting three young kids in an unknown and potentially hostile environment. The news of Seventeen’s survival, let alone his ascension to immortality, filled them with a potent mixture of astonishment and envy.","Seventeen regarded them with a knowing look. “The immortal world,” he explained, “is not the idyllic paradise you might imagine. In many ways, it is even more perilous than the mortal realm. With my current abilities, I would be utterly defenseless against many true immortals. You must understand, immortals often don’t even need to lift a finger to kill. Their very aura can crush a person. Furthermore, the beasts there have awakened their spiritual intelligence, making them formidable opponents with astonishing fighting prowess...”","That night, under the soft glow of the courtyard lanterns, Seventeen painted a vivid picture of the immortal world for his former brothers, recounting both its breathtaking wonders and its stark cruelties. His tales left them awestruck and envious of the possibilities, yet also deeply shocked by the inherent dangers. They had naively imagined a realm of pure bliss, only to learn that even in immortality, strife and slaughter were inescapable realities.","However, even with this newfound understanding of the darkness that existed alongside the light, their yearning for that realm persisted. The allure of a lifespan twice that of ordinary mortals, the chance to witness unimaginable sights and experiences, far outweighed the knowledge of potential hardship. Despite the cruelty, a deep regret gnawed at them for not having been blessed with such divine fortune.","Early the following morning, Feng Jiu began Pan Hong’s treatment. With precise movements, she inserted slender silver needles into his legs, channeling spirit energy to stimulate blood circulation and clear the meridians. She then instructed the family to prepare a medicinal bath for him. As she returned to the courtyard, she observed Pan’s father overseeing the arrival of the gifts sent by the Emperor in the early hours.","“Madam, these are gifts from the Emperor,” Pan’s father announced, gesturing to his men as they carefully placed the various items on a table in Feng Jiu’s courtyard. “They are nothing, of course, compared to the treasures you have undoubtedly seen, but they are offered as a small token of the Emperor’s goodwill.”","Feng Jiu smiled dismissively. “You may keep them. These things are of no practical use to us.”","Understanding her words, Pan Ning instructed his men to have the items moved to the main courtyard. They recognized that what they considered valuable treasures were likely insignificant trinkets to beings of Feng Jiu’s stature.","Feng Jiu strolled leisurely out of the courtyard and settled onto a nearby seat, her gaze softening as she watched the children playing. With a gentle wave of her hand, she beckoned Pan’s father and Pan Ning to join her at the table.","“Pan Hong’s leg will only require three days of silver needle acupuncture,” she explained. “For the remaining time, regular soaking in the medicinal bath will facilitate a gradual recovery. Once he can stand and walk, ensure he practices every morning. Gentle exercise will accelerate his healing process.”","Pan’s father and Pan Ning listened intently, replying in unison, “Understood, we will remember that.”","Suddenly, Boqing came running towards them, his small hand tugging at Pan Ning’s sleeve. “Father! Grandfather! I want to cultivate immortality like Yue’er and Muchen!” he exclaimed. “I want to be as strong as them. Father, not only can’t I beat Muchen, I can’t even touch Yue’er’s clothes!”","He had come to terms with his inability to defeat Muchen, but the fact that he couldn’t even graze Yue’er’s garments was a source of considerable frustration.","“Don’t be silly!” Pan Ning chided him gently.","“I’m not being silly! I just want to cultivate immortality!” Boqing stubbornly refused to back down, undeterred by his father’s mild scolding. Instead, he turned to his grandfather, tugging at his sleeve. “Grandfather, I want to cultivate immortality! I want to become very powerful!”","“Don’t be silly, child,” Pan’s father said, patting his grandson’s hand in an attempt to calm him.","Seeing that his grandfather wasn’t yielding, Boqing’s eyes darted towards his aunt, who possessed an ethereal beauty. He approached her, tilting his head slightly to look up at her – even so, she was still taller. He gazed at her with hopeful eyes. “Aunt Feng, can I cultivate immortality too? Can I become as powerful as Muchen and Yue’er?”"]},{"number":4655,"title":"Chapter 4655: Determined","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Pan's father and Pan Ning exchanged a quick glance before turning their expectant gazes back to Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu looked at the energetic little boy with the determined expression before her. A wave of fondness washed over her as she thought of her own brother's son. A gentle smile touched her lips as she asked, \"Do you even know what cultivating immortality entails?\"","\"Immortality makes you super strong! If I become an immortal, maybe I can finally beat Muchen!\" He glanced at Muchen and Yue'er, who were now approaching their mother, his mind still fixed on his long-standing rivalry. He was a boy, and older than Muchen, yet victory had always eluded him.","Feng Jiu's smile softened at the child's innocent ambition. She reached out and placed her hand gently on his head, then her eyebrows rose in surprise, and a soft laugh escaped her lips.","\"I didn't expect him to be a natural martial arts prodigy.\"","Hearing this unexpected assessment, Pan Ning couldn't help but lean forward, his voice filled with hope. \"Madam, my son...\"","\"He possesses the physique of a Mystical cultivator and has the potential to cultivate. Moreover, his bones and muscles are exceptionally well-suited,\" Feng Jiu explained with a warm smile.","\"Then, then, then...\" Pan's father stammered, overcome with a sudden rush of nervous excitement, rendering him momentarily speechless.","\"Aunt Feng, then can I cultivate with Yue'er and Muchen?\" Boqing's eyes sparkled with anticipation, his little face beaming with excitement.","Feng Jiu smiled thoughtfully. \"Their training regimen wouldn't be suitable for you. However, if you are truly determined to step onto the path of immortality, I can find a good place for you to learn.\" As she spoke, her gaze shifted to Pan Ning and Pan's father, who stood anxiously beside her.","She didn't need to elaborate. Pan Ning immediately understood the implications. \"If you are willing to send my son to train to become an immortal, the Pan family will be eternally in your debt,\" he said earnestly, standing up and bowing deeply.","\"Yes, yes, yes,\" Pan's father echoed fervently.","Seeing their eagerness, Feng Jiu's expression turned slightly more serious. \"Do you both understand that the world of immortality can also be incredibly cruel? Simply entering it doesn't guarantee a safe and prosperous life. If he chooses to remain in the mortal realm, I believe your Pan family is destined for a life of comfort and influence. But if he ventures into the world of cultivation, he would have to start from the very bottom. There's a real possibility that before he even has a chance to grow strong, he could be crushed by others and perish in the constant struggles. Would you still want him to take such a risk and enter the cultivation world?\"","Her words hung in the air, causing Pan's father and Pan Ning to fall into a thoughtful silence. Perhaps they had some vague understanding of the dangers, but having the stark reality laid out before them forced them to confront the weight of their potential decision.","If they allowed Boqing to go with Feng Jiu to the cultivation realm, and if he were to thrive and achieve greatness, their Pan family would become a lineage with cultivators. Perhaps generations later, their descendants might even have opportunities to enter that realm because of Boqing's success. But the immediate reality was that Boqing was still so young – could they truly make such a profound and potentially perilous decision for him?","Boqing, however, seemed to have no such reservations. He looked from his grandfather to his father, and then finally declared with unwavering determination, \"I'm going, I'm going! I want to become very powerful!\"","\"Aunt Feng, can I go too?\" Bowen stepped forward, his eyes fixed on Feng Jiu with hopeful anticipation.","Feng Jiu turned her gaze to Bowen, reached out to briefly touch him, and then shook her head gently. \"You don't possess spiritual roots, nor are you a Mystical cultivator. You cannot cultivate immortality; your path lies in the mortal realm.\" In the mortal world, children born with innate spiritual roots were exceedingly rare, so it was not entirely surprising that Bowen lacked the necessary foundation for cultivation.","Bowen's shoulders slumped with disappointment, and he quietly stepped aside, a clear look of envy in his eyes as he glanced back at Boqing."]},{"number":4656,"title":"Chapter 4656: Lonely","paragraphs":["\"Mother, let's take Boqing with us! We can practice together and grow up together,\" Yue'er suggested with a bright smile. Then, a thoughtful expression crossed her face as she looked at Boqing, then at Pan Ning, and finally asked with a touch of concern, \"Boqing, are you sure you can bear to leave your father and mother? If you come with us, you won't be able to see them anymore. What will you do?\"","Hearing this, Boqing's initial excitement seemed to falter, his expression becoming momentarily blank. He turned to his father, his brow furrowed as he muttered, \"I won't see them anymore? Then, when I grow up, can't I come back?\"","Feng Jiu smiled reassuringly. \"Yes, when you are strong enough, you can naturally come back.\"","Boqing turned back to his father, his small face now etched with seriousness. \"Father, when I grow up and become very powerful, I will come back to see you.\"","Hearing his son's earnest words, Pan Ning felt a complex mix of emotions stir within him, which ultimately settled into a soft sigh of acceptance. He bowed solemnly to Feng Jiu. \"Madam, please take Boqing with you! Whether it leads to good fortune or hardship, it will depend on his own destiny.\"","\"Let him follow us when we leave! Don't worry, I will find a good place for him,\" Feng Jiu replied with a reassuring smile, offering no further explanation. Her earlier questions had simply been to gauge their willingness. Now that the decision was made, she, who possessed the ability to take the child away, would naturally ensure he found a suitable environment to learn and grow safely.","With the matter settled, the Pan family discussed the arrangements discreetly, keeping the news confined to a few key members.","Following Feng Jiu's instructions, shortly after their departure, the Pan family was to spread the word that Boqing had succumbed to a sudden illness. She wanted them to act as if Pan Boqing had never existed. For the Pan family, this complete disappearance was the only way to guarantee their long-term safety.","In the subsequent days, once Pan Hong was able to stand for short periods, Feng Jiu bid farewell to the Pan family. Their arrival had caused a significant stir, but their departure was quiet and unceremonious.","Boqing's mother, Pan Ning's wife, watched her son follow the departing figures, her heart heavy with a mixture of hope and sorrow. Overwhelmed by the unknown future, she fainted into Pan Ning's arms, uncertain if she would ever see her child again.","Aboard the airship, Boqing sat huddled to one side, silently wiping away his tears and sniffing as their former home receded into the distance. A firm resolve solidified within him: he would definitely return in the future! He would come back to see his father and mother, as well as his great-grandfather and grandfather.","\"Brother Boqing, here's some spirit fruit for you. Don't cry,\" Yue'er offered him a brightly colored fruit.","\"A man should shed blood but not tears. It's shameful,\" Muchen said, his usual cool demeanor intact. However, he seemed to possess a quiet understanding of the ache his brother felt at leaving his parents. Therefore, although his delicate little face remained composed, his tone softened slightly as he added, \"My mother will find you a good master. When the time comes, you must train hard. When you grow up and become powerful, you can come back. There's no need to cry.\"","\"Woo woo, I just want to cry, don't mind me. I'll just cry without bleeding, woo woo...\" he rambled on childishly, wiping his eyes with the back of his hand and turning his back to Muchen.","Hao'er walked over silently and sat down beside Boqing, quietly gazing out at the vast expanse of the sky.","At the bow of the airship, Feng Jiu closed her eyes, resting on a plush couch. Hearing the children's quiet exchanges, she opened her eyes and glanced at them. A pang of reluctance tugged at her heart as she contemplated the day when her own children would eventually leave her side."]},{"number":4657,"title":"Chapter 4657: Not appropriate","paragraphs":["Chapter 4657: Not appropriate","Her gaze drifted towards the masked man who sat cross-legged in the corner of the airship. His breathing was even and deep, his eyes closed in quiet contemplation. A faint, shimmering barrier enveloped him, a subtle layer of protection around his still form.","Over the course of their journey, she had observed this ritual of his – finding a quiet space to sit in meditation. It wasn’t the focused intensity of martial arts practice; it seemed more akin to... his spirit having momentarily detached itself from his physical body.","Recalling his enigmatic words, that this vessel was not truly his own, that he had merely borrowed it to traverse realms, her suspicion solidified into a near certainty: his soul was indeed leaving his physical form during these trances.","Half a year. In just half a year, her children would follow him, embarking on their own paths.","A deep breath filled her lungs, then slowly escaped. After a brief pause, she straightened and beckoned to her three children. “Come here.”","Instantly, the three of them gravitated towards her. Yue’er nestled into her embrace, while Muchen and Hao’er stood attentively at her side.","“Mother, Mother, what kind of master are you going to find for Brother Boqing?” Yue’er asked, her small face tilted upwards from the comfort of her mother’s arms.","Feng Jiu gently stroked her daughter’s hair and smiled softly. “He is a Mystical Cultivator, so naturally, we will seek out a Mystical Cultivator as his master. Don’t worry, my little one! Mother will find him a good one.”","“Mother, Uncle is a Mystical Cultivator,” Muchen pointed out.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s eyebrows arched slightly. “You mean send him to your uncle and ask him to take him as a disciple?” Her initial thought had been to place Pan Boqing within a reputable sect. With a single word from her, he would undoubtedly receive exceptional training, regardless of the sect.","“Is that not a good idea?” Muchen asked, his young eyes filled with genuine confusion.","Feng Jiu shook her head gently. “It’s not that it’s a bad idea, Muchen, but it’s not entirely appropriate. Because he is your uncle, I can’t simply decide to make him his disciple. My plan is to send Boqing to a well-regarded sect and find him a dedicated master there. As long as he possesses talent and is willing to work hard, he will undoubtedly have a bright future.”","“Mm hmm,” Muchen nodded in understanding. He trusted his mother’s judgment, sensing that she had her own well-considered reasons and was surely acting in Boqing’s best interest. He didn’t press the matter further.","“Mother, where are we going now?” Hao’er inquired.","“We are going to the Xuanyuan Empire, to your grandfather’s place,” Feng Jiu replied. “Since I found you, I have only notified him of your return but haven’t yet taken you to see him. This time, we will stay there for a while.”","The thought of sending her children away soon made her cherish these moments even more. She would have fewer opportunities to see them in the future, so this visit would allow them to spend precious time with their grandfather. Moreover, she needed to find the right moment to tell him about Mo Ze.","Pushing those thoughts aside for the moment, she focused on her children. “My darlings, you’ve almost used up all the medicinal pills I gave you, haven’t you? Is there anything you need? Mother will find time to make some more for you.”","“Mother, Mother, we’ve run out of the medicinal pills for treating internal injuries! Last time, Big Brother didn’t even want to use them himself! He gave them all to us,” Yue’er said quickly, her voice filled with concern.","“Mother, we’re also running out of medicine for treating external injuries,” Muchen added.","Hearing their needs, Feng Jiu nodded reassuringly. “Yes, Mother knows. I will help you refine some more and distribute them to you later.” It seemed she would need to prepare a substantial supply of medicinal pills for them, knowing they would soon be venturing out on their own. “Later, Mother will also prepare a piece of protective clothing for each of you. Wear it always, and you won’t be easily injured.”"]},{"number":4658,"title":"Chapter 4658: Where is Mo Ze?","paragraphs":["Chapter 4658: Where is Mo Ze?","Feng Jiu retrieved a book that compiled various spirit medicines and presented it to Yue’er, saying, “This book not only meticulously records the medicinal properties of a wide array of spiritual remedies but also features clear and detailed illustrations for each one. Your mother has also included some personal notes and insightful observations within its pages. Keep it safe and look through it whenever you find the time.”","“Mother, Yue’er already has one,” the little girl responded, her expression a mixture of surprise and slight confusion. She indeed had a copy of her mother’s treasured medicine manual nestled within her spatial storage.","Feng Jiu offered a gentle smile and clarified, “Ah, but this one is different from the other. Please keep it nonetheless! These particular remedies are no longer of practical use to me. Don’t you harbor a keen interest in the study of medicine and the intricacies of poisons? Then, immerse yourself in more books and dedicate yourself to diligent study. Only through your own hands-on experimentation will you truly grasp the effects of each individual medicine.”","The little girl nodded her head in apparent understanding, then carefully accepted the offered book and beamed sweetly, “Thank you very much, Mother.”","Feng Jiu affectionately patted her daughter’s head. Subsequently, she retrieved other items from her spatial dimension, intending them for Hao’er and Muchen, with the foresight that they might prove beneficial in their future endeavors.","After imparting some instructions to the children, she rose and entered the cabin, leaving Leng Shuang to maintain a vigilant watch outside. Once inside, Feng Jiu retreated into her personal space to diligently refine medicinal pills specifically tailored for her children’s well-being.","Several days later, the elegant spaceship gracefully descended just outside the imposing palace gates of the Xuanyuan Empire. As the vessel touched down, the alert guards stationed at the palace entrance swiftly relayed news of their arrival within the imperial compound.","Upon hearing the news of Feng Jiu and her companions’ arrival, the Xuanyuan Monarch’s face broke into a wide smile of pure joy. He didn’t even deem it necessary to wait within the palace for them to be formally announced. Instead, he eagerly rushed out himself, making his way directly to the palace gates.","“Grandfather!” Yue’er exclaimed, her short legs carrying her swiftly towards the approaching Xuanyuan Monarch, her voice brimming with uncontainable excitement.","“Hahahaha, my precious granddaughter has arrived! Let Grandfather take a good look at how much you’ve grown,” the Xuanyuan Monarch chuckled warmly. He gently picked up the child, affectionately squeezed her chubby little hands, and tenderly stroked her small head, his happiness growing with each passing moment he gazed upon her.","“Good, good, you haven’t lost any weight at all. You’re nice and chubby, just as you should be, nice and chubby!” He declared happily, his gaze sweeping over the children who had returned safely, a profound sense of relief finally settling in his heart.","“Grandfather,” Hao’er and Muchen said in unison.","“Grandfather,” they repeated, stepping forward and bowing respectfully towards him. “We have returned.”","“Good, good, it is wonderful that you are back, truly wonderful that you are back,” he responded, nodding emphatically as tears began to well up in his eyes. He then turned his gaze towards Feng Jiu and said with heartfelt gratitude, “It is truly good of you to have brought the children back safely. Now that they are here, I can finally rest easy. You have truly worked tirelessly this time.”","As he spoke, his eyes briefly scanned the individuals accompanying Feng Jiu. He registered a slight surprise upon noticing that, alongside the familiar faces of her entourage, there was a masked man he did not recognize, as well as a stern-looking, black-clad bodyguard and a quiet little boy. Du Fan, Leng Hua, Leng Shuang, and the others were all present, but Mo Ze was conspicuously absent.","“Where is Mo Ze? Why did he not return with you?” He asked, a trace of concern in his voice.","“Father,” Feng Jiu called out softly, stepping forward to address him. “Let us go inside and talk properly!”","Hearing her words, the Xuanyuan Monarch paused for a brief moment, then chuckled good-naturedly. “Right, right, look at me! You have traveled all this way, and I am standing here asking you questions. Come, come, please follow me inside. Are you feeling hungry? I will instruct the imperial kitchen to prepare some food for you all, after which you can properly rest.”","The group then proceeded to enter the grand palace. As they arrived within its opulent walls, the Xuanyuan Monarch’s face remained illuminated with joy. He promptly instructed the royal chef to prepare a lavish meal and directed servants to arrange comfortable accommodations for their guests.","Later that evening, as everyone else retired to their respective quarters to rest after their journey, Feng Jiu quietly made her way to the Xuanyuan Monarch’s private palace."]},{"number":4659,"title":"Chapter 4659: Unable to return","paragraphs":["Chapter 4659: Unable to return","“Have a seat!” The Xuanyuan Monarch gestured towards a nearby seat and then inquired directly, “Did something happen to Mo Ze?” In truth, the moment he noticed his son was absent from their arrival and observed Feng Jiu’s evasiveness regarding his whereabouts, a trace of suspicion had taken root in his heart. However, he struggled to comprehend what could possibly pose a threat to someone of Mo Ze’s considerable strength.","Feng Jiu nodded somberly, settled onto a chair, and began to explain, “Father, before we successfully located the children, Mo Ze was involved in an accident. It occurred during his advancement.”","“Advancement?” The Xuanyuan Monarch’s heart sank when he heard her words. Advancement in cultivation was never a trivial matter, often fraught with peril.","“This is what happened...” Feng Jiu told him in detail the events of that fateful day. Finally, she concluded, “My brother has returned to the realm under Mo Ze’s jurisdiction to conduct a thorough investigation. On the day of Mo Ze’s accident, there was significant upheaval within that realm, yet his spiritual consciousness did not completely dissipate. Therefore, we believe that he is still alive, but his current location remains unknown to us.”","Upon hearing this explanation, the Xuanyuan Monarch let out a soft sigh, tinged with worry. “The sound of thunder did reach our ears here at that time,” he recalled, “but it was too distant, and consequently, we received no specific news and remained unaware that something had befallen him.”","He fixed a heavy gaze upon Feng Jiu and said with grave concern, “Under the onslaught of such a formidable lightning tribulation, who would dare to assert that he remains alive? Even if a fragment of his spiritual consciousness persists, it may merely be a matter of time before it too fades. The sheer power of such a tribulation is immense; even someone as strong as he might not have been able to withstand it entirely!”","“No,” Feng Jiu stated firmly, her voice unwavering. “I do not believe he is dead, and I refuse to believe that he no longer exists in this world. I would rather cling to the hope that he is simply recovering from his injuries in some secluded place.”","“He is my son,” the Xuanyuan Monarch said, his voice softening with affection. “How could I not wish for him to be alive? My concern lies in the possibility that you are nurturing too much hope, which could lead to an even more devastating blow in the future. It is good to have hope, but you must also prepare yourself mentally for other possibilities. You cannot allow yourself to be completely shattered if your hopes are ultimately unfulfilled, lest your very beliefs crumble.”","Feng Jiu remained silent for a moment, offering no immediate response. She understood that his words stemmed from a place of love and a desire to shield her from potential future pain. However, she was unwilling to accept his implied conclusion and steadfastly refused to believe that Mo Ze was no longer alive. In her heart, he was still out there.","The Xuanyuan Monarch decided to steer the conversation away from this sensitive topic. “The children are still unaware of this, aren’t they?” he asked gently. “Have you considered how you will tell them?”","“I haven’t yet figured out the best way to break the news to them,” Feng Jiu admitted, a hint of worry lacing her tone. “They are still young, yet they possess a remarkable sensitivity. If I tell them, I fear their young hearts will be unable to bear such sorrow.”","Hearing her apprehension, he sighed softly and offered a different perspective. “The children are stronger than you might think. You can be honest with them. They are already quite perceptive and will likely understand more than you realize.”","“Father,” Feng Jiu said, shifting the focus of their conversation slightly, “actually, I came here to discuss something else entirely.” She looked directly at him as she spoke.","“Yes, please go ahead. I am listening. What is it?” He prompted.","Feng Jiu reached out and discreetly cast a soundproof barrier around them before continuing, “Mo Ze is in grave danger because someone within the Immortal Realm is actively trying to harm us. Therefore, I am planning to send the three children away for their safety. The masked man who accompanied us today is a powerful being from the Immortal Realm. He is...”","She carefully and thoroughly explained the gravity of their situation to him, detailing the potential threats and outlining her reasoning behind this difficult decision, hoping that he would understand and support her plan.","“You mean you intend to send all three children to the Immortal Realm?” the Xuanyuan Monarch asked, his brow furrowing in concern. “If you do that, will they even be able to return?”"]},{"number":4660,"title":"Chapter 4660: I’ll be waiting","paragraphs":["Chapter 4660: I’ll be waiting","“I am not entirely certain about the specific circumstances in the Immortal Realm at this moment, but for the time being, yes, that is the plan,” she affirmed with a nod.","“Since you lack complete knowledge of the situation there, how can you be absolutely sure that sending the children up there will guarantee their safe upbringing? How can you be certain that this individual, who doesn’t even disclose his name to you, will genuinely protect them?” The Xuanyuan Monarch pressed, his concern evident in his unwavering frown.","Hearing Feng Jiu’s admission of uncertainty only deepened his apprehension.","“I have been observing him for a period and my intuition tells me that he is worthy of trust.” Feng Jiu stated with conviction. “Besides, there is an additional matter concerning Yue’er that I need to discuss.”","Within the confines of the soundproof barrier, their conversation remained private, unheard by anyone outside the palace walls. Meanwhile, as evening descended, the children were enjoying themselves, exploring the unfamiliar grandeur of the imperial residence. Boqing, who had never before witnessed such splendor, was particularly enthralled.","“It is so incredibly beautiful here!” Boqing exclaimed in wide-eyed amazement to Muchen. “Your grandfather is actually the Monarch! That is so unbelievably amazing!” He had never imagined that his new friends held such an esteemed status.","Muchen cast a sidelong glance at Boqing and stated matter-of-factly, “Of course, my grandfather is amazing, but my father and mother are even more so. They are Sovereign Rulers, far more powerful than even the Monarch. In the future, I too will become as powerful as my father and mother, so you won’t stand a chance against me.”","“I don’t believe you,” Boqing retorted, unconvinced. “I will also become incredibly powerful in the future. I will definitely defeat you!”","“Brother Boqing, I will take you to see the spirit beasts that are kept within the palace grounds,” Yue’er interjected, stepping forward and gently taking his hand. “My grandfather also has immortal cranes that can fly! I will show them to you.”","“Really? That’s fantastic! Let’s go see them right now!” Upon hearing this, Boqing’s eyes sparkled with excitement, and his face lit up with pure joy, instantly forgetting their previous playful disagreement.","It could almost be said that, aside from the initial pangs of homesickness and the occasional secret tears shed during the first day or two away from his own family, Boqing no longer succumbed to sadness when thinking of his parents. Instead, he was increasingly captivated by the novel and fascinating experiences that surrounded him.","During their stay, he had already encountered numerous strange and wonderful sights, and he eagerly anticipated the possibility of seeing and learning even more in the days to come.","Leng Hua and Leng Shuang, maintaining their ever-vigilant watch, observed the children heading towards the Spirit Beast Garden and followed discreetly behind. Although the palace grounds were considered secure and devoid of any immediate threats akin to the Devil Lord, they remained close by, prepared to offer protection should any unforeseen circumstances arise.","After a brief two-day stay within the palace, Feng Jiu instructed Du Fan to escort Boqing to the sect where she, Ye Jing, and her brother had once honed their cultivation skills. This particular sect offered training not only in spiritual cultivation but also in mystical arts. After careful consideration, she had concluded that sending Boqing there offered the most promising path for his future development.","On the day of their departure, Feng Jiu watched as the children bid farewell, a pang of melancholy tugging at her heart. She knew that this parting might signify a long separation, making future reunions difficult.","“When you arrive there, you must focus diligently on your cultivation and avoid unnecessary conflicts with others. If you find yourself facing an opponent you cannot defeat, remember to retreat swiftly,” Muchen instructed Boqing stiffly, his young eyes tinged with red.","“Woo woo woo, I understand. I will miss you all dearly. When I become strong, I will come back to find you and challenge you to a fight, and this time, I will definitely win,” Boqing sniffled, wiping away his tears as he spoke.","Muchen’s mouth twitched slightly. He had been feeling a touch sentimental himself, but Boqing’s tearful declaration shifted his emotions to a more subtle place. He could only manage a somewhat rigid nod and a simple, “I will be waiting.”","“Brother Boqing, please take good care of yourself. I selected this dagger from Grandfather’s treasure chest, and I want to give it to you for self-defense,” Yue’er said earnestly, placing a small dagger into his hands."]},{"number":4661,"title":"Chapter 4661: Speaking up","paragraphs":["Chapter 4661: Speaking up","Clutching the dagger tightly, Boqing wiped away the last of his tears and nodded earnestly. “Yes, I understand. I will take very good care of myself. You all take care too, and don’t get lost again!”","“Alright, it’s getting late, we should be going!” Du Fan stepped forward and gave Boqing a reassuring pat on the shoulder. He then turned to Feng Jiu and said, “Master, I will escort him to the sect first and return after settling things there.”","“Alright, go ahead!” Feng Jiu nodded in acknowledgment, watching as Du Fan retrieved his flying artifact and departed with Seventeen and Boqing. Only then did she turn her attention to her three children.","“Let’s head back to the Palace now! Let’s spend some time with your Grandfather,” Feng Jiu said gently, patting each of them on the head.","The three children followed her inside. Yue’er, her small brow furrowed with concern, asked, “Mother, will we ever see Boqing again?”","Feng Jiu held her daughter’s hand as they walked, her gaze fixed on the path ahead. “Nothing in this world lasts forever, my dear. When fate allows, things will come together, and when it doesn’t, they won’t. We must simply let things unfold naturally and not try to force what isn’t meant to be.”","The three children listened quietly, absorbing her words. After a thoughtful pause, they nodded in unison and said, “Yes, Mother, we understand.”","“Mother, where is Father?” Muchen asked, looking up at her with earnest eyes. “You haven’t told us where Father has gone. Mother, has something happened to him?”","Feng Jiu’s steps faltered momentarily, and a fleeting shadow crossed her face. She lowered her gaze, looked at her son beside her, and offered him a gentle smile. Reaching out, she softly ruffled his hair. Noticing that Hao’er and Yue’er were also looking at her expectantly, as if waiting for her answer, she directed her gaze towards a palace fence not far in the distance and said, “Let’s go over there! I will tell you everything.”","The three children followed her to the railing. As she sat down, they mirrored her action and settled beside her. All three pairs of eyes were fixed on her, waiting patiently for her to speak.","“Some time ago, the blood curse that afflicted you was weakened, and it was indeed connected to your father. Something unexpected occurred while he was undergoing an advancement in his cultivation, and at present, we do not know his exact whereabouts. However, please do not worry too much; he will be alright. Perhaps he is simply resting and recuperating in a secluded place. Once he has recovered, he will undoubtedly return to find us.”","Feng Jiu offered them only a broad explanation, carefully omitting the perilous nature of the situation. She alone understood the true extent of the danger, but she did not want her children to dwell on it or become excessively worried. Therefore, she provided them with only a general overview.","“Even Mother doesn’t know where Father is?” Yue’er asked, her brow furrowed with worry as she looked up at her mother.","Feng Jiu smiled reassuringly, gently stroking her daughter’s head. “Your father is incredibly powerful, so there is no need to fret too much about him. However, Mother has something else important to tell the three of you.”","“Mother, what is it?” Hao’er inquired.","“In the near future, Mother will be sending you to different places to seek out skilled masters to train with. Therefore, during this time, you must remember everything that Mother teaches you. It is possible that you will need this knowledge in the future.”","“Mother is sending us away?” Yue’er asked hurriedly, her small hands clutching tightly at her mother’s sleeves. “Where are you sending us? We don’t want to find other masters; we only want to cultivate with Mother.”","“Mother, I don’t want to leave you either,” Muchen added, his voice reflecting his reluctance. “I want to stay here with you.”","“Mother, I also want to stay with you,” Hao’er echoed, looking up at her with pleading eyes. “I don’t want to leave you.”"]},{"number":4662,"title":"Chapter 4662: Be careful","paragraphs":["Chapter 4662: Be careful","Listening to the children’s words, Feng Jiu felt a pang of bitterness in her heart. She looked at them and smiled faintly, saying, “You must listen to your mother. Whatever your mother does is for your own good.”","The three children listened, exchanged glances, and then fell silent.","“Alright, I’ll take you to Grandfather. You must keep him company. Your mother will go back and refine medicinal pills for you.” She took the children by the hand and walked towards the main hall. After sending them there, she asked Leng Hua to look after them, then entered her room and with a thought, flashed into her private dimension.","About a month later, Du Fan returned. Upon arriving at the palace, he first went to Feng Jiu to report that he had successfully sent Bo Qing to the sect and Seventeen to the Fengwei camp for rigorous training.","As for Luo Yu, Qin Xin, and the others, he had instructed them to manage affairs at their respective bases, and therefore, they did not accompany him on this trip.","“Master, Luo Yu and the others are diligently handling all other matters. There are no significant incidents occurring anywhere at the moment. You can rest assured that everything is proceeding as usual,” Du Fan stated as he carefully poured Feng Jiu a cup of freshly brewed tea.","Feng Jiu had just finished refining a large batch of medicinal pills, and the faint scent of various herbs clung to her clothes. She appeared slightly weary, so she gratefully took a sip of the warm tea before responding, “With them diligently watching over things, I am naturally at ease. We have been here for almost a month, and I am planning to take the three children out to experience the outside world for the remainder of our stay. You should return and rest for now. Pack your belongings and prepare for our departure tomorrow.”","“Yes, Master,” Du Fan replied respectfully, bowing slightly before taking his leave.","“Master, I have prepared your bath water. Would you like to bathe first?” Leng Shuang inquired softly as she approached.","“Mm,” Feng Jiu replied, standing up and gently rubbing her shoulders to ease the lingering tension. “Where did the children go to play?”","“They are currently practicing martial arts with Leng Hua at the training ground,” Leng Shuang informed her.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu nodded in understanding and went to take a bath, eager to wash away her fatigue and find some much-needed relaxation.","At the martial arts training ground, Muchen and Muyue were engaged in a spirited competition. They focused on unarmed combat, and on several occasions, Muchen effortlessly managed to throw Yue’er to the ground.","However, the surface of the martial arts training ground was not hard stone, but rather covered with a thick layer of fine sand, ensuring that falls were more of an inconvenience than a source of injury. Despite this, the little girl found herself repeatedly landing in the sand, and her youthful temper began to simmer.","“I refuse to believe that I can’t knock my brother down!” Yue’er declared with determination, her gaze fixed on her brother who stood firmly in a stable horse stance. A mischievous glint flashed by her eyes, and revealed a sly smile. In the next instant, she charged forward, and instead of swinging her small fists in attack, she used her entire small body to ram into him with surprising force.","Muchen was caught off guard when he saw his younger sister charging towards him with her head lowered like a tiny calf. He quickly reached out to block her small head, but the determined little girl used all her might and actually managed to knock him off balance and onto the soft sand.","“Hahahaha, brother fell down too!” Yue’er exclaimed gleefully. Instead of getting up, she lay on top of Muchen, waving her arms triumphantly and shouting with unrestrained joy.","Not far away, Hao’er, who was undergoing his own training with Leng Hua, heard the commotion and turned to observe. He saw his younger brother and sister playfully wrestling in the sand. A rare, gentle smile touched his usually serious face at the sight.","However, just at that moment, his expression abruptly changed. The fine sand on the ground suddenly began to swirl rapidly, coalescing and taking the menacing form of a sand creature that lunged directly towards the unsuspecting Muchen and Muyue.","“Be careful!”"]},{"number":4663,"title":"Chapter 4663: I’ll go in","paragraphs":["Chapter 4663: I'll go in","Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Almost at the same time he shouted, Leng Hua's expression changed, and he immediately rushed towards Muchen and Muyue. However, the sand man formed from the fine sand rushed towards the two children at an extremely fast speed.","\"Quick, get out of the way!\" Leng Hua shouted loudly, while at the same time, he gathered the wind in his palm and sent out a wind blade.","\"Whoosh! Bang!\"","A sharp whistling sound echoed as the wind blade sliced through the air, trailing a fierce gust of wind. Immediately afterward, the palm strike struck the sand-formed figure with precision, causing it to shatter into a cloud of sand. A yellow talisman also drifted down to the ground.","Seeing this, Leng Hua breathed a sigh of relief, and even Hao'er, who had run over, let out a slight sigh of relief. The two little guys lying on the ground also recovered from their stupor and quickly stood up, patting the fine sand off their bodies.","But just then, the talisman on the ground suddenly exploded with a bang and scattered into pieces. At the moment of the explosion, the fine sand on the martial arts training ground swirled, and a wall of sand rose up from nowhere, surrounding them all.","\"No!\"","Leng Hua breathed a sigh of relief, but then saw the sudden change. He immediately took out an item from his spatial ring and crushed it, then gathered his qi and rushed towards the two children, shouting, \"Hao'er, come quickly!\"","Hao'er had the strength of a Golden Core cultivator and was quick to react, so Leng Hua's first thought was to save Muchen and Muyue. After all, their combat strength was limited, and if they really encountered danger, they would not be able to protect themselves.","\"Whoosh! Whoosh!\"","The wind and sand swirled, and the fine sand on the ground was whipped up to form a wall of sand that surrounded the group. In the middle, some of the fine sand quickly coalesced into human shapes and attacked Muchen and Muyue.","The two little ones had already recovered from their shock and saw the human-shaped killers formed from the fine sand. Muchen immediately pulled his sister and ran towards Leng Hua.","\"Sister, hurry!\"","The sudden change on this side caused the guards to quickly report it. Feng Jiu, who was bathing with her eyes closed, suddenly felt as if she had sensed something. She immediately gathered her energy and rose up, splashing water everywhere. At the same time, she quickly put on her undergarments and her outer robe, not even bothering to tie the sash, and rushed outside.","Leng Shuang, who was standing guard outside, didn't understand what was going on, but when she saw her master rushing out while tying her sash, she knew that something was wrong. She immediately gathered her energy and followed.","The masked man in the courtyard next door also seemed to sense something was wrong. Under his mask, his eyebrows furrowed slightly, and his closed eyes suddenly opened. He gathered his energy and rushed outside.","The Xuanyuan Monarch rushed over after hearing the report from his guards, but when he arrived at the training ground, he saw that it had been sealed off. The fine sand that had been spread on the ground had formed four walls that surrounded the entire training ground, making it impossible to see inside. He could only feel a powerful aura surging within.","\"Hao'er! Chen'er! Yue'er!\"","Xuanyuan Monarch shouted, but he couldn't hear any voices from inside, only the sound of wind and sand swirling around. So, he gathered the spirit energy in his body and prepared to rush in to take a look, but just as he did, a hand grabbed his shoulder. Before he could see who it was, he heard Feng Jiu's voice.","\"Father, I'll go in.\" As Feng Jiu spoke, she pushed him away with her hand."]},{"number":4664,"title":"Chapter 4664: They’ve started","paragraphs":["Chapter 4664: They've started","Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","As the Xuanyuan Monarch was pushed back, he saw a red figure dart forward and disappear into the sand wall in the blink of an eye.","Seeing that it was Feng Jiu, he did not go in, but took a step back and waited. Just then, the masked man also arrived, but he did not go in. Instead, he stood beside him, quietly watching the scene in front of him, a thoughtful look in his eyes.","In the middle of the training ground, inside the sand wall, Leng Hua destroyed the human-shaped fine sand, but those human-shaped fine sand did not have life. When struck, they scattered to the ground, forming a pile of loose sand. Yet in the next moment, the loose sand gathered again, reforming into a human shape and charging toward them. This repeated endlessly. Despite his considerable strength, he could not block the sand figures while also protecting the two children.","Seeing four or five sand figures surrounding the two children, Leng Hua and Hao'er immediately shouted, \"Quick, get out of the way! Run!\"","The two of them struck out with their palms, trying to destroy the sand figures, but unexpectedly, after surrounding the two children, the sand figures scattered into a pile of sand on the ground, then quickly piled up again and buried the two children.","\"Ah!\"","The wind and sand swirled and covered the two children, seemingly wanting to bury them alive. Yue'er, who had never encountered such a situation before, cried out in alarm and instinctively hugged her head and crouched down.","Seeing this, Muchen hurriedly used his small body to shield his sister. Just when they thought they would surely be buried alive, they heard a familiar and reassuring voice.","\"Draw a prison on the ground! Break it!\"","The moment Feng Jiu's voice rang out, the three children looked towards the source of the voice and saw their mother not far away, dressed in a red robe, her exquisite face covered with a cold expression. Her hands formed a strange mark, and she held a talisman between her fingers. As the mark in her hand fell, the talisman was burned by the flames rising from her fingertips.","As she uttered the word \"break,\" the ground seemed to be struck by a stone, sending out circles of powerful energy. In that instant, the sand swirling around them fell to the ground, and the fine sand that had formed into human shapes scattered, revealing fragments of talismans among the sand.","\"Mother!\"","\"Mother!\"","\"Mother!\"","The three children cheered joyfully and ran towards her. The moment they saw her, they forgot their fear and were filled with joy and peace.","Feng Jiu glanced around and saw that the sandstorm had calmed down. She then looked at the three children and asked, \"Are you alright? Are you hurt?\"","\"Mother, we're not hurt, but Mother, what were those things just now? Why did the sand turn into people?\" Hao'er asked.","\"Talismans.\" The masked man slowly walked forward, glanced at the people standing in the training ground, then fixed his gaze on Feng Jiu.","The masked man looked at Feng Jiu and said in a deep voice, \"They've already started to go after you. You don't have much time left.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu pursed her lips, glanced at him, then looked at the three children and said, \"It's alright, Mother is here, don't worry.\""]},{"number":4665,"title":"Chapter 4665: Safety","paragraphs":["She looked at the talismans scattered on the fine sand, waved her hand, and a flame shot across, burning all the talisman fragments to ashes.","\"What’s going on? Who used talismans against you?\" The Xuanyuan Monarch stepped forward and asked, looking at the children who were unharmed, he secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","\"Father, don’t worry, everything is alright. I’ll take the children back to rest first, and I’ll come find you in a moment.\" Feng Jiu looked at him and said.","Hearing this, the Xuanyuan Monarch nodded, \"Alright, you go ahead!\" He watched them walk towards the side hall where they would rest, then sighed lightly, shook his head, and walked back with his hands behind his back.","After Feng Jiu sent the three children back to their rooms and told them to take a bath first, she turned to Leng Hua and asked, \"Are you alright?\"","\"I’m fine.\" Leng Hua said apologetically, \"I just didn’t protect the three Young Masters well.\"","\"You did very well. Keep an eye on them! Clean up a bit, we’ll leave tomorrow,\" Feng Jiu instructed, then asked Leng Shuang to stay behind. Seeing the masked man sitting in the courtyard, she said, \"I’m going to say goodbye to my father.\"","With a heart heavy, Feng Jiu went to the main hall, where Mo Ze’s father was already waiting. Seeing her come in, he motioned for her to sit down.","Feng Jiu sat down and said, \"Father, I’m planning to leave with the children tomorrow.\"","Hearing this, the Xuanyuan Monarch hesitated and asked, \"You’re leaving? Is it because of what happened today?\"","\"I was already planning to leave. I wanted to take the children out to see more of the world, but I didn’t expect today’s events to happen, so I’m leaving tomorrow,\" she had originally planned to leave tomorrow, but now that this had happened, she couldn’t stay here any longer, for fear of causing trouble for him or even the empire.","\"Then where are you going? Do you have a destination?\" he asked, feeling a pang of sadness at the thought of his three grandsons leaving.","Feng Jiu paused for a moment and said, \"We still need to go above. As for the rest, we haven’t decided yet. Half a year is almost up, so I might ask the children to leave with their master early.\"","\"Alas! I understand. Go now! Take good care of yourselves. Nothing is more important than safety. No matter where you go, if you have the chance in the future, bring the children back to see me. If you can’t come back, remember to send me a message to let me know that you are all safe,\" he sighed softly, his words betraying his loneliness.","Feng Jiu moved her lips, but didn’t know what to say. In the end, she just nodded and said, \"I will.\" She took some medicinal pills out of her space and said, \"Father, keep these medicinal pills with you just in case. If you encounter any unsolvable problems or difficulties in the future, you can send a message to my brother and ask him to come and help.\"","He didn’t refuse and took the pills directly, replying, \"Alright, I understand.\"","Feng Jiu stood up, looked at him deeply, and said, \"Father, parting is the saddest thing. You don’t need to see us off tomorrow morning.\"","Hearing this, his heart ached, and he looked at her and said, \"All right, take good care of yourselves. Don’t worry too much about us. We are all fine here. Just take care of yourselves.\"","After talking for a while, Feng Jiu turned and left. The Xuanyuan Monarch watched her receding figure and said silently in his heart, \"Safety is the most important thing. You must grow up safely...\""]},{"number":4666,"title":"Chapter 4666: Determined","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, Feng Jiu and her party left swiftly on an airship. The Xuanyuan Monarch did not see them off, but stood on high ground and watched from afar as their airship slowly rose until they disappeared into the clouds. Only then did he turn away and slowly walk back...","At the bow of the airship, Feng Jiu set up a soundproof barrier and looked at the masked man, saying, \"Didn’t you say they couldn’t come down? Then how did they use talisman techniques to summon assassins?\"","The masked man leaned against the side, looking more relaxed than Feng Jiu. He glanced at her, then looked at the clouds outside the spaceship and said, \"They can’t come down, but that doesn’t mean they can’t do anything. What’s more, they’ve dealt with Xuanyuan Mo Ze, so they won’t let you live. It’s only a matter of time before they strike again. And now that they’ve made their move, there’s no way they’ll stop.\"","He paused for a moment, then said casually, \"It seems that the rest of the journey won’t be too boring.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s eyes flashed and she said, \"Shouldn’t you tell me what’s going on up there?\"","\"What should I tell you? That your current strength is still no match for those people up there, who can crush you like an insect at any moment? Or that those powerful people up there want to kill you, and you’re going to face a life-threatening situation from now on?\"","He glanced at Feng Jiu, gently swaying the wine cup in his hand, with a half-smile on his lips, \"I heard that you are the destined one, who will break through the heavens, to be the Sovereign of the world? Perhaps those who claim to know the past and present have prophesied such things, but in the eyes of those above, those deemed to possess such a destiny are doomed to suffer countless hardships, and may even perish at any moment. Even if you somehow manage to grow strong, before you can ever reach their level, they will have countless opportunities to eliminate you and ensure your survival is impossible.\"","Feng Jiu pursed her lips, frowned slightly, and said in a faint voice, \"I don’t want to know those things. I just want to know how I can find my enemies. Also, is ascension the only way to see those powerful beings you spoke of? What kind of place is this Nine Heavens Immortal Realm you mentioned?\"","Hearing this, he smiled slightly and shook his head: \"I can’t tell you that because it’s highly likely that you won’t be able to ascend in this lifetime. You must know that in order to ascend and transform into an immortal body, you must first endure 9981 lightning tribulations before you can break through the sky and ascend to immortality. Since the powerful beings above are trying to destroy you, how could they let you pass through those 9981 lightning tribulations?\"","He smiled and said, \"We’ll talk about these things when you have the chance to ascend to immortality in the future!\" With that, he drank the wine in his cup in one gulp, then poured it onto the deck, propped his head up with one hand, closed his eyes, and rested there, clearly not wanting to say any more to Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu glanced at him, pursed her lips, and didn’t say anything else. She just waved her hand to remove the sound barrier, stood up, and walked around a bit.","She came to the front of the airship and watched it fly through the clouds, watched the wind and clouds brush against the ship, and looked at the endless sky ahead. She couldn’t help but glance back at the three children, her mind made up.","No matter what lies ahead, she would keep going! Anyone who dared to stand in her way would be destroyed!"]},{"number":4667,"title":"Chapter 4667: Vortex","paragraphs":["Chapter 4667: Vortex","Two days later, the airship glided through the sky. There was a tranquil atmosphere, where they were either deeply engrossed in cultivation or peacefully resting.","However, this serene scene was abruptly disrupted as the weather above took a turn for the worse, darkening ominously. Initially, a fierce wind howled, causing the airship to sway gently. This was soon followed by a fine rain that descended from the heavens like a shower of needles.","“Why did it suddenly rain?” Du Fan exclaimed, his eyes snapping open as he registered the unexpected change in the sky. Startled by the sight of the needle-like rain, he quickly rose to his feet.","A protective barrier of spiritual energy enveloped the airship, effectively shielding it from the elements. Nevertheless, Du Fan made his way to the bow, his gaze fixed on the unusual weather patterns, keenly observing for any potential anomalies.","“What’s wrong? Is something amiss?” Leng Hua inquired, approaching Du Fan, his eyes also fixed on the now-rainy sky. Noticing the increasingly dark conditions, he voiced his concern: “Should we consider finding a place to land for the time being?”","“Isn’t Master currently refining medicinal pills within the spatial dimension? He’s likely unable to leave at the moment,” Du Fan replied, his attention still directed towards the increasingly oppressive atmosphere of the sky.","“If Master is unable to exit the spatial dimension, then we must take control of the airship and initiate a landing ourselves. It would be prudent to halt our journey temporarily. Look, the wind is intensifying, and the rain is becoming heavier. The airship will inevitably become unstable and begin to shake during flight,” Leng Hua asserted, convinced of the necessity to find a safe place to anchor.","Upon hearing this, Du Fan nodded in agreement. “Alright, let me ascertain our current location.” With these words, he moved to the side of the airship and peered down at the swirling clouds below, extending his divine sense to probe the terrain beneath.","“Du Fan! Quickly! Maneuver the airship downwards and land!” Leng Hua’s voice suddenly held a sharp note of alarm, causing Du Fan, who was focused on his downward probe, to snap his attention back.","“What is it?”","Du Fan turned to see a noticeable shift in Leng Hua’s expression. Following his gaze, Du Fan’s eyes widened in disbelief. Approximately ten meters ahead of their airship, a massive swirling vortex had materialized in the sky. The vortex was enormous and utterly black, emitting a loud whooshing sound that cut through the wind and rain, as if possessing a powerful suction force that was actively drawing their airship towards it. Even the airship, which had been moving at a leisurely pace, suddenly lurched forward with alarming speed.","“No! Quick, call our Master!”","Du Fan cried out, urgently instructing Leng Hua to contact their Master. Simultaneously, he swiftly mobilized his spiritual energy in a desperate attempt to regain control of the airship, initiating a sharp turn while simultaneously attempting a rapid descent.","However, they had severely underestimated the sheer power of the vortex. Despite Du Fan’s frantic efforts to steer the airship downwards, the suction generated by the swirling mass remained terrifyingly potent, as if invisible hands within the vortex were relentlessly pulling them inward. The airship became completely unmanageable, hurtling uncontrollably towards the dark abyss.","Furthermore, the relentless suction caused the airship to tilt precariously to one side. Even the three children who were diligently cultivating in a nearby cabin were jolted by the violent movement and instinctively rushed out to ascertain the cause of the disturbance.","“Get back inside! Do not come out!” Leng Shuang commanded firmly, physically pushing them back into the cabin, fearing for their safety amidst the unfolding crisis.","Consequently, the three children were forced back into the cabin by Leng Shuang after barely stepping out. The violent swaying of the airship caused them to lose their balance and fall to the floor.","“Master! Master!”","Leng Hua anxiously pounded on Feng Jiu’s cabin door, his worried gaze darting back towards the rapidly approaching vortex. However, just as he felt the latch of his master’s door begin to turn, he witnessed the entire airship being violently engulfed by the dark, swirling vortex..."]},{"number":4668,"title":"Chapter 4668: Bizarre","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu was originally refining medicinal pills in her space. Just as she had finished refining a batch of pills and was about to open the furnace, she heard Leng Hua’s anxious cries and the sound of someone banging on the door. She immediately rushed out, but upon opening the cabin door, she was met with disorienting darkness and a world spinning around her. She couldn’t even stand steadily and swayed with the violent shaking of the ship.","In that instant, she felt an immense force tugging at the airship, causing it to lose all stability before being violently sucked into something. A wave of dizziness washed over her, followed by the sharp crack of the airship’s protective barrier shattering. The vessel then plummeted downwards as if it had been dropped from an extreme height.","\"No! Du Fan, Leng Shuang, quickly follow me and stabilize the airship! Leng Hua, take care of the three children and do not let them come out!\" Feng Jiu shouted without hesitation. Recognizing the gravity of the situation, she swiftly gathered her spiritual energy and propelled herself out of the airship, moving rapidly beneath it to try and counteract its descent.","The moment her command rang out, Du Fan and Leng Shuang reacted with equal speed. They each took hold of one of the three corners of the plummeting airship. However, even with their combined spiritual energy reinforcing the vessel, they struggled against the overwhelming force that was throwing it around. Consequently, as the airship crashed downwards, they could only manage to decelerate its fall and minimize the extent of the damage.","Bang, bang, bang!","The airship slammed onto the ground with a jarring impact but did not come to an immediate stop. Instead, it skidded for approximately ten metres before colliding with several trees, finally grinding to a halt after scraping against the sand and gravel.","Once the dust settled and the airship was still, Feng Jiu, Du Fan, and Leng Shuang climbed out, a collective sigh of relief escaping their lips. Immediately thinking of the three children who were still inside, Feng Jiu swiftly jumped back onto the damaged airship.","\"How are the children?\" Feng Jiu asked urgently.","Only then did Leng Hua cautiously open the door to the children’s cabin. He saw Hao’er tightly embracing Muchen and Muyue, the three of them huddled together on the floor, their faces pale with fear and shock. Upon seeing him, they seemed to release a collective breath they hadn’t realized they were holding and quickly scrambled to their feet.","\"Mother!\"","The three children rushed towards Feng Jiu, their small bodies trembling with lingering fright.","\"It’s alright, are any of you hurt?\" Feng Jiu asked, her eyes carefully scanning each child for any signs of injury from the violent shaking.","\"No, we fell onto the deck and couldn’t get up, so we didn’t hurt ourselves,\" Hao’er replied.","\"Mm hmm, no injuries,\" Muchen and Muyue echoed in agreement, nodding their heads.","\"That’s good,\" Feng Jiu breathed a sigh of relief, gently touching their small faces. Just then, a realization seemed to strike her, and she led them out of the damaged cabin. Her brow furrowed involuntarily as she took in the unfamiliar surroundings.","Earlier, she had been entirely focused on trying to stabilize the plummeting airship and hadn’t had a moment to observe their descent. Now, as she looked around, she found the place to be strangely oppressive.","Furthermore, while it had been midday when they were previously flying, here it was pitch black, and an unnerving silence hung in the air. There wasn’t even a trace of spiritual energy, as if they had somehow arrived in a place where it was completely blocked.","\"Master, a vortex suddenly appeared in the sky earlier, so we quickly turned the ship around, but we were sucked in before we could escape,\" Du Fan explained, his gaze sweeping over the surroundings, a growing sense of unease evident in his expression.","\"Why hasn’t that person emerged?\" Feng Jiu murmured, only then realizing that the masked man, who had been a passenger, had not made an appearance since the chaotic descent."]},{"number":4669,"title":"Chapter 4669: Soul Separates","paragraphs":["\"He went into the cabin this morning and said not to disturb him. He hasn’t come out yet,\" Leng Shuang stated, her gaze fixed on the tightly sealed cabin door.","Upon hearing this, Feng Jiu’s brow furrowed slightly, but she refrained from checking on him immediately. Instead, she walked towards the bow of the airship and surveyed their surroundings. It appeared they were nestled within a mountain hollow, completely enclosed by lush trees and dense undergrowth, with towering peaks that seemed to pierce the clouds above.","\"Du Fan and Leng Hua, the two of you go and scout the area. See if there are any dwellings nearby and try to determine our current location,\" Feng Jiu instructed the pair, her tone decisive.","\"Yes, Master,\" they replied in unison, leaping into the air and soaring away on their swords.","Feng Jiu then turned her attention to the sky. She swiftly gathered her spiritual energy within her hands, preparing to cast a protective barrier around the damaged airship. However, just as the barrier began to form, a sudden intuition flickered within her, and she glanced down at her hands, her eyes narrowing with a flash of insight.","\"Do not wander off and stay within the airship,\" Feng Jiu instructed the three children, her voice firm.","\"Mm, we understand,\" the children replied earnestly, their eyes following her as she approached the closed cabin door. They trailed behind her, watching as she knocked.","\"Knock, knock.\"","Feng Jiu rapped twice on the door, but there was no response from within. She called out, \"If you do not open the door, I am coming in.\" After a brief pause, silence still emanated from the cabin. With a subtle movement of her divine sense, she placed her hand against the door and gently pushed it open.","The cabin was surprisingly spacious. Besides a bed for resting, it contained ample room for other belongings. Feng Jiu stepped inside, her gaze immediately drawn to the figure seated cross-legged on the bed.","A distinct aura enveloped the figure, clearly indicating the presence of a protective barrier. However, Feng Jiu’s keen senses detected that only the faintest trace of life force remained within his body at that moment.","He sat motionless with his eyes closed, appearing to be in a deep state of meditation, completely oblivious to the world outside.","Feng Jiu briefly observed him, recalling some of the things he had mentioned during their journey. She then paused and addressed the three curious children who had followed her to the doorway. \"You guys, go outside first!\"","\"Alright,\" the children replied, their curiosity piqued but obediently backing away.","Once the children had left the cabin, Feng Jiu moved closer to examine the seated figure more intently. She confirmed her initial assessment – his soul was indeed absent from his physical form. A frown creased her brow. Without disturbing the protective barrier, she turned and walked away.","She remembered him mentioning that this physical body was not his original one, implying that he could not inhabit it indefinitely and that his soul had to periodically return to its true vessel. She simply hadn’t anticipated encountering this situation so soon.","Considering her recent discovery, a sense of urgency settled in her heart. It seemed imperative that they leave this strange place as quickly as possible.","Meanwhile, Du Fan and Leng Hua, who had been tasked with investigating the surroundings, were flying through the deepening night on their swords. Suddenly, they both experienced a gradual decrease in their speed, and an inexplicable heaviness seemed to weigh down their bodies.","\"Something seems wrong...\" Before Leng Hua could complete his sentence, his vision abruptly went black, and he lost consciousness, plummeting from his sword.","\"Leng Hua!\"","Du Fan cried out in alarm, his spiritual energy surging around him instinctively. But at that precise moment, an eerie, bluish-green flame flickered into existence directly in front of him and then vanished just as quickly. Almost simultaneously, the spiritual energy surrounding his own body seemed to be suppressed, his vision darkened, and he too succumbed to unconsciousness, falling downwards.","The two figures plummeted from the night sky, yet they did not strike the ground. Instead, it was as if an unseen force gently cradled them, halting their fall and beginning to move them forward..."]},{"number":4670,"title":"Chapter 4670: Refuse to leave","paragraphs":["Chapter 4670: Refuse to leave","At the airship, Feng Jiu’s brow remained furrowed as she scanned their surroundings, but Du Fan and Leng Hua were nowhere in sight. A vague sense of foreboding arose in her heart, and she immediately summoned the contract beasts in her space.","“Fire Phoenix, Cloud Devouring.”","Three beams of light appeared, and as they dissipated, the majestic Fire Phoenix and two imposing Cloud Devouring beasts stood before her.","“What’s wrong?” Fire Phoenix inquired, its gaze sweeping over the area. Sensing the peculiar aura, its voice shifted slightly. “It’s demonic energy!”","“Demonic energy?” Feng Jiu’s eyebrow arched in surprise. “I did sense that the aura here was somewhat strange, and I couldn’t utilize my spiritual energy as effectively, but I hadn’t considered it to be demonic energy.”","Beasts possessed an acute sensitivity to demonic energy, so if the Fire Phoenix identified it as such, its assessment was undoubtedly accurate.","“Du Fan and Leng Hua went out to investigate and have not yet returned. I am concerned that something may have befallen them. You remain here and keep watch. I will go and take a look,” Feng Jiu stated, preparing to disembark from the airship. Just as she was about to step off, a voice called out.","“Wait a moment.”","Hearing this voice, Feng Jiu was slightly taken aback. She turned to see the masked man emerging from the cabin. Observing his presence, she remarked, “Didn’t your soul depart from your body earlier? I thought your soul was unable to return here.” She hadn’t anticipated his swift awakening.","“I didn’t expect something to occur in such a short span of time. They have actually brought you to the demon realm,” the masked man sighed, stepping out slowly. His gaze fell upon Yue’er beside Feng Jiu, pausing for a moment before returning to Feng Jiu. “I must take them away. This place is not suitable for them.”","Feng Jiu remained silent for a moment, her eyes shifting to the three children. After a brief pause, she inquired, “You said this is the Demon Realm? I’ve noticed that the spiritual energy here is restricted. How will you be able to take them away? Furthermore, the blood curse on Yue’er and Chen’er has not been completely eradicated.”","“The longer they remain in the Demon Realm, the more challenging it will become for them to utilize their spiritual energy. Now that we have just arrived, I can still manage to take them away, but if we linger any longer, the outcome is uncertain. Moreover, I have received information indicating that they intend to trap you here permanently. Even with your considerable power, it will be exceedingly difficult to tear open a section of the sky and return to your original realm.”","“I won’t go! I don’t want to leave Mother! Wherever Mother is, Yue’er will be too!” Yue’er exclaimed, tightly embracing her mother and clinging to her legs.","“I won’t go either! Mother is in danger; I won’t leave! I want to stay with Mother!” Hao’er declared, standing resolutely by Feng Jiu’s side.","“I’d rather die than leave!”","Muchen also moved to Feng Jiu’s side, firmly grasping her hand and looking warily at the masked man. “We’re not leaving! We won’t go with you! Even if this is the Demon Realm, we want to stay with Mother! We don’t want Mother to be in danger!”","Hearing their fervent declarations, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but sigh softly. She gently stroked Yue’er’s head and said, “It is dangerous here. Sooner or later, you will have to become his disciples. It is better to follow your Master and leave.”","“No! No! I don’t want to!” Yue’er cried, her eyes reddening as she looked up at her mother with a piteous expression. “Mother, Yue’er doesn’t want to leave you. I don’t want to, please don’t make me go!”","Her voice was choked with tears, and she glared fiercely at the masked man, her small face set with determination. “If you dare to take us away, I will hate you forever! I will never acknowledge you as my Master!”"]},{"number":4671,"title":"Chapter 4671: Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 4671: Demon","Hearing this, the masked man who had been about to step forward stopped in his tracks. He fixed his gaze on the small girl, who resembled a cornered animal with her slightly reddened eyes filled with a mixture of anger and apprehension. A soft sigh escaped his lips, and a fleeting hint of helplessness flickered across his eyes. He then turned to Feng Jiu and said, “Aren’t you going to search for them? Go ahead! We will wait for you here.”","Observing this exchange, Feng Jiu glanced at the masked man, then patted the heads of the three children beside her. “You stay here and wait for me. Mother is going to look for Du Fan and Leng Hua.”","“Mother, please come back safely. We’ll wait here for you!” Yue’er’s soft, childish voice was filled with worry as she gently pulled on her mother’s hand. “My brothers and I will wait here for Mother to return. We won’t go anywhere until you come back.”","Warmth spread through Feng Jiu’s heart. She affectionately rubbed Yue’er’s small head and said, “Alright, be good. Mother will be back soon.” She then looked at the masked man and offered a brief, “Thank you for your help.”","As soon as the words left her lips, she gathered her spiritual energy and swiftly departed from the airship, heading in the direction Du Fan and Leng Hua had gone.","Shuttling through the darkness of the night, she felt the demonic energy in the air growing increasingly dense. Apart from the sound of the wind whistling past her ears, an unnerving silence permeated the surroundings. Suddenly, she came to an abrupt stop and looked back.","The airship was no longer visible, as if shrouded by a thin, ethereal fog. Her thoughts turned to the three children within, and then to the reassuring presence of the Fire Phoenix and the masked man who were there to protect them. Reassured, she didn’t linger and continued on her way.","“Leng Hua?”","Feng Jiu called out in surprise. She spotted a figure sitting in the tall grass ahead – it was indeed Leng Hua, who had left with Du Fan just moments ago. However, he was now sitting there completely still, his face blank and devoid of any expression. A sense of urgency propelled her forward.","“What happened? Did you encounter...” She reached out to touch his shoulder, but the moment her fingers brushed against him, her voice caught in her throat, and she recoiled swiftly.","Whoosh!","Two thick vines shot out from the ground with startling speed, as if they were sentient beings. Had she not reacted instantly, she would have been ensnared. Looking back at the spot where Leng Hua had been sitting motionless, she saw a horrifying transformation. He had morphed into the shape of a large, grotesque tree.","The tree trunk was as thick as two people could embrace, and though it possessed few branches and leaves, they swayed ominously. Strangely, Leng Hua’s face was now visible on the rough bark of the trunk, contorted in what appeared to be a silent struggle within the wood.","“What a demon tree!”","A cold fury hardened Feng Jiu’s gaze as she took in the horrifying scene. She extended her hand, and the Blue Edge sword, radiating a vibrant green light, materialized in her grasp. With a surge of spiritual energy from her palm, flames erupted around the blade, and a fiery red figure – the manifestation of her intent – soared upwards, raising the glowing sword high above its head, poised to strike down at the monstrous demon tree below.","“Master, don’t!”","Suddenly, the human face embedded in the demon tree let out a piercing, shrill scream. The sound resonated with a chilling familiarity, causing Feng Jiu’s hand to tremble involuntarily, making the descending sword veer slightly to the side.","Whoosh! Bang!","A violent gust of wind roared downwards, and the green sword qi, now carrying streaks of fiery energy, slashed down towards the ground, carving a deep, jagged furrow in the earth. Dirt and debris erupted outwards, and flames ignited along the dry grass and fallen branches, spreading rapidly. In an instant, the leaping flames illuminated the dark night sky, burning away the oppressive demonic energy in the air. A faint, unsettling sizzling sound could be heard amidst the crackling fire."]},{"number":4672,"title":"Chapter 4672: Underground Palace","paragraphs":["Chapter 4672: Underground Palace","The sound was like oil meeting fire as a sharp, sizzling noise resounded. As the flames danced and grew, the oppressive demonic energy in the vicinity began to wane, visibly shrinking back as if in fear. Even the surrounding trees seemed to recoil from the encroaching light and heat. Sensing an opportunity amidst the chaos, the demon tree itself made a desperate attempt to flee.","But Feng Jiu was swift. Gathering her inner energy, she blurred into the shadows, a determined hunter pursuing its prey. She allowed the flames to continue their work, a cleansing force against the encroaching darkness. With a powerful leap, she closed the distance and plunged the gleaming Blue Edge sword directly into the demon tree’s thick trunk.","The impact resonated with a sharp, cracking sound, and a viscous, greenish-blue sap oozed from the wound. Simultaneously, a heart-wrenching scream tore from the demon tree as its massive form shuddered and began to shrink rapidly. In mere moments, the towering entity was reduced to a pathetic, human-sized tree stump, still faintly pulsating with a malevolent energy.","“Tell me,” Feng Jiu’s voice was sharp and demanding, the Blue Edge now withdrawn and pointed directly at the diminished tree, “Where are my people?” She pressed her sword down, increasing the force behind the sword’s tip, piercing the woody flesh once more. A thin trickle of sap escaped, accompanied by the tree demon’s desperate cries for mercy.","“Don’t kill me! Please, don’t kill me! I’ll take you there,” it pleaded, its voice laced with terror at the prospect of its centuries of cultivation being extinguished in an instant.","Reluctantly, the tree demon began to lead the way. As they moved through the darkened landscape, Feng Jiu’s eyes flickered downwards, though her body remained still. With subtle grace, she conjured a small, intense flame in the palm of her hand. In the next heartbeat, her hand shot out, striking a patch of ground that appeared utterly black and empty.","“Bang!”","“Ah!” A sharp cry of pain erupted from the seemingly vacant spot. The force of Feng Jiu’s palm, amplified by the searing flame, landed with a solid impact. A quantity of dark, viscous liquid splattered onto the ground. With a swift wave of her hand, Feng Jiu swept the foul substance aside.","The demon tree, ever opportunistic, seized the moment to try and escape again. But Feng Jiu merely snorted in disdain. With a casual flick of her wrist, the Blue Edge flashed, severing several thick branches from the humanoid tree stump.","“Ah!” The demon tree yelped, startled, and instinctively crouched lower. Seeing its severed limbs lying uselessly on the ground, it turned back to Feng Jiu, its remaining form trembling. “I... I can’t take you any further,” it stammered, fear evident in its voice. “Otherwise, the Demon King will surely kill me.”","“And you’re not afraid that I’ll kill you right now?” Feng Jiu countered, her gaze unwavering. She idly played with the cluster of flames in her hand, the flickering light casting an ominous glow on her face. “Or would you prefer to experience what it feels like to burn as firewood?” Her voice was dangerously cold.","The sight of the heavenly fire sent a fresh wave of terror through the tree demon. It shrank back, its woody surface seeming to pale. “No, no! I’ll take you there. I’ll take you there, is that alright?” Only then did it fully resign itself to its fate, leading Feng Jiu onward. They finally arrived before an enormous tree, its girth so wide it would likely take seven or eight people to encircle its trunk. The demon tree recoiled slightly. “Go in there,” it mumbled, pointing a remaining branch towards the massive tree. “That’s the place.”","Feng Jiu studied the indicated tree. It was undeniably large and lush, and the demonic energy surrounding it was noticeably denser than in the surrounding area. However, apart from its size and the faint oppressive aura, it appeared unremarkable.","“How do we get in?” Feng Jiu inquired, her eyes narrowed.","“Go around the tree trunk once to the left, then once to the right,” the tree demon whispered, its gaze darting nervously around their surroundings. “Then slap the trunk and shout ‘open,’ and it will open.”","“An underground palace?” Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow, a hint of surprise in her voice.","“Yes, yes,” the tree demon stammered. “The Demon Queen herself came out to capture those two people and took them inside. The Demon Queen... she loves to drain the essence of immortals. If you don’t want to see them reduced to nothing but white bones, you’d better hurry and go inside.” As it spoke, the tree demon edged backward, clearly anxious to put as much distance as possible between itself and Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu glanced at the retreating demon tree, then turned her attention to the massive trunk before her. Following the demon’s instructions precisely, she circled the tree once to the left, then once to the right. Finally, she placed her palm against the rough bark and shouted, “Open!”","A gaping doorway appeared in the midst of the colossal tree trunk. Without hesitation, Feng Jiu stepped forward and disappeared into the darkness beyond."]},{"number":4673,"title":"Chapter 4673: Found","paragraphs":["Chapter 4673: Found","It was indeed an underground palace. As Feng Jiu descended the stone stairs, faint sounds drifted from the depths within. Lining both sides of the descending passage, clusters of eerie green ghostly flames flickered, casting an unsettling illumination on the path below. The spectral green glow added an eerie atmosphere to the place.","The ghostly flames danced with an unseen current, and a subtle flow of air stirred the stillness. It was clear that this underground palace possessed more than a single entrance and exit, suggesting a connection to the outside world somewhere within its depths. Surprisingly, upon entering, Feng Jiu encountered not a single demon in the initial passage. She continued along the dimly lit path and soon discovered that the underground passage opened into a vast mountain hollow. On the far side of this cavernous space, a large congregation of demons had gathered.","Feng Jiu positioned herself close to the cool stone wall, subtly turning her head to observe the flickering ghostly flames ahead, the source of the muffled sounds she had initially heard. As her eyes adjusted to the eerie light, the scene before her came into sharp focus. Approximately a hundred demonic beings of various grotesque shapes and sizes milled about. In the very center of this unsettling assembly, two figures hung suspended upside down. There was no mistaking them: Du Fan and Leng Hua.","Seeing her companions seemingly unconscious and dangling precariously at the mercy of these demonic creatures, a surge of protective anger coursed through Feng Jiu. Her gaze swept across the assembled demons, finally settling on two imposing figures standing slightly apart from the main throng.","One was a female demon, her features heavily made up, exuding a seductive yet sinister aura. Her demonic energy was undeniably potent, a palpable force in the cavernous space. Beyond her alluring and captivating appearance, the sheer intensity of her demonic energy was difficult to ignore.","The figure beside her possessed a face that was strangely obscured, as if veiled by a perpetual layer of mist. Despite this visual ambiguity, the raw power of the demonic energy radiating from his body was undeniable. It was immediately apparent to Feng Jiu that these two must be the Demon King and Demon Queen mentioned by the terrified tree demon.","As she mentally strategized a plan to rescue Du Fan and Leng Hua, a distinct voice echoed from within the gathered demons.","“Why did you bring these two back?” the voice, tinged with worry, resonated through the cavern. “They are under the command of that Ghost Doctor, Feng Jiu. If she discovers that you have captured them, she will undoubtedly come looking for us. Won’t that just invite unnecessary trouble?” The Demon King, his gaze fixed on the two cultivators hanging upside down, addressed the demon queen beside him. “Let them go! Pretend you never saw them here.”","Upon hearing this, the Demon Queen slowly raised her heavily lashed eyes, casting a seductive yet calculating glance at the Demon King. “Let them go?” she purred, her voice laced with a dangerous nonchalance. “Don’t forget the instructions from the immortal above – they specifically said to get rid of them. If we simply release them, how will we explain our failure?”","She paused, idly toying with her long, bright red fingernails, her gaze sharp and unwavering. “Besides,” she continued, her tone hardening, “if we let them go, those immortals certainly won’t let us off the hook. Not to mention the promises they made – they assured us that if we complete this task, we will receive a significant reward.”","The Demon King scoffed, his obscured features conveying his disdain. “Hmph! How can you possibly take what those beings say seriously? In my opinion, they merely seek to use that ghost doctor, Feng Jiu, to bring about the destruction of our demon clan. Why else would they send these two here, instead of anywhere else? Is Feng Jiu someone you can afford to provoke? She is the Sovereign Ruler! Even the Devil Lord himself fought her and ultimately lost his soul. We are nowhere near as powerful as the Devil Lord, and she has shown no interest in fighting us. Why on earth would we invite her wrath?”","The Demon King’s voice was cold and firm as he reiterated his command, his gaze flicking between Du Fan and Leng Hua before settling back on the Demon Queen. “Let them go. Just allow them to leave this place as quickly as possible.”","The Demon Queen shot him a sidelong glance, a hint of mockery in her crimson eyes. “Why is it that you fear no one else, yet you tremble at the mere mention of Feng Jiu?”"]},{"number":4674,"title":"Chapter 4674: Diversion","paragraphs":["Chapter 4674: Diversion","“How can it not be the same? Just listen to me! You won’t go wrong,” the Demon King insisted, a note of desperation creeping into his voice. “I truly wish to meet her, but I’m afraid she won’t even come!” The Demon Queen merely offered a light smile, clearly not taking his anxieties to heart.","Feng Jiu listened to their exchange for a moment longer, a plan forming in her mind. She quietly retreated into the deeper shadows, retrieved a talisman from her spatial storage, and with a subtle flick of her wrist, sent it flying. A moment later, her voice echoed from the direction she had just vacated, amplified and chilling: “Hand over my people!”","The command reverberated through the underground palace, laced with an icy, murderous intent. Instantly, the hundred or so demons gathered in the cavern were jolted by surprise and scattered in disarray. “No! It must be Feng Jiu!” Panic flared in the Demon King’s voice. He had no desire to become an enemy of Feng Jiu, let alone engage her in battle. If she had indeed breached their defenses...","“What are you afraid of? I will go and meet her,” the Demon Queen scoffed. She addressed the smaller demons with a dismissive wave of her hand. “Leave a few to keep watch. The rest of you, come with me!”","“Yes, Your Majesty!” the demons chorused, falling into a disorganized line behind their queen as she swept towards the passage leading further into the underground complex. Once they had all disappeared from view, Feng Jiu moved with lightning speed, flashing forward to where Du Fan and Leng Hua hung suspended. With swift, precise movements of her sharp blade, she dispatched the two demons guarding them, and a pulse of energy from the Blue Edge severed the restraints.","“You... you... you...” The Demon King, who had been sitting and sighing in anxious anticipation, suddenly saw a flash of red. He recoiled in surprise, but as his eyes focused, he saw a figure clad in vibrant crimson, possessing a strikingly beautiful face framed by an air of quiet composure, yet radiating a powerful and captivating aura. Though he had never laid eyes on Feng Jiu before, he knew instinctively that this woman could be none other than the legendary ghost doctor.","“You... you are that Ghost Doctor, Feng Jiu?” the Demon King stammered, his misty features gradually coalescing, revealing a face that was not particularly handsome, bordering on slightly unsettling. At this moment, however, his gaze was fixed solely on Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu ignored his hesitant inquiry. Instead, she swiftly pinched the philtrum acupoints of Leng Hua and Du Fan, rousing them from their unconscious state. Had she not been concerned that the demons might inflict further harm upon them, she wouldn’t have wasted even a single talisman to create a diversion.","“Master?” The two men blinked, disoriented for a moment, before quickly righting themselves. They found their legs slightly numb and tingly, as if their circulation had been restricted.","“It’s good that you’re awake,” Feng Jiu said, her gaze then turning to the Demon King. “Based on what you were saying earlier, there is someone who intends to use you to harm me? Do you know their identity?”","As she spoke, she slowly advanced, the sharp tip of the Blue Edge tracing a line on the stone floor with each deliberate step. The Demon King, while not weak himself, had no desire to antagonize Feng Jiu. He wanted to avoid a confrontation at all costs. “Let’s talk, let’s talk,” he urged hastily.","“I want to know the identity of the people you were just discussing!” Feng Jiu demanded, her voice leaving no room for evasion.","“They...” The Demon King began to answer, but his words were abruptly cut short by a sudden commotion erupting from the passage behind him.","“Kill them!” the Demon Queen’s shrill voice echoed through the cavern, followed by a surge of smaller demons charging forward.","Du Fan and Leng Hua were initially caught off guard by the sudden attack, clearly not expecting such brazen aggression. Seeing the horde of demons descending upon them, Du Fan sneered. “Let’s see who kills whom!” he declared, with a swift flick of his wrist, he opened the fan he held, and a sharp blade of compressed air shot forth towards the advancing demons."]},{"number":4675,"title":"Chapter 4675: Must Die","paragraphs":["Chapter 4675: Must Die","“Whoosh!”","“Clang!”","“Bang bang bang!”","The underground palace erupted in a cacophony of sound. The sharp whistle of displaced air mingled with the ringing of clashing swords and the dull thuds of impacts, creating an immediate and chaotic scene. Hundreds of monstrous figures swarmed Feng Jiu, Du Fan, and Leng Hua, their greenish-blue blood splattering across the stone floor. Piercing screams and guttural roars echoed through the confined space, the sounds lingering ominously.","“Stop fighting! Stop fighting! Everyone, cease this!” The Demon King bellowed, his voice strained above the din. However, Feng Jiu and her companions paid him no heed. The lesser demons, panicked and desperate, darted around with their heads clutched in their hands. Finding no avenue of escape, they fought with the ferocity of the cornered.","Some of the demons shed their humanoid guises, revealing their monstrous true forms to engage in the desperate struggle. Yet, against the combined might of Feng Jiu, Du Fan, and Leng Hua, these creatures were pathetically weak. It was clear that only the Demon King and the Demon Queen possessed the power to truly challenge them.","Observing the growing number of her fallen brethren littering the ground, a flash of bloodthirsty cruelty ignited in the Demon Queen’s eyes. Her gaze fixated on Feng Jiu’s exquisite features and slender form, a sinister smile slowly spreading across her painted lips.","With a fluid gesture, she extended her hands and twisted her body, undergoing a grotesque transformation. Her limbs elongated and scaled over, her torso contorted, and she became a terrifying snake demon with a human face and a serpentine body. As her serpentine form writhed and her clawed hands moved, faint, chilling hissing noises cut through the chaotic battle sounds.","Feng Jiu glanced down and saw a horrifying carpet of snakes slithering across the stone floor. Some were as thin as chopsticks, others as thick as fingers, and some as wide as two hands. The snakes displayed a vibrant array of colors, and some even sported bright, ominous crowns upon their heads. Their gaudy hues were a clear indication of their potent venom.","Although Feng Jiu, Du Fan, and Leng Hua possessed bodies highly resistant to poison, capable of withstanding even the deadliest toxins, none of them relished the prospect of being bitten by these venomous creatures.","Instinctively, Feng Jiu drew her gleaming Blue Edge sword and slashed through the air. Then, raising the intense flame in her palm, she channeled its fiery energy into the blade. With a resounding “whoosh,” a torrent of fire erupted from the sword, sweeping towards the writhing mass of snakes on the ground.","“Come behind me!” Feng Jiu shouted, directing Du Fan and Leng Hua to retreat to her side.","Heeding her command, the two men simultaneously leaped back, swiftly positioning themselves behind their master. However, just as they settled into their protective stance, a flash of red blurred past them, heading directly towards the transformed Demon Queen.","Seeing Feng Jiu’s decisive action, the Demon King’s initial instinct was to intervene, to aid his queen. But after taking a single step forward, he abruptly halted. The Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu was the Sovereign Ruler, and even in the Demon Realm, her formidable strength and unparalleled skills were legendary. Her mastery of medicinal pills was extraordinary, but her true terror lay in her astonishing combat prowess. How many powerful beings had fallen by her hand, their deaths echoing across the heavens and earth, solidifying the fearsome reputation of the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu?","He dared not provoke her, let alone make her his enemy, for he knew with chilling certainty that such an act would inevitably lead to his own demise. He could only lament the machinations of those above, who had clearly orchestrated this deadly encounter. Whether Feng Jiu perished at their hands or they fell before her, it would be a favorable outcome for those shadowy figures. But now that events had spiraled to this point, he felt powerless to stop the inevitable.","He knew, with a sinking feeling in his gut, that the Demon Queen was doomed. If he dared to interfere, even he would surely meet his end by Feng Jiu’s merciless blade.","“Ah!”","A piercing, bloodcurdling scream ripped through the din of battle, momentarily silencing the lesser demons. Hearing the agonizing cry, they froze, their movements arrested in disbelief. They ceased their frantic fighting and turned their gazes towards the source of the horrifying sound – the Demon Queen. What they saw widened their eyes in utter shock and terror."]},{"number":4676,"title":"Chapter 4676: Don’t Dare","paragraphs":["Chapter 4676: Don’t Dare","The emerald-green demon blood spurted out as the demon queen’s serpentine head was completely severed, flying through the air before landing amidst the other demons. One demon, caught off guard, instinctively reached out to catch the falling head. It stared at the demon queen’s wide-open eyes, which were filled with terror and resentment, and then let out a piercing scream.","“Ahhhhhhhhhhh!”","With that scream, the little demon instinctively recoiled and threw the demon queen’s head upwards, tossing it away from the others. This time, no one stood foolishly to catch the severed head. Instead, they automatically stepped back to avoid it, allowing the demon queen’s head to fall to the ground and roll several times until it came to a stop.","The surrounding demons dared not make a sound, staring in shock and terror as their demon queen’s head had been severed from her body, her snake-like form crashing to the ground with a heavy thud. The red-clad human woman stepped onto the fallen body, and then with a swift, ruthless thrust, the green-glowing sword in her hand pierced through the demon queen’s torso. In front of all the demons, she cut open the demon queen’s belly and extracted her snake gallbladder and a Neidan. Even though they were demons accustomed to violence, the bloody and cruel scene made them turn pale, swallow hard, and instinctively retreat, fearing that they would suffer the same fate as their queen.","The Demon King was also visibly shocked by the scene unfolding before him. He hadn’t anticipated Feng Jiu taking the Demon Queen’s snake gallbladder and medicinal pill without uttering a single word, let alone cutting open her abdomen in front of all his subjects. The entire scene and her ruthless methods sent a chill even through his demonic heart.","“Does anyone else desire death? I don’t mind sending them on their way,” Feng Jiu said, turning back. Her cold gaze swept over the assembled demons before finally settling on the Demon King. Under her intense stare, the demons instinctively backed away further, not daring to utter a single word. The Demon King looked at the lifeless body of his Demon Queen, as if he wanted to speak, but in the end, he merely let out a heavy sigh.","“I advised her not to provoke you, but I never expected...”","Feng Jiu regarded him coldly. “You had no intention of opposing me, and therefore, even though you are a demon, I would not have harmed you. However, if you wish to avenge your demon queen, I will naturally oblige you.”","The subterranean flames continued to burn fiercely, and the demons cautiously avoided them, their eyes fixed on their Demon King, awaiting his command.","“I certainly have no desire to go against the Ghost Doctor,” the Demon King said with another sigh. “The demon queen was wrong to capture your people, and now you have taken her life. I sincerely hope the Ghost Doctor can spare my remaining demons. As for anything the Ghost Doctor wishes to know, I will tell you everything within my knowledge.”","Hearing this unexpected concession, Feng Jiu’s eyes flashed with interest. She glanced sharply at the Demon King before immediately raising her hand and waving it. The burning flames were instantly extinguished. However, as the flames died down, the acrid smell of burning flesh and earth wafted upwards from the ground, stinging their nostrils.","“Ghost Doctor, this way please,” said the Demon King, gesturing for them to follow him.","Feng Jiu acknowledged his gesture and followed him forward. Behind them, Du Fan and Leng Hua moved slowly, keeping pace with the Demon King until they entered a cave. It was a cavern located beneath a mountain peak, quite different from the underground palace they had previously encountered. Instead, it resembled more closely a place where a demon king might cultivate and reside.","“Ghost Doctor, please sit down!” the Demon King offered.","He then settled himself down and looked directly at Feng Jiu, saying, “Our Demon Realm exists outside the Three Realms of Heaven, Earth, and Humans. It could almost be said that we have no contact with you immortals. This time...”"]},{"number":4677,"title":"Chapter 4677: Back","paragraphs":["Chapter 4677: Back","His voice faltered, and a hint of hesitation flickered across his face. Then, as if he had made a firm decision, he gritted his teeth and said, “I truly didn’t want things to escalate this way. I never desired to become enemies with the Ghost Doctor, and I was unaware that they had dispatched him to our Demon Realm. We only discovered his arrival after he was already here. The higher-ups issued the order to eliminate you. The Demon Queen didn’t even consult me before capturing your two subordinates. I...”","Feng Jiu interjected, “I am already aware of that. What I want to know is about the individuals who seek my demise.”","“Those four are powerful entities hailing from the Upper Immortal Realm, also known as the Four Great Emperors. That is the extent of my knowledge. I know nothing further. After all, the Upper Immortal Realm is not a place we can easily access, so my understanding of it is very limited,” the Demon King explained, indicating his lack of further information.","The Four Great Emperors?","Feng Jiu’s eyes flashed subtly, and she remained silent for a moment before inquiring, “I observe that the Demon Realm is shielded by a barrier. Now that we wish to depart, do you possess a means to send us away?”","“Of course, I can assist with your departure.” Hearing her desire to leave, the Demon King felt a wave of relief wash over him. He dared not keep this harbinger of death within the Demon Realm any longer. Since she was willing to leave, he would naturally expedite her departure as swiftly as possible.","“Let’s proceed then! My airship is parked some distance away. Send us away, and we shall consider this matter concluded,” Feng Jiu stated slowly, her gaze sweeping over the surrounding demons.","Consequently, Feng Jiu led the Demon King, Du Fan, Leng Hua, and the others towards the location of the airship.","Upon reaching the airship, they were enveloped by pitch-black darkness, and a palpable demonic energy surged through the air. Dimly, specks of bright green light floated eerily in the surroundings. The masked man stood at the bow of the airship, with the three children positioned beside him. Leng Shuang also stood nearby, patiently awaiting the return of her Patriarch.","The surroundings were quiet, and not a single word was spoken by anyone aboard the airship. The Fire Phoenix perched silently on Mu Chen’s shoulder. The two Cloud Devouring beasts lay quietly to the side. Perhaps sensing the oppressive atmosphere, Yue’er gently tugged at the masked man’s robe.","Feeling the tug on his robe, he turned his head and looked down at the small child beside him. Seeing her delicate and cute little face, his eyes softened involuntarily, and he asked gently, “What is it?”","“Will something bad happen to my mother?” Yue’er asked, tilting her head upwards, her beautiful eyes filled with worry.","Hearing this, he smiled reassuringly and said, “No, with your mother’s strength, even if she were to encounter the ruler of the Demon Realm, she would undoubtedly defeat him overwhelmingly.”","“Then can we leave this place?” Yue’er asked again, her voice laced with hope.","“Don’t worry! With me here, everything will be alright. Besides, your mother is no pushover. Even if things get a little troublesome, we will definitely leave here safely in the end.” He gently rubbed Yue’er’s head and offered a comforting smile.","“Are the people who want to harm us very powerful? Can my mother not defeat them right now? You are so powerful, do you know where my father is at the moment? When will he come back?” Yue’er grabbed his hand that was resting on her head and asked a flurry of questions, her brow furrowed with concern.","“Don’t dwell on such thoughts too much, child. It is futile to ask these questions,” he replied softly, a faint, enigmatic smile playing on the corners of his lips as he chose not to answer her directly.","“Master has returned!” Cloud Devouring’s voice suddenly boomed, breaking the tense silence. He took two steps forward and looked towards the figures approaching from a short distance away. However, upon noticing the large demon following closely behind them, his posture remained guarded, his eyes narrowed with suspicion."]},{"number":4678,"title":"Chapter 4678: Farewell","paragraphs":["Chapter 4678: Farewell","Seeing the large demon trailing behind Feng Jiu, a knowing smile flickered across the masked man’s eyes, and he murmured in a low voice, “It appears matters are about to become quite intriguing.”","The Demon King accompanied Feng Jiu and the others to the airship. His eyes narrowed slightly when he observed the ancient divine beast, the Fire Phoenix, and the two Super Sacred Beasts within. He refrained from entering, addressing Feng Jiu instead, “Ghost Doctor, please proceed inside! I will send you on your way.”","“Alright,” Feng Jiu replied and led Du Fan and Leng Hua across the barrier and onto the airship.","“Mother!”","“Mother, you’re back!”","“Mother!”","The three children eagerly rushed to her side. Seeing her safe return, their faces lit up with happy smiles.","“You’re back. Come now, Mother will take you into the cabin. The Demon King is sending us away, so the airship will likely shake again.” She ushered the three children into the cabin first but did not allow them to remain there. Instead, she immediately transferred them into her spatial dimension.","Feng Jiu closed the cabin door and emerged, gesturing for Du Fan and the others to take a seat and hold on firmly, lest they be thrown about by the airship’s imminent shaking.","The masked man stood at the bow, glancing at Feng Jiu with a hint of surprise. “It seems I underestimated your capabilities,” he remarked.","Feng Jiu returned his gaze and said slowly, “You should be grateful that we are not adversaries.”","Hearing this, the man chuckled softly, looked up at the sky, and commented, “Indeed, those who have incurred your enmity must be experiencing considerable unease at this very moment!”","Feng Jiu remained silent, for at that instant, the demonic energy emanating from the Demon King outside the airship surged dramatically. His figure expanded dozens of times in an instant, appearing as if he were single-handedly supporting the heavens and the earth.","With a shout, he tore a gaping hole in the fabric of the sky with his bare hands. The edges of the tear were held open by his immense demonic energy, seemingly struggling to close but unable to fully do so.","The Demon King reached out his colossal hand and lifted the airship from below, propelling it forcefully into the exit he had created in the sky. As the airship was launched through, the tear behind it swiftly sealed shut, as if it had never existed.","“We’re back,” Feng Jiu murmured, gazing at the familiar expanse of the sky. Night had already fallen, but the sky was a breathtaking canvas dotted with countless stars. The faint flow of spiritual energy in the air carried a familiar and comforting aura.","A soft smile graced her lips as she gently steered the airship to fly at a leisurely pace before walking into the cabin. Moments later, she emerged with the three children by her side.","“Mother, we’re back!” Yue’er exclaimed, jumping up and down happily on the deck of the airship.","Feng Jiu smiled, bent down, and scooped her daughter into her arms, looking at the man in the mask. “Two more days! I will stay with them for two more days, and after that, you can take them away.”","She understood that the current circumstances were not conducive to the children remaining with her. Despite her reluctance to part with them, their separation was inevitable.","“Mother,” Yue’er whispered, hugging her tightly and burying her small face in her mother’s neck. “Mother, do we really have to leave?”","Feng Jiu sighed softly and said, “Yue’er, be a good girl. Mother is doing this for your own well-being. You witnessed what transpired today. This is not the first instance, nor will it be the last. If you stay with me, sooner or later you will face danger again.”","Yue’er listened intently to her mother’s words and remained silent. Hao’er and Mu Chen, standing quietly beside her, lowered their heads and closed their eyes, lost in their own thoughts.","“We can follow Master and leave, but can’t Mother come with us?” Yue’er couldn’t help but ask, her gaze turning towards the masked man with a hopeful expression."]},{"number":4679,"title":"Chapter 4679: Meet in the Upper Immortal Realm","paragraphs":["Chapter 4679: Meet in the Upper Immortal Realm","Hearing the little girl address him as ‘Master,’ the masked man’s lips curved into a gentle smile. “Little one,” he said, his voice soft, “it seems you only call me Master when you desire something from me. Unfortunately, even I am unable to grant this particular request.”","“Why can’t you?” Yue’er asked, her brow furrowed in confusion. “Didn’t you say you were very powerful?”","Hearing this, he chuckled lightly. “No matter how powerful I may be, I cannot obstruct the brilliance of the Phoenix Star. If I were to take her to the Upper Immortal Realm now, it would undoubtedly lead to chaos up there.”","He turned his gaze to Feng Jiu. “Although I cannot take you with me at this moment, you possess the potential to ascend to the Immortal Realm yourself in the future. By then, you should also have developed the strength to contend with those who seek to harm you. Your presence will be far more impactful when you ascend with your own power. To go now would merely be an act of fleeing.”","“Just assist me in safeguarding the three children. You need not concern yourself with anything else. If I wish to ascend, I will naturally do so when the time is right. There is no urgency,” Feng Jiu said, meeting his gaze steadily. “Two days. In two days, take them away!”","“Very well,” he replied, offering no further argument and agreeing directly to her request.","For the subsequent two days, Feng Jiu dedicated her time almost entirely to the three children, imparting knowledge, sharing stories, and replenishing their spatial storage with ample supplies, just in case. They all cherished these final moments together, but despite their deep reluctance to part, the appointed day eventually arrived. Early that morning, the airship continued its gentle flight, and everyone on board gathered at the bow to bid farewell to the masked man and the three children.","“Mother, what shall we do if we miss you in the future?” Yue’er cried, throwing herself into Feng Jiu’s embrace, tears welling up in her bright eyes. Although Hao’er and Muchen remained silent, their eyes were visibly red, and they stood quietly to one side, gazing at their mother as if trying to etch her image permanently into their memories.","“It will be alright. When you arrive there, listen attentively to your master and practice diligently. After I see you off, I will also enter a period of seclusion for a while. When the time is right, I will prepare to advance and ascend. Once everything is settled, I will come and find you myself,” she spoke softly, her words a soothing balm to their young and troubled hearts.","“Mother, what about Father? Will he come and find us with you?” Muchen couldn’t help but ask, his voice filled with longing.","“Yes, Mother will come and find you with your father. Until then, you must be obedient, do not wander off, take good care of yourselves, and do not cause worry for your mother and father,” Feng Jiu said, holding his small hand. She then took Hao’er’s hand and intertwined it with Muchen’s. “You three siblings must support each other and grow up safely together.”","“Yes, Mother, we understand. We will definitely listen to you,” the three children nodded earnestly, their eyes shining with newfound determination.","“Take this. It may prove helpful to you in the future,” the masked man said, handing Feng Jiu an object that resembled a seal or a magical artifact.","Feng Jiu accepted it with both hands, offering a sincere, “Thank you. Please take good care of the three children in the future.”","“Mm, then we shall depart now. We will meet again in the Immortal Realm in the future.” With these words, he glanced at Feng Jiu, then formed an ancient seal with his hands and gently touched the foreheads of the three children. A brilliant flash of golden light erupted, and in the next instant, the three children vanished without a trace.","Feng Jiu stood momentarily stunned, her lips parting to speak, when she felt a powerful air current begin to swirl around them. In the following moment, a blinding flash of golden light shot straight upwards into the vast expanse of the sky..."]},{"number":4680,"title":"Chapter 4680: Four Great Emperors","paragraphs":["Chapter 4680: Four Great Emperors","Feng Jiu stared blankly as the golden light disappeared into the sky, taking the three children with it. A deep sense of loss and sadness filled her heart.","She stood quietly at the bow of the boat, watching until a long time had passed, before finally returning to the cabin. “I’m going to rest. Wake me when we arrive at Sky Mountain,” she said before falling silent within the cabin.","Du Fan, Leng Hua, Leng Shuang, and the others watched, sighing in their hearts. They, too, were reluctant to let their three young masters leave, but they all understood that their departure was for the best.","In the Upper Immortal Realm, within a grand palace, four powerful beings sat together, deep in discussion.","“Didn’t you say you were sending Feng Jiu to the Demon Realm? How come I heard that the Demon King sent her back? What’s going on? Didn’t you dispatch anyone to investigate?” A man in black robes, possessing a thick waist and broad shoulders and appearing to be in his thirties, inquired calmly. The sharp gaze beneath his sword-like eyebrows was piercing, deterring direct eye contact.","“Who knew that the Demon King was so cowardly? He didn’t even dare to avenge the Demon Queen’s death but instead sent Feng Jiu and her group away,” another man frowned, his dignified face revealing his displeasure. “What a waste of such a prime opportunity.”","A middle-aged man then spoke, his tone resolute. “Feng Jiu is the Phoenix Star of Heaven’s Will. How could she perish so easily in the Demon Realm? In my opinion, Feng Jiu’s life must be taken by our own hands. We cannot rely on others.” As he spoke, he rose to his feet, placing his hands behind his back, and looked at the other three. “Just wait! There will always be a chance to end her life. Isn’t that Xuanyuan Mo Ze right within our grasp?”","“Speaking of that Xuanyuan Mo Ze, it is said that the spirit consciousness of that world has not completely dissipated and is gradually solidifying and growing stronger. I’m afraid that Xuanyuan Mo Ze is not dead but is perhaps recovering from his injuries somewhere, biding his time for the opportune moment,” another man mused thoughtfully, his brow slightly furrowed. “If that’s the case, then we are indeed facing trouble.”","Yet another person picked up a cup of spirit tea, took a deliberate sip, and said dismissively, “What trouble? If they wish to ascend to immortality, they must first endure ninety-nine lightning tribulations. Are we afraid that we won’t have a chance to interfere? No matter how formidable they become, how can they possibly surpass the four of us?”","“That is true, but the rate of growth of these two has been astonishing. If we allow them to mature further, they will truly become the rulers of the world. At that juncture, what would become of the status of the Four Great Emperors?”","“They are merely insignificant cultivators from the lower realm. Even if they gain dominion over a portion of the world, do they dare to compete with us? We will not tolerate their ambition!” The middle-aged man stated in a composed voice, snorted lightly, and continued, “If they aspire to ascend to immortality, we shall see if they possess the necessary qualifications!”","The group exchanged knowing glances and smiled in unison. They lifted their cups of spirit tea and took a sip. One of them commented, “Indeed. We are powerful beings of heaven and earth, the esteemed Four Great Emperors. How challenging could it be to end the lives of those two? If we decree that they shall live, they cannot die. If we decree that they shall die, they cannot live!”","“Hahahaha! Well said! Come, allow me to propose a toast with tea!” Another person laughed heartily and raised his spiritual tea towards them.","“Please!” The other three reciprocated the gesture, then took a sip of their spiritual tea, exchanged glances, and smiled."]},{"number":4681,"title":"Chapter 4681: Azure Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 4681: Azure Emperor","After sharing some spiritual tea and engaging in conversation for a while, they rose to depart. Abruptly, one of them halted, turned back, and glanced at the other three, remarking, “Come to think of it, we haven’t heard much about the Azure Emperor of Yunxiao Mountain lately, have we?”","“He has never been amicable towards us, so we don’t pay him much attention. Why bring him up so suddenly?” another inquired.","“I simply have the feeling that we haven’t seen him in a long time. He didn’t even attend the banquet hosted by the Great Emperor of the South Sea last year.”","“The Azure Emperor has always considered himself exceptional and never associates with us. Furthermore, I heard that his beloved disciple failed to survive his tribulation and was reduced to ashes. I doubt he would readily venture out and about.”","“Although we have never formally engaged in combat, I have consistently heard from those outside our circle that the Azure Emperor is the most powerful of all the great emperors, especially after emerging from seclusion a few years ago; his strength has significantly increased.” One person’s face grew serious as he exhaled lightly and said, “But fortunately, this individual does not concern himself with the affairs of others and invariably acts alone, which is advantageous, as he will not interfere with our plans.”","The others nodded in agreement and exited without uttering another word.","Indeed, Azure Emperor’s strength was immeasurable, yet he was also a person who paid no heed to the outside world. Since he would not interfere with them, they naturally would not dedicate excessive attention to him.","At present, their primary concern remained dealing with Feng Jiu. The titles of Phoenix Star and Sovereign of the World presented a considerable threat to their authority.","The individual they feared had already arrived at the base of Sky Mountain aboard an airship.","Feng Jiu gazed at the snow-white expanse of Sky Mountain and addressed Du Fan and the others, “Wait for me here; I’ll go take a look.” With that, she disembarked from the airship, gathered her spiritual energy, and ascended towards the mountain peak.","However, to her astonishment, as she entered the territory of Sky Mountain and attempted to climb, she found herself unable to proceed. Observing the barrier that materialized before her upon contact, her eyes flickered, and she halted in her tracks.","Only then did she realize that the entire Sky Mountain was encased within a barrier. The potent barrier shielded Sky Mountain like an invisible dome. She stared at it blankly, lost in thought for a moment.","Was it Old Man Tianji’s demise that triggered the activation of the barrier around Sky Mountain? Or was it something else entirely? Was Mo Chen still on Sky Mountain? Or had he already ascended to immortality?","Questions flooded her mind, yet she did not attempt to forcefully breach the barrier. Instead, she paused briefly, then turned and walked back towards the airship.","Shortly after Feng Jiu’s departure, Du Fan and the others also noticed the barrier that had enveloped Sky Mountain. Just as they were expressing their surprise, they saw their master returning.","“Master, are we unable to go up?” Du Fan inquired.","Feng Jiu shook her head and replied, “A barrier has been erected. I presume they don’t want anyone ascending.”","Upon hearing this, the group exchanged concerned glances. Finally, Leng Hua asked, “Master, where should we proceed next?”","Feng Jiu looked towards the sky, pondered for a moment, and then said, “You all should return! I, on the other hand, am going to find a secluded place to cultivate. You guys investigate and see if you can locate Mo Ze. If you obtain any news, inform me.”","Seeing her resolve, the others didn’t press further, simply saying, “Alright, we will depart tomorrow.” They understood that perhaps this time, their parting might extend for several years before they saw each other again."]},{"number":4682,"title":"Chapter 4682: Mo Ze’s Whereabouts","paragraphs":["Chapter 4682: Mo Ze’s Whereabouts","In the depths of a certain sea area, Xuanyuan Mo Ze, whom everyone was searching for, lay in a deep slumber. He was enveloped by the immense pressure of the seawater, his entire being was encased within a protective, bubble-like barrier. Within this tranquil enclosure, he remained utterly still, his breathing barely perceptible, akin to one who had departed from the living realm.","Throughout the abyssal expanse, various spirit fish and formidable sea monsters swam along the dark currents. Yet, they all instinctively steered clear of the area surrounding Xuanyuan Mo Ze. The bubble that enveloped him emitted a gentle glow, contrasting with the potent aura that emanated from within. This bubble-like phenomenon cast a subtle green glow, an almost imperceptible shimmer in the deep-sea darkness, discernible only upon close inspection.","While the spirit fish and sea monsters of the deep dared not approach Xuanyuan Mo Ze, the ambient spirit energy of the ocean subtly permeated his seemingly lifeless form in delicate wisps. He remained in his unconscious state, suspended in a silent slumber.","Meanwhile, in the Upper Immortal Realm, atop the majestic Yunxiao Mountain, three young children were peacefully sleeping within the humble confines of a thatched cottage. Perhaps drawn by the gentle rays of sunlight filtering through the simple dwelling, the eldest, Hao’er, stirred and opened his eyes. He sat up, his gaze taking in the unadorned interior of the thatched cottage. A momentary stillness washed over him as if a thought had just surfaced, and it took him a brief moment to fully regain his awareness.","The subtle movements of Hao’er must have reached the ears of Muchen and Muyue, who occupied the other two beds within the small space. They soon stirred, rubbing the sleep from their eyes and sitting up to regard their older brother.","“Big Brother? What’s wrong?” Yue’er inquired, her voice still laced with the drowsiness of just awakening. Her hair, disheveled from sleep, framed her delicate features, which nonetheless retained a charming and endearing quality.","“Nothing,” Hao’er replied, his gaze directed towards the brightening sky visible through the cottage opening. “I just thought it was time to get up and practice.” The morning sun cast a soft and warm glow, creating a comfortable ambiance. He swung his legs over the side of the bed and called the other two, “Get up and wash yourselves! Let’s go outside to practice.”","“Yeah!” The two younger children responded in unison, promptly rising to attend to their morning business.","After a swift wash, Yue’er approached Hao’er, her hair still adorably messy, and requested, “Big Brother, help me tie my hair.”","Hao’er, who had just completed a series of stretches, turned at the sound of her voice. Seeing Yue’er’s approach with her tangled locks, he walked over to her. “Yue’er,” he said gently, “Big Brother will teach you how to tie your own hair. Pay close attention, okay?”","Upon hearing this, Yue’er looked up at him, her eyes flickered momentarily, and then she nodded in agreement.","“Alright,” she affirmed.","“Yue’er, you’re so clever,” Hao’er said with a warm smile, praising her willingness to learn. He then led her back to the room, seated her before the simple bronze mirror, and patiently began to instruct her on the intricacies of tying her hair.","Yue’er watched his movements with focused attention, diligently trying to learn the process. However, a question soon bubbled to the surface. “Big Brother, why haven’t we seen our master since he came back? Why did he leave us here and not take care of us? Does he not want us anymore? If he doesn’t want us, will he send us back to our mother?”","Hearing Yue’er’s heartfelt query, Muchen, who had been standing nearby, also listened with keen interest. Since their arrival at this place, they had not encountered the man who had brought them here, the one they were told was their master. Furthermore, they had been left alone in this modest thatched hut for several days, with no other presence besides the three of them.","“Master must be busy,” Hao’er reassured them, his gaze drifting towards the outside. “Besides, he left us here with food delivered by the Bifang bird every day. Maybe he’ll come find us when he’s finished with his tasks.” As he spoke, his eyes caught sight of a magnificent seven-colored bird soaring gracefully across the vast expanse of the sky."]},{"number":4683,"title":"Chapter 4683: Who Are You?","paragraphs":["Chapter 4683: Who Are You?","Muchen and Muyue followed Hao’er’s gaze outside and when they saw the Bifang bird, neither of them said anything. Their enigmatic master had been absent for several days, yet this celestial bird had remained a constant presence, safeguarding them and even providing them with spirit birds for food.","“Alright, can you tie it now, Yue’er?” Hao’er asked gently.","Yue’er glanced at her reflection, a smile gracing her lips as she nodded. “Mm hmm, Yue’er can tie it just the way Big Brother taught me. What’s more, Yue’er can also braid hair, so in the future, Yue’er will be able to manage her own hair~”","“Mm, that’s good. Let’s go! Let’s go outside to practice,” Hao’er announced to the two younger children.","“Yeah~” they replied in unison, trailing after him to an open area where they began to diligently learn the martial moves, one after the other. The Bifang divine bird, which had been circling in the sky for a while, cast a downward glance at the trio before gracefully landing on a neighboring mountain peak, settling there to observe their practice.","As noon approached, the Bifang divine bird perched on the distant peak seemed to perceive a subtle shift in the atmosphere. Its gaze turned towards the main peak, its magnificent wings unfurled, and it soared in that direction.","Meanwhile, at the main peak, the heavy stone door of a secluded cave creaked open, and a figure clad in pristine white emerged. His movements were fluid and elegant, each step accompanied by a gentle flutter of the white robe, as if a divine wind was billowing gently and surrounded them. Silence seemed to fall upon the surroundings, as if one feared disturbing an immortal dwelling in the mountains.","Beyond the striking celestial aura that enveloped him, his appearance was equally captivating. Their face possessed an unforgettable quality, deserving of the poetic title ‘fallen immortal.’ Yet, while his aura hinted at a detached, otherworldly being, their peach-blossom eyes held a spark of playful mischief, creating a captivating duality of both ethereal grace and earthly charm.","His jet-black hair cascaded loosely casually, unbound by any tie, falling naturally to frame his face. Stepping out of the cave, he gazed towards the sky, noting the return of the divine bird Bifang. A subtle curl tappeared on his lips as he asked, “How are those three little guys?”","The Bifang divine bird tilted its head, its intelligent eyes fixed on the figure before it. “They came looking for you after they woke up, but they’ve been practicing on their own these past few days. They did try to wander off, but I gently guided them back and let them play within the thatched hut. Do you wish to see them?”","“It is indeed time,” the white-clad figure replied. He turned and strolled leisurely towards a stone table situated beneath the shade of a large, ancient tree, and gracefully sat down as he said,”Go, bring them here!”","With a powerful beat of its wings, the Bifang divine bird ascended into the sky once more. Reaching the three children, it alighted beside them and announced, “Come, I will take you to see your master.”","Upon hearing these words, Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue exchanged startled glances. Without hesitation, they clambered onto the divine bird’s broad back, their small hands gripping its feathers tightly. As the Bifang bird took flight, their bodies lifted into the air. A rush of wind swept past their faces, prompting them to instinctively close their eyes. Moments later, they felt the gentle descent and stillness of the bird.","“We are here, you can get down now.” The Bifang bird announced, crouching low to allow the children to safely get off its back.","The three children cautiously dismounted and looked around, their gazes naturally drawn to the person seated serenely beneath the large tree. For a fleeting moment, a shared sense of bewilderment washed over them, for the figure before them bore little resemblance to the master who had brought them to this place.","Despite their confusion, they stepped forward, their small feet moving in unison. Their eyes scanned the surroundings, noting the absence of any other individuals. Finally, Yue’er, her voice filled with innocent curiosity, posed the question that was on all their minds: “Who are you?”"]},{"number":4684,"title":"Chapter 4684: Bestow A Name","paragraphs":["Chapter 4684: Bestow A Name","Upon hearing Yue’er’s innocent question, the Azure Emperor turned his head slightly, a gentle laugh escaping his lips as he regarded her. “Little girl, have you already forgotten your master?” He then turned fully, sweeping his hand in a broad gesture around their surroundings. “Then look around you, do you sense anything familiar?”","Yue’er’s eyes widened in response to his words, her large, expressive eyes fixed on him, blinking in rapid succession. After a thoughtful pause, she spoke in a soft, surprised tone, “Master? Hmmmm?You look different! Although my strange master always wore a mask, I can still tell it that he isn’t you. Besides, this is my first time here, so how could anything feel familiar?”","The Azure Emperor smiled, bemused. “That form was merely the one I adopted in the lower realm. It is not my true body. This is my true appearance. Your mother is already aware of this, but upon our return, my soul was somewhat unstable, so I spent a few days in meditation to recover.”","“So, you’re the real master we were told about?” Yue’er blinked again, her gaze unwavering as she continued to study him, thinking that her master’s eyes were so beautiful! They looked like they were always smiling, making her want to smile too.","“Indeed, I’m the real thing,” he confirmed with a light chuckle. His gaze swept over the three children as he continued, “The blood curse that afflicts your bodies will be removed by me within three days. At that time, the contracted beasts that have been suppressing your powers will also awaken. However, I must inform you that you are in danger. There are many outside who seek your lives and even intend to use you to threaten your mother. Your mother has entrusted you three little troublemakers to my care. From this moment forward, you must heed my words and avoid unnecessary trouble.”","“Mmm hmm!” The three children nodded in earnest agreement.","“Furthermore,” the Azure Emperor continued, his tone becoming slightly more formal, “Azure Emperor is my title. Everyone in the outside world knows me as the Azure Emperor. You must remember this. From now on, should anyone inquire about your master, you are to state that the Azure Emperor of Yunxiao Mountain is your master. My title will serve as a shield, protecting you from being bullied by those in positions of power.”","He spoke calmly, his gaze fixed on the three attentive faces before him. Seeing their earnestness, a flicker of satisfaction warmed his expression. The corners of his lips subtly curved upward, and a hint of a smile fleeted across his eyes.","“Yes, we understand,” the three children replied solemnly, secretly committing his words to memory.","“Also,” he added, his gaze becoming more serious, “now that you have become my disciples, you must no longer use your former names. I will bestow upon you new names, and when you venture out into the world in the future, you are to use only these names. As for your true names, remember never to utter them, for doing so could lead to your demise. Do you understand?”","“Yes,” the three responded in unison. No sooner had the word left their lips than Yue’er, her curiosity piqued, piped up, “Master, what names will you give us?”","“Once you enter my Yunxiao Mountain, you become members of my Azure Emperor’s lineage,” he declared, his voice resonating with a gentle authority. “Starting today, Hao’er will be known as Yun Chen, Muchen will be called Yun Yuan, and Yue’er will be named Yun Qi.” As he spoke the name Yun Qi, a subtle light flickered in his eyes as he looked directly at Yue’er. The little girl was tilting her head, softly repeating the name “Yun Qi,” a simple act that seemed to soften his gaze.","“Thank you, Master, for giving us names,” Hao’er and Muchen said in unison, a sense of understanding dawning within them. They knew that with these new identities, their connection to Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu would remain concealed.","“Master, why is my name so simple? Is it just Yun Qi?” Yue’er asked, a touch of confusion in her voice."]},{"number":4685,"title":"Chapter 4685: Cave Abode","paragraphs":["Chapter 4685: Cave Abode","“Well, your name is Yun Qi. From now on, I’ll also call you Little Qi.” He smiled, appearing to be in a genuinely good mood, his entire countenance radiating happiness.","Hao’er cast a sidelong glance at his master, a flicker of thought crossing his mind that the nickname bestowed upon their sister was somewhat peculiar. Moreover, he couldn’t help but notice the significant softening of his master’s expression whenever he addressed her by that name.","Considering his master’s recent, noticeably gentler treatment of his sister, coupled with the current unusual circumstances, Hao’er suppressed his burgeoning doubts. He held their mother’s judgment in higher regard than his own. The fact that their mother had instructed them to become this man’s disciples and follow him here was sufficient proof in his young mind that this individual was trustworthy.","“Alright, now let me tell you a little about this place,” the Azure Emperor said, his gaze encompassing the three children. “As you can see, you are the only inhabitants here besides myself. Consequently, you will be responsible for your own food, clothing, and shelter. Yunxiao Mountain is protected by a powerful barrier, rendering it impenetrable to outsiders, and by the same token, preventing you from leaving.”","He slowly paced before them, his hands clasped behind his back, a faint smile playing on his lips. “However, these mountains also abound with spiritual medicine fields and spiritual fruit trees. The care of these resources is generally entrusted to puppets I have created. Within these mountains, besides my own cave abode, Little Qi’s cave abode is ready. As for the two of you, I suggest you explore and choose a location that appeals to you. You can then excavate your own cave abodes. You can also venture into the forest behind the mountain to fell trees and fashion stone tables, chairs, and other necessities. Here, self-sufficiency is paramount. Of course...”","He paused, his eyes meeting each of theirs in turn. “If you master the art of puppet-making, you can enlist their assistance in these tasks. Every six months, I will administer a small test, and once a year, a more significant trial. I will also take you out to interact and exchange knowledge with others. In two days, after the blood curse within you is dispelled, I will accompany you down the mountain. I will take you to the city to acquire any necessities you may require. Take this time to consider what you need to purchase. In the future, you will be permitted to descend the mountain once every three months, but I will only accompany you on the first occasion. After that, you will be responsible for your own journeys down the mountain.”","“Master, can we go anywhere on Yunxiao Mountain?” The little girl fluttered her long lashes, her beautiful eyes sparkling with excitement as she looked up at him.","“Yes, you can go anywhere on Yunxiao Mountain,” the Azure Emperor confirmed with a nod. Turning to her, he added, “Come, Little Qi! I will take you to see your cave abode.”","“Yeah!” Yue’er replied with unrestrained enthusiasm, eagerly tugging on her two brothers’ hands to follow their master towards the cave abode.","Upon entering the cave abode, Hao’er, Muchen, and Yue’er exchanged surprised glances. The interior bore the distinct impression of having been recently inhabited. Everything within seemed complete and well-maintained, and they even noticed a small, adjoining kitchen area.","“Master, who used to live here?” Hao’er inquired, his gaze directed at the Azure Emperor who stood within the cave abode with his hands behind his back, surveying their surroundings.","“This is where your senior sister lived back then, but she unfortunately failed to transcend her tribulation and was reduced to ashes, so it has remained unoccupied ever since,” the Azure Emperor explained, his gaze softening as he looked at Yue’er. “Little girl, you will reside here from now on.”","“Master, this was my senior sister’s home. Am I really allowed to live here?” Yue’er’s little head tilted innocently as she asked."]},{"number":4686,"title":"Chapter 4686: Talented","paragraphs":["Chapter 4686: Talented","“Yes, you may. You can live here from now on.” He gently rubbed her head and said, “See if there’s anything you need. I’ll go down the mountain to buy it in a few days.”","“Mm hmm~” Yue’er replied with a bright smile.","Hao’er looked up at him and asked, “Master, can you teach us how to make puppets first?” They were still young, and many tasks proved difficult for them to accomplish independently. Possessing puppets would definitely make things considerably easier.","The Azure Emperor cast a glance at him, placed his hands behind his back, and began to walk towards the outside of the cave, saying, “Follow me.”","They followed him to the stone table situated outside their cave abode and watched attentively as he retrieved several pieces of talisman paper, cinnabar, and a brush, placing them carefully on the table. He then said, “First, I will teach you how to create puppets using talisman paper. This method will be relatively straightforward for you to grasp. Observe closely.”","He paused, his gaze sweeping over them, before picking up the brush. He dipped it deliberately into the cinnabar and then proceeded to draw a complex symbol on the talisman paper. Ceasing his writing, he instructed them, “Copy this symbol exactly. You must draw it in a single, continuous stroke, and as you lift the brush to begin, you must imbue it with your spirit energy.”","“Master, can this really be used as a puppet?” Yue’er asked, her eyes fixed on the talisman paper with unconcealed curiosity.","The Azure Emperor picked up the inscribed talisman paper, subtly activated it with a flick of his wrist, and tossed it lightly into the air. The moment it touched the ground, it underwent a remarkable transformation, materializing into a handsome young man. The three children couldn’t help but widen their eyes in astonishment, their faces lighting up with delight.","“Go boil some water and prepare some tea,” the Azure Emperor instructed the newly formed puppet. The young puppet responded immediately and turned to carry out the task.","“Master, how did you do that? That’s so amazing!” Yue’er exclaimed excitedly, stepping forward eagerly. “I want to learn it too! I want to learn it too!”","The Azure Emperor smiled warmly and explained, “When you draw a talisman and activate it, you only need to focus your thoughts on the appearance you desire for the puppet, and it will transform according to your mental image. However, this type of talisman puppet has a limited lifespan. In the future, when you master advanced puppet making techniques, you will only need to place some crystal stones within them, and they will perpetually obey your commands and perform any task you assign. Furthermore, they will also become formidable fighters.”","He then stood up, smoothly brushed off his robe, and announced, “Alright, you guys can begin practicing now!” He reached into his space and took out several pieces of talisman paper, handing them to the children. He then took out another two talisman brushes and a small container of cinnabar. Only after ensuring they had the necessary materials did he walk over to a shady spot beneath a nearby tree. With a wave of his hand, a comfortable-looking soft couch appeared before him. He then lay down on it to rest.","Witnessing this, the three children eagerly gathered around the stone table and began their practice. Hao’er, being a few years older than both Muchen and Muyue, naturally grasped the technique more quickly. However, despite their young age, Muchen and Muyue were remarkably gifted and intelligent. The three of them diligently practiced without interruption until the light began to fade into dusk. It was only then that the Azure Emperor, who had been peacefully sleeping under the shady tree not far away, finally opened his eyes.","As he opened his eyes and turned his head slightly, he observed Hao’er expertly throw out a completed talisman. As soon as it was activated by Hao’er’s spiritual energy, it instantly transformed into the figure of a man.","Upon witnessing this, the Azure Emperor’s eyes flashed with surprise, and an unusual light flickered across his smiling, captivating peach blossom eyes. He couldn’t help but focus his gaze on Hao’er, a hint of astonishment evident in his expression.","He hadn’t anticipated that this child would possess such remarkable talent and quick understanding. Had he truly mastered the basics after only an afternoon of practice? With such innate ability, how exceptionally outstanding would he become as he matured?","At that moment, a feeling of profound excitement welled up within him. Just how extraordinary would his three disciples become when they reached their full potential?","“Wow! Big Brother, you’re so incredibly good! You actually drew it successfully?” Yue’er exclaimed, her small face radiating pure surprise and delight."]},{"number":4687,"title":"Chapter 4687: Anticipation","paragraphs":["Chapter 4687: Anticipation","When Muchen saw that his Big Brother had finished drawing the talisman, his eyes lit up with joy, and he looked at his Big Brother with admiration. He secretly resolved to draw carefully and learn as quickly as possible. Hao’er glanced at the newly appeared figure and smiled, “Yes, I’ve learned it. I’ll teach you.” With that, he took a step forward and approached the two younger children. “That’s enough for today! It’s getting dark, and you’ve been practicing all afternoon. We’ll continue tomorrow,” the Azure Emperor announced as he walked over to where the three of them were gathered. He looked at them and inquired, “Are you going to eat the Fasting Pills or the roasted chicken?”","“Master, do you have any rice? I want to eat porridge~” Yue’er asked softly, her voice tinged with longing.","“No,” he replied, shaking his head. He observed the little girl’s disappointed expression before saying, “In two days, when you go down the mountain, remember to buy some spirit rice. You can also have the puppets plant spirit rice in the spirit fields on the mountain then.”","“Yeah! We’ll buy some seeds then~” she exclaimed, her spirits lifting, and she smiled with a sparkle in her eyes. That day, they ended up eating roasted spirit chicken once again. Since Hao’er and Muchen did not yet have their own cave abodes, they returned to the thatched cottage to sleep. Yue’er, not wanting to stay in the cave abode alone, followed them back to spend the night in the familiar cottage.","Early the next morning, Hao’er began drawing talismans and conjuring up puppets with the specific purpose of helping him build their cave abodes. He and Muchen deliberately chose locations for their abodes not far from Yue’er’s, ensuring that the three of them could easily keep each other company. After arranging for the puppets to commence construction on the cave abodes, Hao’er returned to teach Muchen and Muyue the intricacies of drawing talismans.","“It should be like this. Watch closely, this is how you draw it,” he instructed, holding the brush and guiding them with care. “You must imbue spirit energy into the very tip of the brush as you begin. Only then will the talisman drawn with the vermilion ink carry potent spiritual energy.”","“Big Brother, does mine look right?” Muchen asked, picking up a talisman he had just completed and showing it to Hao’er for inspection.","“Mm, that’s good. That’s already a well-formed talisman, and a second-level one at that,” Hao’er replied with a smile as he praised.","“Muchen is very talented.”","Since they were the only ones staying in the mountain, their master had bestowed upon them formal names, which they had diligently written down to use when they eventually ventured down the mountain. However, in their secluded mountain dwelling, they still habitually addressed each other by their childhood names.","“Big Brother is the best. Big Brother drew a third-level talisman,” Muchen stated with admiration.","“I’ll keep drawing; I can draw a third-level talisman too.”","“Yes, you definitely can,” Hao’er affirmed with a nod.","While the two boys were talking, Yue’er was concentrating carefully as she drew her own talisman. The symbols she drew were a little crooked and smaller than the example, but she carefully compared her work to the one drawn by their master and finally confirmed that she had accurately reproduced the necessary strokes.","“Big Brother, look! I drew one too. It’s a second-level talisman!” she exclaimed happily, waving the talisman proudly in her hand. On the other side, the three of them had dedicated the entire morning to practicing the intricate art of drawing talisman symbols. Once they had become sufficiently familiar with the process, they dispatched the conjured puppets to assist with various chores, while they seized the opportunity to explore the vast expanse of Yunxiao Mountain and familiarize themselves with their new surroundings.","At the main peak, upon receiving news that the three young disciples had already mastered the fundamental techniques of drawing puppet symbols, the Azure Emperor raised his eyebrows in surprise. His face lit up as a smile of anticipation and a look of genuine pleasure spread across his handsome face.","“These three are truly gifted,” he murmured to himself.","“Yun Chen, being a few years older and already possessing Golden Core cultivation, surprised me by learning the puppet symbols in just half a day. But I certainly didn’t expect those two little ones to grasp it so quickly.”"]},{"number":4688,"title":"Chapter 4688: Significant Day","paragraphs":["Chapter 4688: Significant Day","The Bifang bird lay languidly on its side, listening to his words without so much as raising its head. It finally spoke, “These three were born into extraordinary families, so it’s only natural they possess exceptional talent. Their parents are Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu; how dim-witted could their children possibly be?”","“This time, Xuanyuan Mo Ze didn’t encounter Feng Jiu, but she is indeed no ordinary individual. It’s merely a matter of time before she ascends to immortality. Those people won’t be able to stop her,” the Azure Emperor said slowly, his eyes narrowed as he gazed at the sky.","That day, Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue explored every corner of Yunxiao Mountain, familiarizing themselves with its various peaks. They also observed the spiritual herbs and fruit trees cultivated in the mountain’s spirit fields, confirming that Yunxiao Mountain was indeed as their master had described. Aside from the three of them, there was only their master and the Bifang divine bird. The rest were, at most, mere puppets.","“Big Brother, Master lives alone in such a vast place, so why doesn’t he take in numerous disciples like others do? Then he would have people to attend to his needs, right?” Yue’er asked in confusion as she walked along, holding both her brothers’ hands. Hao’er squeezed her small hand and said as they strolled, “Our master has a simple nature. He has his reasons for not wanting to establish a sect and accept many disciples. As his disciples, we shouldn’t pry too much. Sometimes, knowing too much isn’t a good thing.”","“Big Brother, tomorrow our master will help us break the blood curse. I’m a little worried.” Muchen said, lowering his head and focusing on the ground with each step he took.","Hearing this, Hao’er looked at him reassuringly. “Don’t worry. Master is incredibly powerful, and Mother entrusted us to him and allowed us to become his disciples. He is someone Mother trusts implicitly, and therefore, we must also trust him. No matter what he does, we must believe in him. Don’t fret! Master will definitely break your blood curse.” Upon hearing these comforting words, Muchen nodded in agreement, his anxiety slightly eased.","Yue’er, who was walking beside them, overheard their conversation and chimed in with a cheerful smile, “After the blood curse is broken, Master will let us go down the mountain! Big Brother, have you thought about what you want to buy?” Before either of the boys could respond, she continued excitedly, “I want to buy seeds! I want the puppets to help me plant spirit rice so that we can eat delicious spirit rice in the future. I also want to buy lots and lots of other things!”","“Then do we need to buy a pot or something that we can cook with? We’ll have to cook for ourselves in the future, so we’ll need those things, right?” Muchen couldn’t help but ask as he looked at Yue’er.","“There seems to be a pot in that small kitchen at the cottage, but we can buy a new one and store it in our space,” Hao’er suggested. The three of them continued to chat as they made their way back towards the thatched cottage. Perhaps it was because they had each other’s company, the three siblings drew strength from their bond, so even though they were separated from their mother, as the days went by, they gradually grew accustomed to their new life. Early the next morning, they woke up before dawn, washed their faces and brushed their teeth, and then proceeded to their master’s cave abode on the main peak to wait for him. Today was the significant day their master would finally remove the blood curse that had plagued them. They felt a mixture of nervousness and eager anticipation.","Hao’er was relatively calm since the blood curse afflicting him had already been lifted. Today’s focus was primarily on Muchen and Muyue. However, much to their surprise, despite arriving early, their master did not awaken until close to noon.","“Come in!” the Azure Emperor’s voice finally echoed from within the depths of the cave abode. The three children standing outside exchanged hesitant glances before stepping inside together. As soon as they crossed the threshold of the cave abode, they couldn’t help but freeze in their tracks, their eyes widening in astonishment at the unexpected sight that greeted them."]},{"number":4689,"title":"Chapter 4689: Breaking the Curse","paragraphs":["Chapter 4689: Breaking the Curse","Looking at the sheer size of the cave abode, though called a cave, it resembled a small, intricate palace. It was comprised of several smaller cave chambers, each thoughtfully separated. Night pearls illuminated the walls, and a constant flow of fresh air circulated throughout. It was evident there were multiple exits hidden within.","“What are you standing there for? Come over here!” the Azure Emperor gestured for the two younger children to approach.","Muchen and Muyue obediently walked forward, stopping before him and looking up expectantly, unsure of how he intended to break the formidable blood curse.","The Azure Emperor’s gaze swept over the two children standing before him. He reached out and gently checked their pulses, his expression serious and focused. After a moment of careful examination, he stood up and walked towards one of the stone chambers, saying to them, “You two, come with me.”","Seeing this, Muchen and Muyue quickly followed their master. Hao’er instinctively wanted to follow them in to observe, but he was immediately halted.","“There are some books in the first stone cave on the left. Go in and take a look! Don’t follow them in; you won’t be able to help,” the Azure Emperor instructed without turning his head.","Hao’er stopped in his tracks, watching with a mixture of concern and curiosity as Muchen and Muyue disappeared into the stone chamber. Although worry gnawed at him, his master’s words resonated – he wouldn’t be of any assistance inside. With a slight hesitation, he turned and walked towards the first stone cave on the left.","He pushed open the heavy stone door, which groaned audibly as it pivoted on its hinges, and stepped inside. The door swung shut behind him, and in that instant, it felt as though all sounds from the outside world were completely silenced. He glanced around the chamber and noticed that a soundproof barrier had been meticulously erected within. Gathering his thoughts, he walked towards the towering bookshelves that lined the walls.","There were ten rows of bookshelves, each densely packed with books of varying sizes and bindings. He approached the nearest shelf, his fingers trailing along the spines, and picked up a book from the section dedicated to martial arts manuals. He opened it and began to flip through the pages. Upon seeing the contents, a flicker of surprise crossed his face.","This was clearly a top-tier martial arts manual, meticulously organized into different fighting styles based on the five fundamental elements. He continued to browse through it, absorbing the intricate diagrams and detailed descriptions, before carefully placing it back on the shelf and moving towards the back of the chamber to select another book.","The next book he picked up was dedicated to the elegant and deadly art of sword techniques. As he opened it, the detailed illustrations of the various sword stances and movements left him utterly speechless, filled with a sense of profound artistry and exquisite precision. For a fleeting moment, he couldn’t help but become completely and utterly absorbed in the captivating content.","He was so deeply engrossed in deciphering the intricacies of the sword techniques that he completely lost all track of time. As his mind became fully immersed, his hands began to move almost involuntarily, subtly mimicking the fluid motions depicted in the illustrations. He remained lost in this silent practice until the heavy stone door creaked open, and his master stood silhouetted in the doorway.","Startled back to reality, he hurriedly placed the sword manual back on the shelf, quickly walked forward, and asked with a slight tremor in his voice, “Master, how are the two of them?” He glanced behind his master, but Muchen and Muyue were nowhere in sight.","“The blood curse has been broken, but they fainted from the pain and are now sleeping in the next room,” the Azure Emperor said, his hands clasped behind his back. His face appeared a little paler than before, as if the arduous task of breaking the blood curse had significantly depleted his spiritual energy. The unmistakable signs of exhaustion were etched between his eyebrows.","“Master, how are you? Are you alright? Do you need to rest for a while? I’ll get you a glass of water,” Hao’er said quickly, also noticing his master’s slightly pallid complexion. He hurried over to the stone table outside the chamber, poured a glass of water, and brought it to him.","The Azure Emperor glanced at him, but did not refuse the offered water. Instead, he reached out, took the cup, drank its contents in a few swallows, and handed the empty cup back to Hao’er, saying, “Don’t worry about the two of them. The blood curse has been broken. Let them sleep; they will be fine tomorrow. Go check on them! But don’t wake them up. I need to rest as well.” With that, he didn’t wait for Hao’er to respond and walked towards another silent stone room."]},{"number":4690,"title":"Chapter 4690: Learn a Skill","paragraphs":["Chapter 4690: Learn a Skill","Seeing this, Hao’er hurried into the stone room to check on his younger siblings. As soon as he entered, he saw Muchen and Muyue lying side by side on the cold stone bed. Their clothes were completely soaked with sweat, clinging to their small bodies. It was clear they had endured intense pain. Both of their lower lips showed faint teeth marks, evidence of their silent struggle, and their hair was stuck to their foreheads and necks with perspiration that had yet to fully dry.","Not wanting to disturb them, he didn’t dare to wake them. Instead, he quietly watched over them for a while, his heart aching. He gently took out a clean handkerchief and carefully wiped the clammy sweat from their faces and limbs. Then, silently channeling his spirit energy, he subtly dried their sweat-soaked clothes before settling down to stay by their side, a silent guardian.","They remained asleep until the first light of the next morning began to filter into the room. Muchen was the first to stir, his eyes fluttering open to see his Big Brother sleeping soundly on the very edge of the stone bed, a picture of quiet devotion. He was about to carefully get out of bed when Yue’er woke up beside him, her movements still groggy with sleep.","“Big Brother, why are you sleeping here?” Yue’er mumbled, rubbing her eyes with a small yawn. She had just woken up, and her little face was still clouded with sleepiness, as if the events of the previous day had already faded from her memory.","“Are you awake?” Hao’er also stirred at that moment, his eyes opening to meet theirs. He sat up quickly and asked with genuine concern, “How do you feel? Are you feeling any better now?”","“Qilin,” Muchen suddenly called out, his voice still a little weak. A flash of bright light momentarily filled the room, and the majestic Qilin beast materialized before them, its gentle eyes fixed on its young master.","“Huh? My brother’s Qilin is here! Does that mean I can summon my little spirit fox too?” Yue’er exclaimed happily, her drowsiness instantly forgotten. She eagerly called out, “Little spirit fox, come out quickly!”","As soon as the words left her lips, the magnificent Nine Tails Spirit Fox appeared with a soft whoosh, gracefully landing on the bed. It looked around the room with intelligent eyes, stretched languidly, and then spoke in a melodious voice, “Master, the oppressive blood curse that bound you has finally been broken. That vile thing was suppressing us, preventing us from reaching you.”","“Great! The blood curse is really broken!” Yue’er clapped her small hands together with joy. She hopped out of bed and declared, “Is Master going to take us down the mountain to go shopping today? Let’s go find him!”","“After Master broke the blood curse for you yesterday, I couldn’t help but notice that he looked a little pale. I wonder if he’s feeling any better today,” Hao’er said, his brow furrowed with concern. However, his worry didn’t stop him from following the energetic Yue’er out of the stone room.","Unexpectedly, as soon as they stepped out of the stone chamber, they saw their master sitting calmly at the stone table outside, looking completely refreshed as he leisurely sipped tea and read a book.","“Master!” Yue’er called out brightly, quickly running forward to greet him with unbridled enthusiasm.","“Master,” Hao’er and Muchen said in unison, their demeanor a little more reserved. They bowed respectfully, offered their greetings, and then stood quietly to one side, observing their master.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the ethereal Nine Tails Spirit Fox and the noble Qilin beast, then addressed the two younger children, “Take back your contract beasts. In the future, unless it is absolutely necessary, do not let them appear in front of other people.”","Understanding the importance of his words, the two children quickly willed their beloved contract beasts back into their personal spaces.","“Master, are we going down the mountain now? Can we go and get something to eat?” Yue’er asked with an eager smile.","The Azure Emperor looked at the three of them, a faint smile on his lips. He then waved his hand gently over them. They felt a soft breeze wash over them, and it was as if a subtle weight had been lifted from their bodies. They suddenly felt incredibly refreshed and light.","“Hey? This isn’t the dust-removing technique! Master, what kind of technique is this?” Yue’er asked curiously, her eyes wide with innocent wonder.","“It is similar to the dust-removing technique in its effect, but the key difference lies in its deeper cleansing action. While the dust-removing technique merely removes surface dust and dirt from your clothes, this cleansing technique makes you feel as though you have just taken a thorough bath and changed into fresh garments, saving you the trouble of actually bathing and changing,” the Azure Emperor explained patiently.","“Master, I want to learn this too!” Yue’er exclaimed with an enthusiastic smile, her desire to learn evident."]},{"number":4691,"title":"Chapter 4691: Going Down the Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 4691: Going Down the Mountain","The Azure Emperor cast a sidelong glance at her and said, “Your magic is useful, but it doesn’t negate the need for bathing. This magic is best used occasionally when you are traveling and lack bathing facilities. When you have the opportunity, it’s always better to properly bathe and change your clothes.”","With that, he stood up and announced, “There are two hot spring spirit ponds on Yunxiao Mountain. In the future, you can use the smaller spirit pond for bathing. The spring water possesses properties that strengthen your muscles and bones, allowing you to cultivate more efficiently.”","“We know that spirit pond! We’ve been there before. There are two, a large one and a small one, but it seems like there’s a formation barrier protecting them,” Yue’er chimed in.","“Alright then, go back and wash up first, and then wait for me at the mountain gate,” he instructed, gesturing for them to return and freshen up.","“Yes, Master,” the three replied in unison and left to prepare.","They had anticipated a long journey from Yunxiao Mountain to the nearest town, so they were quite surprised when they arrived at the bustling city gate by noon.","However, the three children exchanged curious glances at their master. They couldn’t quite articulate it, but they sensed that his appearance had subtly shifted since they had departed the mountain. Moreover, even though he walked right beside them, they found it strangely easy to momentarily forget he was even there.","What was even more peculiar was that after briefly looking at their master’s face, they would almost instantly forget his features, unable to recall them no matter how hard they tried. Not only that, but the same strange phenomenon applied to each of them. They looked at each other and struggled to clearly remember their own faces, as if a thin, shimmering veil obscured their features, making them difficult to perceive distinctly.","“Did you use some kind of magic, Master?” Hao’er couldn’t help but inquire, his curiosity piqued by this unusual effect.","The Azure Emperor continued to walk with his hands clasped behind his back, his expression serene. “That’s right. People with ordinary cultivation levels would not be able to retain a clear memory of your faces even if they saw you, which will ultimately be safer for all of you.”","He paused briefly, glanced at them with a knowing look, and added, “Sometimes, blending into the ordinary is the greatest blessing.”","Hearing this explanation, the three children didn’t press the matter further. Knowing that this subtle alteration was their master’s doing, they felt a sense of reassurance and accepted it without question.","“I am going to sit in the teahouse up ahead,” he announced, gesturing towards a quaint teahouse not far in front of them. “If you wish to eat or purchase anything, feel free to do so. When you are finished, come and find me there.” From the very beginning, he had no intention of following the three kids as they explored the town.","“Yes, Master,” the three replied obediently and were about to set off on their own when they heard their master’s voice call out again.","“Wait.”","“Master, is there something else? Do you want us to buy something for you to eat? Don’t worry, I’ll buy it for you,” Yue’er offered with a bright smile, ever eager to please.","Hearing her thoughtful offer, the Azure Emperor’s lips curved into a gentle smile. He reached behind him, retrieved a seemingly bottomless cosmos sack, placed it in Hao’er’s hand, and said, “Take this. Buy whatever you desire. Don’t worry about spending too much.”","After a brief pause, he addressed Hao’er specifically, “Yun Chen, you are their older brother. Keep a close eye on them.”","“Yes, disciple understands. Thank you, Master,” Hao’er replied gratefully, bowing respectfully before setting off with Yue’er and Muchen.","“Big Brother, let’s go eat first! I really want to try those green onion pancakes, and some fluffy meat buns, and that sweet sugar water...” Yue’er exclaimed as they walked, her voice bubbling with excitement and anticipation.","“Alright, alright, you little glutton, let’s go eat first,” Hao’er chuckled, smiling warmly as he took both of their hands, leading them towards a small, inviting food stall.","The Azure Emperor watched them for a moment, a fond expression on his face, before slowly strolling towards the teahouse, intending to wait there patiently until they had fully indulged in their exploration and shopping before they all returned to the tranquil embrace of the mountain."]},{"number":4692,"title":"Chapter 4692: An Accident","paragraphs":["Inside the bustling general store, Yue'er, her eyes wide with excitement as she touched the smooth grains of spirit rice, called out to the shopkeeper, her voice ringing with youthful enthusiasm, \"I want one hundred jin of spirit rice!\"","Having satisfied their hunger, the trio had enthusiastically embarked on their shopping spree. Their space was already beginning to fill with various interesting finds. After exploring several establishments, they finally located spirit rice in this particular store. Without hesitation, their first request was for a substantial quantity: one hundred jin.","The shopkeeper, a portly man with a neatly trimmed beard, was initially taken aback by the seemingly outlandish request. He chuckled loudly, a booming sound that echoed through the store. \"One hundred jin of spirit rice? Who are you children? Do you even know what spirit rice is used for? Or how much it costs per jin? Asking for one hundred jin! Honestly! Alright, alright, go and play somewhere else! This is not a playground for children like you. Everything in this shop is very expensive!\"","The shopkeeper shook his head dismissively, not bothering to engage in a lengthy argument with what he perceived as naive children, and simply waved them away, indicating they should leave.","\"How much is a jin of spirit rice?\" Hao'er inquired politely, his voice calm and measured.","As soon as he spoke, the shopkeeper seemed to truly notice the composed, slightly older child among the group. He gave Hao'er a more appraising look and offered a somewhat condescending smile. \"Spirit rice isn't measured in mere coins, young man, but in valuable crystal stones. One jin of spirit rice costs thirty crystal stones. It can significantly aid in one's cultivation, but it's not something everyone can afford. Generally, a single person consumes just a handful per meal. Look, like this.\"","The shopkeeper chuckled again, scooped up a small handful of the precious white grains, spread them out in the palm of his hand, and explained with a knowing wink, \"This small amount is enough to cook a bowl of spirit rice, and you won't need to eat anything else with it. You'll feel full of energy and won't experience hunger for the entire day.\"","The three children naturally understood exactly what he was talking about, as their own mother had often fed them this very spirit rice.","\"Is there a discount if we buy 100 jin?\" Hao'er pressed, his tone still polite but now carrying a hint of seriousness.","Hearing this, the shopkeeper's eyebrows shot up in surprise, and he looked at Hao'er with renewed interest. \"You really want one hundred jin?\" He studied the three children more closely, and a flicker of confusion crossed his face. Their features seemed... indistinct. It was as if he could see them, yet what he perceived were remarkably ordinary, almost forgettable features.","However, having been a shopkeeper in this city for many years, he had learned to be observant. He knew that some disciples of powerful masters possessed techniques to subtly conceal their true identities. This thought prompted him to take another, more careful look at the three children, and he began to ponder the possibilities.","\"Well,\" he said, stroking his beard thoughtfully, \"I don't have a full hundred jin of spirit rice in my shop at the moment. I only have about seventy to eighty jin left. The next shipment won't arrive for a few days. However, if you are willing to take all that I have, I can certainly offer you a discount.\"","\"Do you have any seeds here?\" Yue'er interjected, her earlier excitement about the rice momentarily overshadowed by a new interest.","\"Seeds? We have seeds of all kinds!\" the shopkeeper exclaimed, his usual jovial demeanor returning. \"I pride myself on having the most complete selection in the entire city. Whether you're looking for fruit tree seeds, spirit rice seeds, spirit flower seeds, medicinal herb seeds, or even seeds for spirit wine ingredients, I have it all. However,\" he added with a slight shake of his head, \"I don't deal in common gold coins here, only valuable crystal stones.\"","\"We have crystal stones, don't worry,\" Yue'er assured him confidently. \"I want some spirit rice seeds and some medicinal herb seeds. Take a look at this list and see if you have them. If you do, please prepare them for us.\" Yue'er then carefully produced the list she had diligently written earlier and handed it to the shopkeeper.","The shopkeeper took the crumpled piece of paper and glanced at it. He couldn't help but smile faintly at the somewhat crooked and childish handwriting. He carefully read through the list, nodding as he went. \"Yes, we have everything on here, except for those pots and pans, but those are easy enough to find in another shop. Follow me! I'll show you our selection of seeds, and if you like them, I'll have one of my assistants gather them for you, and then you can settle the payment.\"","\"Alright,\" the three agreed readily and followed the shopkeeper deeper into the store.","\"Ahh!\" Yue'er suddenly cried out in surprise and pain as she stumbled, knocking over a tall, slender jar of fragrant spirit wine that had been precariously perched on a shelf beside her. The rich, intoxicating aroma of the spilled wine immediately filled the air."]},{"number":4693,"title":"Chapter 4693: Counter","paragraphs":["Chapter 4693: Counter","“Sister!”","Hao’er and Muchen were instantly alarmed. They rushed to Yue’er’s side, their expressions full of concern as they helped her to her feet. They saw the sticky wine coating her clothes and the trickle of blood staining the back of her hand where a shard of the broken jar had cut her. Their eyes narrowed with unspoken anger.","Yue’er, who was still stunned from the unexpected collision, was covered in the fragrant spirit wine. The cuts on her hand stung, and her elbows throbbed from the impact. A small cry escaped her lips, and her face crumpled as she stood between her brothers, leaning on them for support.","Before any of the three siblings could utter a word, the man who had carelessly knocked Yue’er over began to berate her, his voice sharp and accusatory. “Where did this little girl come from? Don’t you have eyes?”","The speaker was a man in his thirties, clad in a fine green robe, still clutching a substantial ten-jin jar of spirit wine in his hands. Because his back had been turned and Yue’er was small, he hadn’t seen her behind him and had blundered into her, knocking her down with considerable force. Yet, instead of offering an apology, he immediately shifted the blame.","“Oh my, how could you break my precious spirit wine? This is an excellent vintage! This... this... this...” The shopkeeper, having heard the commotion, turned around to assess the situation. His eyes widened as he took in the scene: the expensive spirit wine splattered across the floor, the shattered remnants of the jar, the three bewildered children, and finally, the indignant man in green.","“You broke the wine, so you have to pay for it,” the shopkeeper stated, his tone surprisingly even. He looked at the three children and then at the man. “Each of you pays half. That seems fair.”","“Hehe, shopkeeper, this little girl stumbled and broke it; it has absolutely nothing to do with me. You expect me to pay for it? Preposterous!” The man in green retorted with a disingenuous smile. He then took a step, intending to brush past the three children and pay at the counter. Unexpectedly, just as he was passing them, Hao’er subtly glanced at him and swiftly extended his foot.","“Ah!” The man in green yelped in surprise. With the heavy wine jar in his arms, he tripped over Hao’er’s seemingly innocuous foot and began to lose his balance, flailing precariously. He desperately tried to regain his footing and turn around, but just at that moment, another customer bumped into him from behind, sending him sprawling to the ground. The wine jar he was holding crashed onto the floor with a resounding shatter, and the remaining spirit wine splashed everywhere. Sharp shards of broken pottery scattered across the floor, and the unfortunate man, unable to react in time, landed face-first directly onto the jagged pieces. For a brief, agonizing moment, only his piercing screams filled the air.","“Hiss! Ahhh!” He groaned, lying on the ground, unable to move for a long moment, his breath in ragged gasps.","Witnessing this dramatic turn of events, the shopkeeper’s eyelids twitched almost imperceptibly. He glanced at the three seemingly innocent children, his expression carefully neutral, and suppressed the shock that rippled through him. He took a cautious step back, deciding to observe the situation before intervening.","Hao’er and Muchen, however, paid the flailing man on the ground no further attention. Their focus was entirely on their injured sister.","“Little Sister, let me help you dry your clothes,” Hao’er said gently, placing one hand on her wine-soaked garments and subtly activating his spirit energy. With a soft shimmer, the fragrant spirit wine on Yue’er’s clothes evaporated completely, leaving them dry, though a faint alcoholic scent still lingered.","Muchen carefully took out a clean handkerchief and tenderly wiped the blood from the back of her hand. He then produced a small vial of medicinal balm, applied it to the cut, and wrapped her small hand securely with the clean cloth. “It’s okay, little sister. You’ll be fine soon,” he reassured her softly.","“Mm hmm, thank you, Big Brother and Brother,” she replied, looking up at them with a grateful smile that warmed their hearts.","“Damn brat!” the man on the ground finally managed to sputter, pushing himself up with difficulty. Having fallen hard onto the sharp shards of the wine jar, several dark patches of blood were now visibly seeping through his green robe."]},{"number":4694,"title":"Chapter 4694: Oppress","paragraphs":["Chapter 4694: Oppress","As the man in green struggled to his feet, his face contorted with rage, he snatched a jagged shard of broken glass from the ground and hurled it viciously at the three children. His movements were surprisingly swift, far faster than an ordinary person could react.","The shopkeeper, witnessing the man’s violent action, gasped and involuntarily took a step forward, intending to intervene. However, before he could move further, he saw the older boy swiftly pull his younger brother and sister out of the general store, narrowly avoiding the dangerous projectile.","“Damn kids! You’re asking for death!” The man in green roared, his anger escalating. He lunged after them, swinging a heavy fist directly at Hao’er.","“Stand aside!” Hao’er commanded, pushing Muchen and Yue’er behind him for safety. He stepped forward to confront the enraged man. As he focused his inner energy, the powerful aura of his peak Golden Core cultivation erupted around him, a tangible wave of spiritual pressure.","“Hiss! Such a small child is actually a peak Golden Core Cultivator? It seems this child must be from a noble family or a major sect, right?” A surprised voice murmured from the growing crowd of onlookers.","“Isn’t that man wearing the green robe of an inner disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect? He certainly looks like one. Why is he picking a fight with a child?” Another voice questioned, filled with disapproval.","“This child is also incredibly bold, daring to confront an inner disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect. He’s definitely not ordinary!” A third voice chimed in with intrigue.","“In my opinion,” an old man with a long white beard mused, stroking it thoughtfully, “this young boy might be a direct disciple of a major power. Look at him, already at the peak of the Golden Core stage at such a tender age. And there’s clearly a concealment spell on him, making his features difficult to discern. An inner disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect fighting him, haha, who knows who will prevail!” The old man’s eyes gleamed with intense interest as he watched the unfolding confrontation. The more he observed the young boy’s remarkably steady stance, his peculiar yet skillful footwork and movements, the more convinced he became that the child’s background was anything but ordinary.","His gaze then shifted to the two younger children standing nearby. They, too, were clearly under the effects of a similar concealment spell, and surprisingly, even with his considerable spiritual strength, he was unable to penetrate the illusion.","The old man refocused his attention on the two combatants. Seeing that the man in green was unable to gain any advantage with his bare hands against the surprisingly adept child, he finally drew his sword. The instant the cold steel flashed in the sunlight, a corresponding glint of light appeared in the little boy’s hand, and a sharp, elegant sword materialized as if from thin air.","“What a fine sword!” the old man exclaimed softly, his eyes shining with appreciation as he beheld the weapon in the boy’s grasp. The sword radiated a palpable aura of cold power, and its sword qi was fierce and intimidating. It was clear at a glance that it was no ordinary weapon, but a rare treasure.","Especially as the boy gripped the hilt, his entire aura seemed to transform, becoming incredibly sharp and dangerous. With a swift twist of his wrist, a dazzling sword flower bloomed outward, and his small figure darted forward with astonishing speed, a blur too fast for the eye to easily follow, directly charging towards the stunned man in green.","The man in green, perhaps arrogant in his status as an inner disciple and underestimating the skill of a mere child, clearly hadn’t anticipated that the boy’s swordsmanship would be far superior to his own. He had likely assumed that, as someone with the same peak Golden Core cultivation, he would easily suppress this “little brat,” even if he had to draw his own weapon. He was sorely mistaken.","Panic flickered in his eyes as he instinctively retreated, raising his own sword to block the incoming attack. The moment the two swords collided, a violent surge of sword qi erupted, rushing directly towards his face.","“Arghhh!” he cried out in pain as the tip of the boy’s sword grazed his wrist, causing him to flinch violently. His own sword clattered to the ground, and he was forced to stumble backward, landing heavily on his buttocks as the sharp point of the boy’s sword pressed menacingly against his forehead.","“No, don’t kill me! I’m a disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect! If you kill me, you’ll become an enemy of the entire Heaven’s Sun Sect!” He shrieked in terror, desperately invoking the name of his powerful sect in a pathetic attempt to intimidate his young assailant.","Hao’er looked down at him coldly, the tip of his sword unwavering against the man’s throat, and asked, his voice devoid of emotion, “You want to live?”"]},{"number":4695,"title":"Chapter 4695: Looking for People","paragraphs":["Chapter 4695: Looking for People","Cold sweat trickled down the forehead of the man in green. He held his breath, terrified that the sharp point pressed against his throat would pierce his skin. He swallowed hard, his voice tight with fear, and stammered, “W-what do you want?”","“Pay the shopkeeper for what you broke, then get out of my sight,” Hao’er stated icily, his gaze unwavering.","“Fine!” the man gritted out through clenched teeth. He fumbled for his cosmos sack, pulled it out, and tossed it roughly towards the shopkeeper. “This should be more than enough!”","The shopkeeper deftly caught the sack, quickly opened it, extracted the crystal stones equivalent to the cost of the spilled spirit wine, and handed the remaining stones back to the trembling man. “Haha, yes, it’s more than enough. There’s even some extra.”","Seeing the payment settled, Hao’er finally retracted his sword, sheathing it behind his back with a fluid motion. “Get lost!” he commanded, his voice carrying an undeniable authority.","The man in green scrambled to his feet, clutching his injured wrist. He shot Hao’er a venomous glare, his eyes burning with resentment, then gritted his teeth and quickly limped away, disappearing into the crowd.","“Good!”","“Well done!”","“That was impressive!”","“Are all kids so skilled these days?”","A ripple of excited chatter spread through the onlookers. Some stared intently at Hao’er, their faces filled with awe and curiosity. “Young Master, who is your esteemed master? You are so young, yet your sword skills are so extraordinary! Your master must be a truly formidable individual!” one man called out loudly.","“Yes, Young Master, please tell us, who is your master? Does your master still accept disciples?” another person eagerly inquired. They couldn’t help but imagine the possibilities if their own children could learn even a fraction of the skill this young boy possessed. Their futures would be secure.","However, Hao’er remained impassive, ignoring the barrage of questions. He turned and walked towards his younger brother and sister, bringing them to the shopkeeper’s counter. “Shopkeeper, please prepare everything on our list.”","“Yes, yes, of course, Young Master,” the shopkeeper replied with a wide, ingratiating smile. He cast a deep, thoughtful look at Hao’er, a shrewd glint in his eyes, and chuckled softly. “Young Master, I will give you a generous discount. If you ever need to purchase anything in the future, please come to me, and I will always offer you the best possible price.” He recognized at once that this was no ordinary child, and he instinctively sensed a remarkable future ahead of him. Cultivating a good relationship now could only bring future benefits.","He personally escorted them through the store, carefully gathered everything on their list, double-checked each item with them, and then efficiently settled their bill.","As he saw them to the door, the shopkeeper lowered his voice and said with a hint of urgency, “Young Master, you would be wise to return to your master or your clan as quickly as possible. That disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect will not take this humiliation lightly. He will undoubtedly seek you out. You have purchased what you needed, so please, hurry back and avoid any further trouble.”","“Alright, we understand. Thank you very much for your kindness,” Hao’er replied politely, offering a small bow of gratitude before leaving the store with Muchen and Muyue.","They didn’t head straight back to the teahouse, as they still had a few more items to buy. So, they turned onto another bustling street, continuing their shopping. Not long after they had departed, the enraged man in green from the Heaven’s Sun Sect arrived at the general store, accompanied by several other imposing-looking men.","“Where are they?” The man in green, who was leading the group, demanded, his eyes scanning the surroundings with a sinister glint.","“Senior Brother, those three little brats were just here. Let me go inside and question the shopkeeper,” the man in green offered, hurrying into the store. His injured wrist was now bandaged, but his hand hung limply at his side, a testament to the severity of the damage. The boy’s sword strike had severed tendons and nerves. Only the skilled physicians within their sect had managed to salvage his hand. The memory of the pain and humiliation fueled his burning hatred.","“Shopkeeper, where did those three little brats go?” He snarled as he entered the store, his malevolent gaze sweeping across the interior."]},{"number":4696,"title":"Chapter 4696: Know Everything","paragraphs":["Chapter 4696: Know Everything","“Haha, it’s you, Young Master!” the shopkeeper greeted with a wide smile, bowing his hands respectfully. His eyes flickered to the bandaged wrist before he chuckled lightly. “Those three children made their purchases and then left. They are no longer in the shop.”","“They left? Which way did they go?” The man in green demanded angrily, his voice laced with frustration.","“I’m afraid I don’t know,” the shopkeeper replied, shaking his head innocently.","“You just took my crystal stones! Give them back to me!” The man in green snarled, stepping forward and grabbing the shopkeeper’s collar. The thought of the valuable crystal stones now in the shopkeeper’s possession sent a pang of fury through him.","“Hehe, Young Master, you must be joking. Those crystal stones are compensation for the fine spirit wine that you unfortunately broke in our humble establishment. How could we possibly return them?” The shopkeeper said with a placid smile, gently but firmly removing the man’s hand from his collar and smoothly straightening the wrinkled fabric.","Seeing how effortlessly the shopkeeper had deflected his grasp, the green-clad man paused, a flicker of unease momentarily distracting him.","“Alright, since it’s compensation, let’s not dwell on retrieving it,” the man in blue interjected, casting a sharp glance at his companion before turning his attention back to the shopkeeper. “Shopkeeper, do you happen to know which direction they headed?”","“Indeed,” the shopkeeper replied with a nod and a friendly smile. He walked to the entrance of his shop and pointed in the opposite direction from where the children had actually gone. “I saw them go that way.”","“Thank you,” the man in blue said with a curt nod, glancing at his entourage before instructing, “Let’s go.”","The man in green followed reluctantly, still seething with resentment. After walking a short distance, he couldn’t contain his frustration any longer. “Senior Brother, why didn’t you insist on getting the crystals back? Clearly...” He trailed off, interrupted by a cold laugh.","“Ask for them back? Ha!” the man in blue scoffed, casting a disdainful look at his companion. “Every established shop in this city has a powerful backer. The shopkeeper of that general store exuded a restrained but strong aura. One could tell at a glance that he is a master, possibly even stronger than both of us combined. You seriously thought we could just demand the crystals back from someone like that? You truly are naive.”","“Are we just going to let this go?” The man in green asked, still unwilling to concede.","“Find those three little brats, and what can’t we take back?” the man in blue sneered, his eyes glinting with malice. “What’s more, how could a mere ten-year-old reach the peak of the Golden Core stage? I am rather curious to meet him myself and see what he is truly capable of!”","Unaware that the shopkeeper had deliberately pointed them in the wrong direction, the group from the Heaven’s Sun Sect pressed on, their search taking them further and further away from their intended targets.","Meanwhile, having completed their initial shopping, the three children strolled past a charming pastry shop. Yue’er, her eyes wide and sparkling with longing, licked her lips like a contented little cat. She turned to her two brothers and pleaded, “Big Brother, Brother, can we please go in and buy some pastries?”","Hao’er and Muchen exchanged indulgent smiles at their little sister’s obvious craving. “Alright, little glutton,” Hao’er chuckled. “Let’s go in and buy some to take back with us!”","“Yay! Alright, then I’ll pick out a few extra to save for later!” Yue’er exclaimed happily, taking their hands and skipping towards the inviting shop.","Back at the teahouse, while patiently sipping his tea and waiting for the three children to return, the Azure Emperor held a small, intricately carved trigram mirror in his hand, subtly observing their activities through its reflective surface. When he saw the three of them holding hands and cheerfully entering the pastry shop, the corners of his lips curved upwards in a faint, affectionate smile.","However, the next moment, his eyes narrowed slightly. He closed them briefly, subtly extended his powerful spiritual sense, and with a barely perceptible flick of his wrist, sent a single drop of tea water hurtling through the air in a specific direction..."]},{"number":4697,"title":"Chapter 4697: Death","paragraphs":["At that very moment, the man in green trailed behind the blue-robed leader of their group. \"Senior Brother,\" he remarked, a hint of doubt in his voice, \"could it be that the shopkeeper wasn’t entirely truthful with us? We’ve searched all this way, and there’s been no sign of those three children.\"","\"Then we keep looking,\" the blue robed man replied, his voice slightly deeper, a cold determination hardening his gaze. \"They’re just a few children. As long as they remain within this city, we will undoubtedly find them! Anyone who dares to lay a hand on a member of the Heaven’s Sun Sect is making an enemy of our entire sect. We cannot allow such insolence to go unpunished!\"","\"Senior Brother is absolutely right,\" the man in green agreed vehemently. \"Those three little brats are unbelievably arrogant. Once we find them, we’ll definitely make them pay dearly—\" His sentence was abruptly cut short by a sharp scream, and he suddenly collapsed to the ground.","\"Junior Brother!\"","The blue robed man whirled around, startled. His face paled visibly, a flicker of fear momentarily eclipsing his anger as he saw his companion lying motionless on the ground. Instinctively, his eyes darted around, searching for any sign of an attacker.","The disciples following closely behind quickly surrounded their fallen comrade, drawing their swords and scanning their surroundings warily, desperate to identify the unseen assailant. However, as they looked around, they noticed that everyone else on the street – even those browsing in the shops and taverns lining either side – were turning their heads to stare at them, their faces etched with surprise and confusion.","Clearly, no one had anticipated that amidst their casual stroll and conversation, one of their group would suddenly be struck down, and the killer hadn’t even revealed themselves.","\"Senior Brother, how is he?\" one of the disciples asked, a tremor of panic in his voice.","\"He’s dead,\" the blue-clothed man stated grimly, swallowing hard to suppress the shock and growing unease churning within him. His eyes were fixed on the small, almost imperceptible wound on the man in green’s forehead. There wasn’t even any blood, yet his companion was lifeless.","Hearing the grim confirmation, the other disciples were stunned into silence. They crowded around the body, noticing the tiny wound on his forehead, utterly bewildered as to what kind of weapon could have caused such a swift and silent death.","\"Carry him back. Let’s go!\" The blue robed man finally commanded, his voice tight as he ordered them to return the body to their sect. They had all come out together for a seemingly simple outing, and now that one of them was dead, they dreaded the inevitable explanations upon their return. The sudden and inexplicable death had shaken him deeply. He couldn’t shake the feeling that it was somehow connected to the three children. Why else would everyone else be unharmed, while only the man in green had been targeted?","Could it be that the children had powerful protectors watching over them? Had these protectors sensed their malicious intent towards the children and eliminated their junior brother as a warning?","The group didn’t dare to linger any longer. They quickly lifted the body and hurried away, their minds racing with the need to report this unsettling incident to their sect elders immediately.","Meanwhile, completely oblivious to the silent retribution that had just unfolded, the three children continued their leisurely exploration of the city, diligently storing their newly acquired treasures into their expansive spatial storage. Perhaps the sheer volume of their purchases, all disappearing into seemingly thin air, had not gone unnoticed, drawing the attention of less scrupulous individuals.","\"These little brats must be carrying a fortune on them. We’ve been tailing them for quite a while now, and there are no adults accompanying them, just the three of them. I say we don’t wait for Big Brother to arrive. Let’s just lure them into the alley up ahead and strike!\" one of the loose cultivators hissed, his eyes gleaming with avarice as he watched the three unsuspecting children strolling ahead.","\"Let’s just wait for Big Brother! We don’t want to get into any unnecessary trouble,\" another loose cultivator cautioned, glancing back down the street and then grinning. \"Look, isn’t that Big Brother coming now?\"","The small group of opportunistic cultivators turned around and saw a man wearing an ostentatious brocaded robe, a toothpick casually dangling from his lips, swaggering towards them."]},{"number":4698,"title":"Chapter 4698: Enquire","paragraphs":["Chapter 4698: Enquire","“Big Brother!” Several of the loose cultivators eagerly crowded around the man as they tried to gain his favor.","“Big Brother, we’ve located some prime targets. We were just waiting for you to arrive and lead the harvest,” one of them chimed in, gesturing ahead. “Big Brother, look! Those three kids up ahead have been buying a mountain of things, and they seem to have an endless supply of crystal stones. We reckon they must be carrying even more valuable treasures, and there aren’t any adults with them, just the three of them. If we snatch them, we’ll definitely make a killing!”","The brocade-clad cultivator, the toothpick still perched jauntily in the corner of his mouth, had been lost in his own thoughts. But when he heard his men’s excited report, he glanced up and froze, a flicker of alarm crossing his face as he spotted the three children.","“Big Brother, let’s lure them into the alley up ahead and silence them permanently! These fat sheep won’t escape our grasp,” the man beside him continued, oblivious to the subtle shift in his leader’s expression. His eyes remained fixed on the three children, gleaming with avarice. “If it weren’t so troublesome to offload three brats, I’d be tempted to just throw sacks over their heads and sell them off.”","“Sell them to hell!” the brocade-clad man cursed under his breath, his hand shooting out to deliver a sharp slap to the other man’s head. “If you have a death wish, by all means, go ahead, but don’t you dare drag me down with you!”","“Big Brother, what’s wrong? Can’t we touch them? They’re just three kids...” the slapped man mumbled, not daring to retaliate. He simply lowered his head slightly and took a step back, confusion clouding his features.","“When I went to grab a bite earlier, I saw that the oldest of those three kids in front of us was at the peak of the Golden Core stage, and he even took down an inner disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect. You really think you can take him on? Are you deliberately seeking your own demise? Also,” the robed cultivator continued, his gaze thoughtful as he watched the three children slowly walk away, “when I was heading over here just now, I overheard some people on the street talking about an inner disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect who died suddenly on West Street.”","He paused, his eyes narrowed in contemplation. “Those three children must be disciples of a major sect or a powerful family, and they clearly have someone protecting them in the shadows. You want to go and provoke them? That’s practically begging for a swift and painful death!”","Hearing this chilling assessment, the loose cultivators broke out in a cold sweat. Their palms turned clammy as they nervously patted their chests. “That was a close call! If Big Brother hadn’t come along, we would have been dead meat!”","Hao’er, leading Muchen and Yue’er, continued to walk forward. After a short while, he glanced back and noticed the group of loose cultivators standing there, watching them intently, but they made no move to follow. Seeing this, he paid them no further mind and continued to guide his younger siblings as they finished their errands.","Around noon, the three of them finally arrived at the teahouse and found their master seated at a window table on the second floor, looking relaxed as he enjoyed the afternoon.","“Master, we’re back~” Yue’er chirped happily, her eyes crinkling into a bright smile as she ran over to him. “I bought something to eat for you, Master! Try it, these mung bean cakes are absolutely delicious!” She reached into her spatial storage, retrieved a delicate pastry, unwrapped it, and placed it enticingly in front of him.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the three of them, his gaze lingering for a moment on the small bandage adorning the back of Yue’er’s hand. “Did you manage to purchase everything you needed?” he inquired, picking up the pastry and taking a small bite.","“Yes, Master, we bought everything,” Hao’er and Muchen replied simultaneously.","“Why does Little Qi smell faintly of wine? Did something happen while you were out?” he asked slowly, his expression subtly concerned.","“I didn’t take good enough care of her, Master. She was accidentally knocked down by someone and had spirit wine spilled all over her, and her hand got cut by the broken jar,” Hao’er hung his head low as he said with self blame."]},{"number":4699,"title":"Chapter 4699: Anger","paragraphs":["Chapter 4699: Anger","“Master, it’s not Big Brother’s fault. He was protecting us,” Yue’er quickly interjected, her voice filled with concern, afraid that the Azure Emperor might scold Hao’er.","The Azure Emperor glanced at her and said sternly, “Didn’t I instruct you? Do not reveal your relationship to anyone outside. From this moment forward, do not call him ‘brother.’ Address him as ‘Senior Brother’ and Muchen as ‘Second Senior Brother.'”","“Oh,” Yue’er replied obediently, stealing a quick, apologetic glance at her two older siblings.","“Have you both remembered?” The Azure Emperor asked, his gaze now fixed on Hao’er and Muchen.","The two boys exchanged a brief look before replying in unison, “Yes, Master, disciple remembers.”","“As Senior Brothers,” the Azure Emperor continued, his voice calm yet carrying an undercurrent of formidable power, “if you ever encounter anyone bullying your Junior Sister in the future, regardless of who they are, teach them a lesson first. If they attempt to kill you, eliminate them before they can carry out their intent! Do you understand?” His seemingly gentle tone held a cold and intimidating aura that sent a shiver down both Hao’er and Muchen’s spines.","“Yes, we understand, Master,” they replied solemnly.","“Since we have completed our errands, let us depart,” the Azure Emperor announced, rising from his seat. He left a single gold coin on the table, smoothly brushed off his robes, and walked out of the teahouse, his hands clasped behind his back.","Seeing this, Yue’er hastily retrieved the half-eaten pastry from the table and placed it back into her space. She then quickly followed her two brothers as they hurried after their master, their steps directed towards the familiar path leading back to Yunxiao Mountain.","On the other side of the city, the venerable elders of the Heaven’s Sun Sect stood around the lifeless body of their fallen disciple, their expressions grim and solemn.","“It was a single drop of water that killed him, not some kind of hidden weapon,” one of the venerable ones murmured, stroking his long white beard thoughtfully. “To be able to manipulate water with such precision and lethality from a distance... this person’s cultivation must be unfathomably deep.”","Hearing this, another elder turned to the blue-robed disciple who had returned with the body and asked in a voice that was outwardly calm but laced with barely suppressed fury, “Didn’t you go down the mountain to purchase supplies? How did you manage to make such dangerous enemies and instigate such a grave incident?”","“Master, please forgive our incompetence,” the blue-robed disciple pleaded, kneeling down and bowing his head low. “At that time, only Junior Brother went to acquire the spirit wine, while the rest of us were occupied with other purchases. We never anticipated that he would become embroiled in a conflict with three children and ultimately be killed.” He remained prostrate, awaiting his master’s judgment.","“Proceed to the Disciplinary Department and receive thirty lashes!” The venerable elder commanded in a deep, resonant voice, his brow furrowed with displeasure as he looked down at the kneeling disciple. “Get up and go!”","“Yes, Master. Disciple will immediately go and receive his punishment,” the blue-robed man replied hastily, quickly rising and hurrying out of the room.","After he had left, the venerable elders turned their attention back to the corpse lying on the ground. One of them finally broke the heavy silence. “What are your thoughts? Who could have possibly killed him in such a manner?”","“Regardless of their identity,” another elder declared, his face flushed with anger, “anyone who dares to harm an inner disciple of the Heaven’s Sun Sect clearly holds our sect in utter contempt. We cannot simply let this pass, or others will believe that the Heaven’s Sun Sect is weak and that our inner disciples can be killed with impunity! I will dispatch someone to the city immediately to gather more information about those three children. We will uncover who is behind this!”","The elder beside him listened intently, pondered for a moment, and then said hesitantly, “That is true, but I am concerned that this might be the work of some reclusive and powerful figure. If that is the case, even our Heaven’s Sun Sect might be powerless to retaliate. Moreover, if the other party is indeed a hidden power, our Heaven’s Sun Sect disciples would be in the wrong for laying a hand on their disciples. If this powerful figure chooses to eliminate them, who among us would dare to voice any opinion?”","“A powerful figure in seclusion? How many such individuals can there truly be?” the first elder scoffed, though a hint of unease flickered in his eyes. “Very well, I will instruct the disciples below to handle this matter with utmost caution for now.” With that, and without offering any further explanation, he brushed his sleeves and strode out of the room, leaving the other elders to contemplate the unsettling events that had just transpired."]},{"number":4700,"title":"Chapter 4700: Teaching","paragraphs":["The one who died was his disciple, while they preferred to avoid unnecessary entanglements, as the sect’s master, failing to address this incident would severely undermine his authority in the future. Moreover, the disciples within their sect predominantly hailed from influential families. He was obligated to provide a satisfactory explanation to the bereaved family.","Meanwhile, the Azure Emperor returned to the tranquil seclusion of Yunxiao Mountain, paying little mind to the three children who trailed behind him. He retreated directly into the depths of his cave abode, his thoughts unreadable.","The three children, on their part, busied themselves organizing the newly acquired items for their small kitchen, diligently drawing more protective talismans, and crafting additional helpful puppets to ease their daily chores. They remained blissfully unaware that their brief foray into the city had inadvertently led to their master eliminating a disciple from a prominent sect, and that members of that very sect were now actively searching for them.","Unfortunately for the Heaven’s Sun Sect, this was the first time the three children had ventured into the city, and they had subtly employed illusion magic to obscure their appearances. This made any form of investigation exceedingly difficult, leaving the sect with few leads to pursue.","The days on Yunxiao Mountain settled into a peaceful rhythm. The three children continued their studies under the tutelage of the Azure Emperor, who wisely tailored his lessons to each child’s individual aptitudes and strengths. He did not impose a uniform curriculum, nor did he teach them identical sword techniques.","Instead, he carefully selected a distinct sword art for each of them, providing personalized guidance in their cultivation and encouraging them to practice and spar using their unique skills.","While Hao’er and Muchen displayed a natural inclination and enthusiasm for swordplay, Yue’er, perhaps influenced by her mother’s deep knowledge, showed a marked preference for the study of medicine. With characteristic diligence, she even took to planting medicinal herbs herself after the puppets had prepared the soil, immersing herself in ancient texts and eagerly seeking clarification from her master whenever she encountered something she didn’t understand.","Observing that Yue’er’s swordsmanship lagged behind her brothers’ and noting her genuine passion for cultivating medicinal herbs, the Azure Emperor one day sought her out in the burgeoning medicinal herb field. He watched silently as the small figure diligently worked under the warm afternoon sun.","Despite her small stature, she was remarkably efficient in her tasks. He watched her carefully carrying water and tending to the delicate plants before finally calling out, \"Little Qi, come here.\"","Hearing his familiar voice, Yue’er turned around, her face lighting up with a bright smile as she saw her master standing nearby. She immediately put down the watering can and hurried over to him. \"Master, why are you here?\"","\"If I hadn’t come, were you planning to continue watering these precious spirit herbs in such an inefficient manner?\" He shook his head gently, a hint of amusement mixed with helplessness in his eyes. \"You are a cultivator, Little Qi. When performing such tasks, you must learn to utilize your spirit energy. Whether you are watering flowers or trees, a simple watering technique will suffice to properly moisten these spirit herbs.\"","As he spoke, he slowly formed an elegant hand seal. The water in the nearby bucket surged upwards, defying gravity. As the final part of the seal was completed, the water instantly transformed into a gentle, fine rain that cascaded softly over the entire spirit field.","\"See? Just like that,\" he said, turning to the little girl beside him. Her eyes were wide with astonishment, a sight that he couldn’t help but find endearing.","\"Master, why didn’t you teach me this spell earlier? I’ve been watering them by hand for days!\" Her initial surprise quickly gave way to playful reproach. She smiled sweetly and tugged on his sleeve. \"Master, master, teach me again! I haven’t quite grasped it yet!\"","Without a word, the Azure Emperor turned and began to walk away, saying simply, \"Follow me!\" He led her at a leisurely pace to a cascading waterfall nestled at the back of the mountain.","\"Practice here,\" he instructed, handing her a thin, worn book. \"Furthermore, there is a set of specific body movements that you must learn diligently.\" He pointed to the book. \"You must study and practice until you can walk across the surface of this waterfall without your boots even getting damp before you are permitted to learn anything else.\"","\"Mmm, Little Qi understands!\" She replied with a determined smile, eagerly taking the book and beginning to flip through its pages, her curiosity already piqued."]}]);
